{"jobs":[{"id":"1cccde14-c90b-4ddd-8d62-e5dd6a0f7f04","title":"Talent Network","department":"Talent Network","team":"Talent Network","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2023-04-06T16:03:40.398+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1cccde14-c90b-4ddd-8d62-e5dd6a0f7f04","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1cccde14-c90b-4ddd-8d62-e5dd6a0f7f04/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Don't see the position you're looking for? We'd still love to hear from you!</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join the Thyme Care <strong>Talent Network </strong>by sharing your resume below. When a new opportunity arises, we'll use the information from these submissions to identify possible matches. No need to apply to the Talent Network if you have previously applied to other roles at Thyme Care. We may not reply to your application, but know that it will be viewed, categorized, and stored to be on hand for whenever a relevant role might open. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Be cautious</strong> of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em>recruitment fraud</em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nDon't see the position you're looking for? We'd still love to hear from you!\n\nJoin the Thyme Care Talent Network by sharing your resume below. When a new opportunity arises, we'll use the information from these submissions to identify possible matches. No need to apply to the Talent Network if you have previously applied to other roles at Thyme Care. We may not reply to your application, but know that it will be viewed, categorized, and stored to be on hand for whenever a relevant role might open. \n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"75df2e47-03fb-45dd-818a-bf206caab9b8","title":"Palliative Care Nurse Practitioner (Multi-State License Preferred)","department":"Member Experience","team":"NP","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-09-30T13:43:22.513+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/75df2e47-03fb-45dd-818a-bf206caab9b8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/75df2e47-03fb-45dd-818a-bf206caab9b8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Palliative Care Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical member of the clinical team caring for our members with serious illness. You will have three primary responsibilities: </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">First, you will see members for specialty palliative care outpatient appointments via video visits as part of an interdisciplinary team consisting of our Community Health Workers, Oncology Nurses, Social Worker, and Palliative Medicine Physician. As one of the first Nurse Practitioners to join the palliative care team, you will be an important part of bringing our model to scale. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Second, you will be responsible for the oversight and direction of interdisciplinary case conferences for our members with advanced serious illness, in which individualized care plans for our members are created and monitored by our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurses. You will provide clinical oversight to the case management team and direct clinical care, as needed. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Third, you will provide education about palliative care to our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurses. In particular, you will focus your teaching efforts on the outpatient management of cancer-related symptoms, serious illness communication skills, and advance care planning. In addition, you will be integral to the development and implementation of our advance care planning program.  </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports into our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/julia-frydman-1b080b1b/\">Senior Medical Director</a> and can be remote or hybrid based in our New York City or Nashville offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete training and are up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete virtual palliative care outpatient visits for our members with the highest degree of clinical rigor. You will work fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be adept at leading interdisciplinary case conferences for members with advanced serious illness, guiding our team of community health workers and oncology nurse navigators in the creation of evidence-based, member-centered care plans that focus on interventions that improve member outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become the go-to person for our oncology nurse navigators and community health workers when they are working with a member who has advanced serious illness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable with and correctly follow policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our metrics and quality standards.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.<br /><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 3 years of nurse practitioner (NP) experience with at least 2 years in palliative care, preferably caring for patients in the outpatient oncology setting. You are an advanced certified hospice and palliative nurse practitioner (ACHPN). It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. <strong>Licensure. </strong>You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted nurse practitioner license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses.<br /><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.<br /><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.<br /><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. <br /><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort using and learning new technology is important.<br /><strong>Identify priorities and take action. </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are addressed immediately.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE \n\nAs a Thyme Care Palliative Care Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical member of the clinical team caring for our members with serious illness. You will have three primary responsibilities: \n\nFirst, you will see members for specialty palliative care outpatient appointments via video visits as part of an interdisciplinary team consisting of our Community Health Workers, Oncology Nurses, Social Worker, and Palliative Medicine Physician. As one of the first Nurse Practitioners to join the palliative care team, you will be an important part of bringing our model to scale. \n\nSecond, you will be responsible for the oversight and direction of interdisciplinary case conferences for our members with advanced serious illness, in which individualized care plans for our members are created and monitored by our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurses. You will provide clinical oversight to the case management team and direct clinical care, as needed. \n\nThird, you will provide education about palliative care to our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurses. In particular, you will focus your teaching efforts on the outpatient management of cancer-related symptoms, serious illness communication skills, and advance care planning. In addition, you will be integral to the development and implementation of our advance care planning program.  \n\nThis role reports into our Senior Medical Director https://www.linkedin.com/in/julia-frydman-1b080b1b/ and can be remote or hybrid based in our New York City or Nashville offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Complete training and are up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. \n\n - Complete virtual palliative care outpatient visits for our members with the highest degree of clinical rigor. You will work fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits. \n\n - Be adept at leading interdisciplinary case conferences for members with advanced serious illness, guiding our team of community health workers and oncology nurse navigators in the creation of evidence-based, member-centered care plans that focus on interventions that improve member outcomes.\n\n - Become the go-to person for our oncology nurse navigators and community health workers when they are working with a member who has advanced serious illness.\n\n - Be comfortable with and correctly follow policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our metrics and quality standards.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.\nExperience. You have at least 3 years of nurse practitioner (NP) experience with at least 2 years in palliative care, preferably caring for patients in the outpatient oncology setting. You are an advanced certified hospice and palliative nurse practitioner (ACHPN). It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. Licensure. You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted nurse practitioner license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses.\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort using and learning new technology is important.\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are addressed immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8c9b617b-04e1-4793-8179-5dc0ff2a810e","title":"Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-20T14:04:23.069+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/8c9b617b-04e1-4793-8179-5dc0ff2a810e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/8c9b617b-04e1-4793-8179-5dc0ff2a810e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our higher-acuity members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.<strong> </strong>This role can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville office.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications. </strong>An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of high-acuity, adult oncology experience. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important. Experience with working remotely and a willingness to learn new technology are required.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong><em><strong> </strong></em>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is </em>$<em>46.35/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</em> <em>OCN certification is required at the time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE \n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our higher-acuity members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed. This role can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville office.\n\nMost of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. \n\n - Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.\n\n - Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.\n\n - Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.\n\n - Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.\n\n - Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.\n\n - Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.\n\n - Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.\n\n - Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.\n\n - Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.\n\n - Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one. \n\nQualifications. An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.\n\nExperience. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of high-acuity, adult oncology experience. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important. Experience with working remotely and a willingness to learn new technology are required.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life. OCN certification is required at the time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care.\n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"04b192df-be34-4db0-a957-4c6c06db5e5d","title":"Oncology Transitions of Care Nurse","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-20T14:04:19.460+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/04b192df-be34-4db0-a957-4c6c06db5e5d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/04b192df-be34-4db0-a957-4c6c06db5e5d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As an Oncology Nurse - Transitions of Care, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus, supporting the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.<strong> </strong>This role can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville office.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications. </strong>An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of oncology nursing or case management experience and are a Certified Case Manager (CCM).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong><em><strong> </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. <em>Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The shift for this role will be 8:30 am-5:00 pm EST or 11:30 am-8 pm EST. To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE \n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As an Oncology Nurse - Transitions of Care, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus, supporting the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed. This role can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville office.\n\nMost of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. \n\n - Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.\n\n - Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.\n\n - Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.\n\n - Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.\n\n - Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.\n\n - Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.\n\n - Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.\n\n - Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.\n\n - Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.\n\n - Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one.\n\nQualifications. An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.\n\nExperience. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of oncology nursing or case management experience and are a Certified Case Manager (CCM).\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. \n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nThe shift for this role will be 8:30 am-5:00 pm EST or 11:30 am-8 pm EST. To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"95d46901-3e1d-4ebd-9d0f-bb4da128f08b","title":"Oncology Nurse Navigator","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-20T14:04:11.034+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/95d46901-3e1d-4ebd-9d0f-bb4da128f08b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/95d46901-3e1d-4ebd-9d0f-bb4da128f08b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, providing triage, support, and education throughout their cancer journey via phone and email.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will be to actively engage with members, address clinical issues, and efficiently manage any escalations that arise. In contrast to Specialty Oncology Nurse roles, this position focuses on symptom management and longitudinal care coordination, rather than on coordinating admissions, discharges, and post-discharge needs to prevent readmission.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The shifts for this position are either 8:30 AM - 5 PM EST or 11:30 AM - 8 PM EST.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Within your first three months, you will:</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and promptly address member needs, providing assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate with the healthcare team on targeted support plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster strong partnerships with payers and the members' oncology and primary care providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Performs other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Member-Centric Approach: </strong>You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented:</strong> You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills:</strong> You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong> An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. <strong>Compact and single-state licensure in New York and/or Illinois is preferred.</strong> Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications: </strong>Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is <em>$41.54/hour.</em> <em>To perform this role, you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations on accessing PHIs. </em>We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Be cautious of </strong></em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em><strong>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</strong><br /></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE\n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, providing triage, support, and education throughout their cancer journey via phone and email.\n\nUnder the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will be to actively engage with members, address clinical issues, and efficiently manage any escalations that arise. In contrast to Specialty Oncology Nurse roles, this position focuses on symptom management and longitudinal care coordination, rather than on coordinating admissions, discharges, and post-discharge needs to prevent readmission.\n\nThe shifts for this position are either 8:30 AM - 5 PM EST or 11:30 AM - 8 PM EST.\n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.\n\n - Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.\n\n - Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.\n\n - Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.\n\n - Identify and promptly address member needs, providing assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.\n\n - Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate with the healthcare team on targeted support plans.\n\n - Foster strong partnerships with payers and the members' oncology and primary care providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.\n\n - Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required\n\n - Performs other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Member-Centric Approach: You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.\n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - Qualifications: An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. Compact and single-state licensure in New York and/or Illinois is preferred. Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. \n\n - Certifications: Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. \n\nThis job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $41.54/hour. To perform this role, you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations on accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.\n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. \n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"13e52b28-5db9-4427-bd92-1ddaad4515b7","title":"Oncology Social Worker (8:30AM - 5:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"Social Workers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-03T22:01:53.374+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/13e52b28-5db9-4427-bd92-1ddaad4515b7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/13e52b28-5db9-4427-bd92-1ddaad4515b7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Oncology Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial, emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment and support: </strong>Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs, providing individual and family support to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resource linkage: </strong>Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care coordination: </strong>Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advocacy: </strong>Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Crisis intervention: </strong>Providing immediate support and intervention in crises such as sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education and support group facilitation: </strong>Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift &amp; additional responsibilities may be required. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong>: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LMSW, LISW, LCSW). </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications</strong>:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:  </strong>Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented</strong>: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills</strong>: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills</strong>: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability</strong>: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $80,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Thyme Care Oncology Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial, emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. \n\n - Assessment and support: Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs, providing individual and family support to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress.\n\n - Resource linkage: Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social needs. \n\n - Care coordination: Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. \n\n - Advocacy: Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. \n\n - Crisis intervention: Providing immediate support and intervention in crises such as sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. \n\n - Education and support group facilitation: Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. \n\nAs a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift & additional responsibilities may be required. \n\nThis role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - Qualifications: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LMSW, LISW, LCSW). \n\n - Certifications:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - People-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\n - Experience:  Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed.  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. \n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - A desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $80,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"db7d2ad1-7c6c-492e-9dc9-4919eea5fc50","title":"Clinical Social Worker (8:30AM - 5:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"Social Workers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-10T19:58:48.229+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/db7d2ad1-7c6c-492e-9dc9-4919eea5fc50","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/db7d2ad1-7c6c-492e-9dc9-4919eea5fc50/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Clinical Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial and emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. Primary responsibilities include: </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment and Counseling: </strong>Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment, and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress. Assess, diagnose, and provide therapeutic interventions to address behavioral health needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Crisis intervention: </strong>Providing immediate support and intervention in behavioral health crises and sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resource linkage: </strong>Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social or behavioral health needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care coordination: </strong>Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, behavioral health providers, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advocacy: </strong>Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education and support group facilitation: </strong>Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift &amp; additional responsibilities may be required. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong>: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LISW, LCSW). </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications</strong>:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:  </strong>Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented</strong>: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills</strong>: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills</strong>: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability</strong>: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $92,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Thyme Care Clinical Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial and emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. Primary responsibilities include: \n\n - Assessment and Counseling: Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment, and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress. Assess, diagnose, and provide therapeutic interventions to address behavioral health needs. \n\n - Crisis intervention: Providing immediate support and intervention in behavioral health crises and sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. \n\n - Resource linkage: Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social or behavioral health needs. \n\n - Care coordination: Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, behavioral health providers, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. \n\n - Advocacy: Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. \n\n - Education and support group facilitation: Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. \n\nAs a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift & additional responsibilities may be required. \n\nThis role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - Qualifications: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LISW, LCSW). \n\n - Certifications:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - People-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\n - Experience:  Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed.  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. \n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - A desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $92,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"984f5ecd-0a76-4127-ab8d-e166b7a3d306","title":"Nurse Practitioner, Oncology Navigation","department":"Member Experience","team":"NP","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-10T17:49:51.933+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/984f5ecd-0a76-4127-ab8d-e166b7a3d306","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/984f5ecd-0a76-4127-ab8d-e166b7a3d306/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong> YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Oncology Navigation Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical clinical team member caring for our members. You will have three primary responsibilities: </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">First, using a telemedicine platform, you will evaluate and manage members identified by our nursing and provider team who have urgent symptoms, complications related to their treatment, or exacerbations of their medical conditions. You will assess presenting symptoms, develop comprehensive care plans, triage to the appropriate level of care, educate patients, and ensure follow-up with relevant primary treating clinicians, including oncology and primary care. You will also complete annual clinical intake visits for select members.  </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Second, you will develop care plans for our members, in collaboration with our onboarding RNs, to address clinical and non-clinical needs and barriers. You will prioritize members’ goals and develop concrete plans for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers to reach these goals. To do this, you will review available medical records, work with external providers, give clinical insights to our care team, and adhere to best documentation practices to drive high-quality care for our members. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Third, you will be responsible for the oversight and direction of interdisciplinary case conferences for our members, in which individualized care plans are created and monitored by our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators. You will provide clinical oversight to the case management team and direct clinical care, as needed.  </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to these primary responsibilities, you may be asked to participate in some holiday, night and weekend emergency coverage as needed. <strong>This role is for the following shift: 11:30am-8pm Eastern.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-trocchia-dnp-fnp-bc-ocn-103671172/\">Nurse Practitioner Team Lead</a> and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be adept at developing evidence-based, member-centered care plans that will guide our Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators in effectively prioritizing our members needs and goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete whole-person urgent care assessments for our members with the highest clinical rigor. You’re working fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become the go-to person for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health workers when working with a member with complex and intersecting needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following policies, procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.<br /><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 3 years of NP experience, including 2 years in adult oncology with urgent care responsibilities and at least one year of telehealth experience. You have an unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensure.</strong><em><strong> </strong></em>You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted Advanced Practice license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses. <br /><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.<br /><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.<br /><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. <br /><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.<br /><strong>Identify priorities and take action. </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to immediately address urgent and important needs.</p><h3>Our Values:</h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and geography. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role if filled within New York City is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n YOUR ROLE \n\nAs an Oncology Navigation Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical clinical team member caring for our members. You will have three primary responsibilities: \n\nFirst, using a telemedicine platform, you will evaluate and manage members identified by our nursing and provider team who have urgent symptoms, complications related to their treatment, or exacerbations of their medical conditions. You will assess presenting symptoms, develop comprehensive care plans, triage to the appropriate level of care, educate patients, and ensure follow-up with relevant primary treating clinicians, including oncology and primary care. You will also complete annual clinical intake visits for select members.  \n\nSecond, you will develop care plans for our members, in collaboration with our onboarding RNs, to address clinical and non-clinical needs and barriers. You will prioritize members’ goals and develop concrete plans for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers to reach these goals. To do this, you will review available medical records, work with external providers, give clinical insights to our care team, and adhere to best documentation practices to drive high-quality care for our members. \n\nThird, you will be responsible for the oversight and direction of interdisciplinary case conferences for our members, in which individualized care plans are created and monitored by our team of Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators. You will provide clinical oversight to the case management team and direct clinical care, as needed.  \n\nIn addition to these primary responsibilities, you may be asked to participate in some holiday, night and weekend emergency coverage as needed. This role is for the following shift: 11:30am-8pm Eastern.\n\nThis role reports to our Nurse Practitioner Team Lead https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-trocchia-dnp-fnp-bc-ocn-103671172/ and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. \n\n - Be adept at developing evidence-based, member-centered care plans that will guide our Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators in effectively prioritizing our members needs and goals.\n\n - Complete whole-person urgent care assessments for our members with the highest clinical rigor. You’re working fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits. \n\n - Become the go-to person for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health workers when working with a member with complex and intersecting needs.\n\n - Be comfortable following policies, procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\nExperience. You have at least 3 years of NP experience, including 2 years in adult oncology with urgent care responsibilities and at least one year of telehealth experience. You have an unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed.  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company.\n\nLicensure. You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted Advanced Practice license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses. \nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to immediately address urgent and important needs.\n\n\nOUR VALUES:\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and geography. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role if filled within New York City is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"23065def-a6e0-48de-91e2-a5ada7f4c32d","title":"Oncology Nurse Navigator (11:30AM - 8:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-11T13:38:46.356+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/23065def-a6e0-48de-91e2-a5ada7f4c32d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/23065def-a6e0-48de-91e2-a5ada7f4c32d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, offering triage, support, and education throughout their cancer journey via phone and email.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will involve actively engaging with members, addressing clinical issues, and efficiently managing any escalations that arise. In contrast to TOC and Complex Oncology Nurse roles, this position focuses on symptom management and care coordination, rather than on coordinating admissions, discharges, and post-discharge needs to prevent readmission.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The shift for this position is 11:30 AM - 8 PM EST. </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Within your first three months, you will:</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and address member needs promptly, offering assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Performs other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Member-Centric Approach: </strong>You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented:</strong> You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills:</strong> You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong> An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. <strong>Compact + single state licensure in New York and/or Illinois licensure is preferred.</strong> Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications: </strong>Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is <em>$41.54/hour.</em> <em>To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. </em>We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Be cautious of </strong></em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em><strong>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</strong><br /></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE\n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, offering triage, support, and education throughout their cancer journey via phone and email.\n\nUnder the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will involve actively engaging with members, addressing clinical issues, and efficiently managing any escalations that arise. In contrast to TOC and Complex Oncology Nurse roles, this position focuses on symptom management and care coordination, rather than on coordinating admissions, discharges, and post-discharge needs to prevent readmission.\n\nThe shift for this position is 11:30 AM - 8 PM EST. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.\n\n - Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.\n\n - Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.\n\n - Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.\n\n - Identify and address member needs promptly, offering assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.\n\n - Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.\n\n - Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.\n\n - Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required\n\n - Performs other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Member-Centric Approach: You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.\n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - Qualifications: An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. Compact + single state licensure in New York and/or Illinois licensure is preferred. Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. \n\n - Certifications: Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. \n\n \n\nThis job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $41.54/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.\n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. \n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1d80a224-d96d-4ff3-9004-59780f63be8d","title":"Oncology Transitions of Care Nurse (11:30AM - 8:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-11T13:38:32.934+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1d80a224-d96d-4ff3-9004-59780f63be8d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1d80a224-d96d-4ff3-9004-59780f63be8d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As an Oncology Nurse - Transitions of Care, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus, supporting the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.<strong> </strong>This role can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville office.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications. </strong>An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of oncology nursing or case management experience and are a Certified Case Manager (CCM).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong><em><strong> </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. <em>Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The shift for this role will be 11:30 am-8 pm EST. To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE \n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As an Oncology Nurse - Transitions of Care, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus, supporting the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed. This role can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville office.\n\nMost of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. \n\n - Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.\n\n - Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.\n\n - Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.\n\n - Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.\n\n - Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.\n\n - Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.\n\n - Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.\n\n - Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.\n\n - Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.\n\n - Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one.\n\nQualifications. An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.\n\nExperience. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of oncology nursing or case management experience and are a Certified Case Manager (CCM).\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. \n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nThe shift for this role will be 11:30 am-8 pm EST. To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f4b9ec15-1e39-47a4-8943-75b4bae35551","title":"Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator (11:30AM - 8:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-11T13:38:18.758+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/f4b9ec15-1e39-47a4-8943-75b4bae35551","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/f4b9ec15-1e39-47a4-8943-75b4bae35551/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our higher-acuity members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.<strong> </strong>This role can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville office.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications. </strong>An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of high-acuity, adult oncology experience. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important. Experience with working remotely and a willingness to learn new technology are required.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong><em><strong> </strong></em>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is </em>$<em>46.35/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</em> <em>OCN certification is required at the time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE \n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Complex Oncology Nurse Navigator, you will be on the frontlines serving our members diagnosed with cancer. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. In it, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, including transitions, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment over the phone to support our higher-acuity members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed. This role can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville office.\n\nMost of your day will be dedicated to speaking with members and handling clinical escalations and tasks. We maintain a schedule that includes your lunch and breaks to ensure sufficient clinical coverage. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed training and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. \n\n - Be comfortable following Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards. Your ability to effectively engage and support our members is reflected in our efficiency metrics and quality standards.\n\n - Identify and prioritize a member's needs and help them remain safe in the community.\n\n - Assist members with care coordination and care management following admissions.\n\n - Coordinate discharge plans with hospital case managers and follow-up care with providers.\n\n - Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.\n\n - Build strong, trusting relationships with payers and providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.\n\n - Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.\n\n - Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.\n\n - Perform virtual home safety evaluations and assess the need for DME/supplies.\n\n - Provide referrals to PT, OT, skilled nursing, palliative care, hospice care, etc., as appropriate.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and by what we are building. You seek to understand problems and help people solve them, especially this one. \n\nQualifications. An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred.\n\nExperience. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience with 3 years of high-acuity, adult oncology experience. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure. \n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in learning new technology is important. Experience with working remotely and a willingness to learn new technology are required.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent and important needs immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate for this role is $46.35/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life. OCN certification is required at the time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care.\n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1d94c6ed-eb94-45fc-a3c8-623747f531b3","title":"Oncology Social Worker (11:30 AM - 8:00 PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"Social Workers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-07T18:03:35.975+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1d94c6ed-eb94-45fc-a3c8-623747f531b3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1d94c6ed-eb94-45fc-a3c8-623747f531b3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Oncology Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial, emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment and support: </strong>Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs, providing individual and family support to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resource linkage: </strong>Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care coordination: </strong>Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advocacy: </strong>Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Crisis intervention: </strong>Providing immediate support and intervention in crises such as sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education and support group facilitation: </strong>Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift &amp; additional responsibilities may be required. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong>: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LMSW, LISW, LCSW). </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications</strong>:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:  </strong>Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented</strong>: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills</strong>: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills</strong>: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability</strong>: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $80,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Thyme Care Oncology Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial, emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. \n\n - Assessment and support: Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs, providing individual and family support to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress.\n\n - Resource linkage: Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social needs. \n\n - Care coordination: Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. \n\n - Advocacy: Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. \n\n - Crisis intervention: Providing immediate support and intervention in crises such as sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. \n\n - Education and support group facilitation: Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. \n\nAs a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift & additional responsibilities may be required. \n\nThis role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - Qualifications: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LMSW, LISW, LCSW). \n\n - Certifications:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - People-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\n - Experience:  Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed.  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. \n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - A desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $80,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"21b81f7f-85eb-4943-9448-834684572044","title":"Senior Director, Corporate Development","department":"Business Development & Operations","team":"Business Development & Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:18:51.288+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/21b81f7f-85eb-4943-9448-834684572044","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/21b81f7f-85eb-4943-9448-834684572044/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Thyme Care continues to scale, we are focused on identifying the highest-impact ways to accelerate our growth, both organically and through acquisitions, investments, and strategic partnerships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director of Corporate Development will lead Thyme Care’s inorganic growth agenda, with a primary focus on acquisitions and investments. You will translate company priorities into actionable growth theses, develop and manage a pipeline of opportunities, and lead the evaluation and execution of transactions that advance Thyme Care’s long-term strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on role that will combine strategy, relationship development, financial analysis, and transaction execution. You will work closely with executive leadership and cross-functional teams to determine where Thyme Care should build, buy, partner, or invest and help turn the highest-priority opportunities into action.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-to-end evaluation of strategic opportunities, including financial modeling, diligence, and structuring, partnering closely with the executive team on go/no-go recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive acquisitions and investments from initial evaluation through close, including financial modeling, valuation, structuring, diligence, negotiation, and execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain relationships with financial sponsors, banks, and strategic counterparties, and translate complex transaction structures into clear recommendations for leadership and the board</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own analysis of complex deal mechanics and synthesize findings into board-ready materials that drive decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build the processes and infrastructure required for a disciplined and scalable corporate development function.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>We’re looking for someone who has:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience across corporate development, investment banking, private equity, growth equity, management consulting, and/or strategic finance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful experience evaluating or executing acquisitions, investments, strategic partnerships, joint ventures, or other complex transactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong financial modeling and valuation skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing investment theses, market maps, competitive landscapes, target screens, or strategic recommendations for senior executives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A high degree of ownership and the ability to drive multiple opportunities forward in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort leading diligence workstreams and coordinating cross-functional input from Finance, Legal, Product, Clinical, Operations, Growth, Data, and other internal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence senior leaders and synthesize complex analyses into clear recommendations.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission matters deeply to you, particularly our member experience.  You are deeply passionate about leveraging technology to improve healthcare outcomes and enhance the experience for all stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose.</strong> Your bias for action and ability to prioritize will be crucial. You know how to identify critical needs and drive timely execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfortable with ambiguity.</strong> You possess a proven track record of thriving in the dynamic and often unpredictable nature of a startup, particularly within the evolving health tech landscape. You embrace change and can adapt strategies as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expertise in Health Tech Business Development &amp; Operations.</strong> Your deep understanding of the health tech market, including its unique challenges and opportunities, and your experience in building strategic partnerships and launching new initiatives, will be critical to your success.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $199,750 - $235,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\n\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs Thyme Care continues to scale, we are focused on identifying the highest-impact ways to accelerate our growth, both organically and through acquisitions, investments, and strategic partnerships.\n\nThe Director of Corporate Development will lead Thyme Care’s inorganic growth agenda, with a primary focus on acquisitions and investments. You will translate company priorities into actionable growth theses, develop and manage a pipeline of opportunities, and lead the evaluation and execution of transactions that advance Thyme Care’s long-term strategy.\n\nThis is a hands-on role that will combine strategy, relationship development, financial analysis, and transaction execution. You will work closely with executive leadership and cross-functional teams to determine where Thyme Care should build, buy, partner, or invest and help turn the highest-priority opportunities into action.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n - Lead end-to-end evaluation of strategic opportunities, including financial modeling, diligence, and structuring, partnering closely with the executive team on go/no-go recommendations\n\n - Drive acquisitions and investments from initial evaluation through close, including financial modeling, valuation, structuring, diligence, negotiation, and execution.\n\n - Build and maintain relationships with financial sponsors, banks, and strategic counterparties, and translate complex transaction structures into clear recommendations for leadership and the board\n\n - Own analysis of complex deal mechanics and synthesize findings into board-ready materials that drive decisions\n\n - Help build the processes and infrastructure required for a disciplined and scalable corporate development function.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n \n\nWe’re looking for someone who has:\n\n - 8+ years of experience across corporate development, investment banking, private equity, growth equity, management consulting, and/or strategic finance.\n\n - Meaningful experience evaluating or executing acquisitions, investments, strategic partnerships, joint ventures, or other complex transactions.\n\n - Strong financial modeling and valuation skills.\n\n - Experience developing investment theses, market maps, competitive landscapes, target screens, or strategic recommendations for senior executives.\n\n - A high degree of ownership and the ability to drive multiple opportunities forward in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment.\n\n - Comfort leading diligence workstreams and coordinating cross-functional input from Finance, Legal, Product, Clinical, Operations, Growth, Data, and other internal teams.\n\n - Ability to influence senior leaders and synthesize complex analyses into clear recommendations.\n\n \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Act with our members in mind. Thyme Care’s mission matters deeply to you, particularly our member experience.  You are deeply passionate about leveraging technology to improve healthcare outcomes and enhance the experience for all stakeholders.\n\n - Move with purpose. Your bias for action and ability to prioritize will be crucial. You know how to identify critical needs and drive timely execution.\n\n - Comfortable with ambiguity. You possess a proven track record of thriving in the dynamic and often unpredictable nature of a startup, particularly within the evolving health tech landscape. You embrace change and can adapt strategies as needed.\n\n - Expertise in Health Tech Business Development & Operations. Your deep understanding of the health tech market, including its unique challenges and opportunities, and your experience in building strategic partnerships and launching new initiatives, will be critical to your success.\n\n \n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $199,750 - $235,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.\n\n \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n \n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n\n \n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"02a7a129-1f31-47e0-94b3-ec29fb1af1ae","title":"Behavioral Health Oncology Nurse","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-07T22:08:15.511+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/02a7a129-1f31-47e0-94b3-ec29fb1af1ae","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/02a7a129-1f31-47e0-94b3-ec29fb1af1ae/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Specialty Behavioral Health Oncology Nurse role is focused on supporting members living concurrently with cancer and with high-complexity, persistent, and multifactorial behavioral health needs. This role will partner closely with our Care Team, including Social Work and Community Health Workers, to address barriers related to behavioral health - serving as the nursing expert, addressing symptom management and clinical education. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. <br /><br />In this role, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment using telemedicine and telephonic platforms to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Care and Member Support</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide ongoing, longitudinal nursing support for members whose behavioral health concerns range from mild adjustment related coping support needs to more severe mental illness. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusting relationships with providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Queue Management and Coordination of Care</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide timely, high-quality care to members while upholding established productivity, quality, responsiveness, and performance expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor assigned queue items, scheduled calls, and Slack communications to ensure timely follow-up and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Route urgent or complex issues to the appropriate care team members or leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, clinical protocols, and documentation standards to maintain quality and operational efficiency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain familiarity with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and external partners to effectively perform daily responsibilities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interdisciplinary Collaboration</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare charts in advance with up-to-date member information and actively participate in interdisciplinary case conferences by listening to and incorporating cross-functional perspectives, sharing nursing assessments and recommendations, and aligning care plans to support coordinated, well-informed patient care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health, including food access, transportation, and other supportive resources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in huddles and pod meetings to provide updates and support coordinated care delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with cross functional stakeholders such as care partners, social workers, medical directors, nurse leaders and external stakeholders such as providers and payers specific to each member</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Culture</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to a team culture grounded in adaptability, resilience, professionalism, and a solutions-focused mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Approach challenges with flexibility and accountability, maintaining composure in a fast-paced and evolving environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate respectfully and constructively with teammates and cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate reliability, ownership, and commitment to shared team goals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS<br /></strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a strong commitment to Thyme Care’s mission and values.<br /><strong>A BSN. </strong>You must have a Bachelor of Science Degree in Nursing, a multi-state, unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) compact license, and willingness to obtain additional state licenses, as needed.<br /><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 2 years in advanced clinical judgment and problem-solving skills in complex, non-linear behavioral health cases. Preferred experience in oncology nursing. Certification as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN) is preferred and will be required within 2 years of hire. .<br /><strong>Collaborative Team Player:</strong> You work effectively with teammates and cross-functional partners, communicating clearly and professionally to support coordinated, high-quality care.<br /><strong>Effective Communicator:</strong> You are an active listener who builds rapport with members and colleagues and communicates thoughtfully and clearly.<br /><strong>Organized, Efficient, &amp; Detail-Oriented:</strong> You manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. You demonstrate superior time-management while maintaining accurate, timely documentation and clear communication<br /><strong>Action-Oriented:</strong> You proactively identify priorities and take timely action to address member and team needs.<br /><strong>Adaptable:</strong> You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and remain flexible as workflows and priorities evolve.<br /><strong>Professional &amp; Reliable:</strong> You demonstrate accountability, composure, and consistency in your daily work, contributing positively to team effectiveness.<br /><strong>Grit</strong>. You’re never afraid to get your hands dirty, but you can also take a step back and connect the company’s strategy to your team’s performance and execution.<br /><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies. </strong>We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in learning new technology is essential.<br /><strong>Bias to action</strong>. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The hourly rate for this role is </em>$<em>46.35. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em>recruitment fraud</em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nThe Specialty Behavioral Health Oncology Nurse role is focused on supporting members living concurrently with cancer and with high-complexity, persistent, and multifactorial behavioral health needs. This role will partner closely with our Care Team, including Social Work and Community Health Workers, to address barriers related to behavioral health - serving as the nursing expert, addressing symptom management and clinical education. This role reports to our RN Care Team Lead. \n\nIn this role, you will conduct clinical assessments, monitor for changes in health, coordinate care, and educate members and caregivers about their diagnosis and treatment using telemedicine and telephonic platforms to support our members as they move through the oncology care continuum. You will demonstrate a strong clinical focus that supports the need for culturally competent care. Additionally, you will help improve Thyme Care’s service offerings by communicating member and provider feedback to our clinical leadership. You will also assist with other administrative projects as needed.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nClinical Care and Member Support\n\n - Provide ongoing, longitudinal nursing support for members whose behavioral health concerns range from mild adjustment related coping support needs to more severe mental illness. \n\n - Monitor member progress, provide regular updates, and establish targeted support plans with the healthcare team in case conferences.\n\n - Build strong, trusting relationships with providers to optimize care and prevent readmissions for our members.\n\n - Conducting telephonic assessments, including pain assessments and medication reconciliation.\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to support the member’s social determinants of health needs, such as food resources, transportation access, and support at home.\n\n - Ensure members have access to medications and appointments, providing referrals and support as appropriate.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\nQueue Management and Coordination of Care\n\n - Provide timely, high-quality care to members while upholding established productivity, quality, responsiveness, and performance expectations\n\n - Monitor assigned queue items, scheduled calls, and Slack communications to ensure timely follow-up and documentation\n\n - Route urgent or complex issues to the appropriate care team members or leaders\n\n - Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, clinical protocols, and documentation standards to maintain quality and operational efficiency\n\n - Maintain familiarity with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and external partners to effectively perform daily responsibilities\n\nInterdisciplinary Collaboration\n\n - Prepare charts in advance with up-to-date member information and actively participate in interdisciplinary case conferences by listening to and incorporating cross-functional perspectives, sharing nursing assessments and recommendations, and aligning care plans to support coordinated, well-informed patient care\n\n - Partner with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health, including food access, transportation, and other supportive resources\n\n - Participate in huddles and pod meetings to provide updates and support coordinated care delivery\n\n - Collaborate with cross functional stakeholders such as care partners, social workers, medical directors, nurse leaders and external stakeholders such as providers and payers specific to each member\n\nTeam Culture\n\n - Contribute to a team culture grounded in adaptability, resilience, professionalism, and a solutions-focused mindset\n\n - Approach challenges with flexibility and accountability, maintaining composure in a fast-paced and evolving environment\n\n - Communicate respectfully and constructively with teammates and cross-functional partners\n\n - Demonstrate reliability, ownership, and commitment to shared team goals\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n\nPeople-first. You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a strong commitment to Thyme Care’s mission and values.\nA BSN. You must have a Bachelor of Science Degree in Nursing, a multi-state, unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) compact license, and willingness to obtain additional state licenses, as needed.\nExperience. You have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 2 years in advanced clinical judgment and problem-solving skills in complex, non-linear behavioral health cases. Preferred experience in oncology nursing. Certification as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN) is preferred and will be required within 2 years of hire. .\nCollaborative Team Player: You work effectively with teammates and cross-functional partners, communicating clearly and professionally to support coordinated, high-quality care.\nEffective Communicator: You are an active listener who builds rapport with members and colleagues and communicates thoughtfully and clearly.\nOrganized, Efficient, & Detail-Oriented: You manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. You demonstrate superior time-management while maintaining accurate, timely documentation and clear communication\nAction-Oriented: You proactively identify priorities and take timely action to address member and team needs.\nAdaptable: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and remain flexible as workflows and priorities evolve.\nProfessional & Reliable: You demonstrate accountability, composure, and consistency in your daily work, contributing positively to team effectiveness.\nGrit. You’re never afraid to get your hands dirty, but you can also take a step back and connect the company’s strategy to your team’s performance and execution.\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in learning new technology is essential.\nBias to action. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The hourly rate for this role is $46.35. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"99bb529b-4a5f-4c2a-a0e7-52775b26eb2d","title":"Enrollment Specialist","department":"Member Experience","team":"Enrollment Specialists","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-08T21:41:10.588+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/99bb529b-4a5f-4c2a-a0e7-52775b26eb2d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/99bb529b-4a5f-4c2a-a0e7-52775b26eb2d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Enrollment Specialist, your job is to talk to prospective members, educate them on our services, and encourage them to join Thyme Care to receive free-of-cost support throughout their cancer journey. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the first touch point for members who are eligible for Thyme Care, Enrollment Specialists build a foundation of trust by listening deeply, and taking the time to understand each member’s needs so we can successfully enroll them into our program. You will also be responsible for carefully documenting member needs and preferences to enable our team to best care for each member.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports into our Enrollment Specialist Team Lead and in it you will be expected to make outbound calls to anywhere from around 80 - 100 prospective members every day, depending on your assignment. To ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes lunch and two breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed virtual onboarding and training (three weeks long) and be up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be completing around 80 outbound calls with prospective members each day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable with and correctly follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reach out to eligible members to inform them of Thyme Care’s services and ways we can support them in their cancer care journey. You’ll also build strong, trusting relationships with members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction you have with them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explain the benefits of Thyme Care’s program so that both members and caregivers understand how we can help them and enroll them in our program and the value of our services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Obtain consent from members, conduct enrollment surveys, and identify and escalate any urgent member needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your quality and productivity goal.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>THIS ROLE IS IDEAL FOR INDIVIDUALS WHO:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have experience in sales roles. You know how to build trust, listen deeply, and overcome objections, and you want to continue to hone this skill; <strong>or</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are recent college graduates with 1+ years of experience in a fast-paced environment. Bonus points for experience working in a healthcare environment, start-up, or in a sales capacity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first Approach.</strong> You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about helping people during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metrics Focused.</strong> You can hit your daily, weekly, and monthly goals and frequently exceed them. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth Mindset</strong>. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator.</strong> You are a clear and articulate communicator, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with technology</strong>. You have experience working with Zoom, Google Suite, and Slack, and are comfortable learning new technologies with minimal guidance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Start-up Flexibility.</strong>  You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, and priorities is par for the course and you are energized by start-up life.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Private Working Environment</strong>. To ensure member privacy and compliance with healthcare privacy laws, you must operate in a private, quiet and secure environment during the entirety of your scheduled shifts, and have reliable, high speed internet available at all times (and the ability to check/verify this prior to joining).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successful candidates are resilient, goal-oriented, adaptable, and energized by connecting with people during critical moments in their lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $24.03/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Bonus potential:</strong> Up to $2,500 per quarter (up to $10,000 annually) for exceptional performance. New hires are eligible to participate in the bonus program only after successfully graduating from their 90 day probationary period.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The shift for this role will be 9:00am–5:30pm EST, Monday through Friday.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Be cautious of </strong></em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em><strong>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs an Enrollment Specialist, your job is to talk to prospective members, educate them on our services, and encourage them to join Thyme Care to receive free-of-cost support throughout their cancer journey. \n\nAs the first touch point for members who are eligible for Thyme Care, Enrollment Specialists build a foundation of trust by listening deeply, and taking the time to understand each member’s needs so we can successfully enroll them into our program. You will also be responsible for carefully documenting member needs and preferences to enable our team to best care for each member.\n\nThis role reports into our Enrollment Specialist Team Lead and in it you will be expected to make outbound calls to anywhere from around 80 - 100 prospective members every day, depending on your assignment. To ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes lunch and two breaks.\n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed virtual onboarding and training (three weeks long) and be up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. \n\n - Be completing around 80 outbound calls with prospective members each day.\n\n - Be comfortable with and correctly follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.\n\n - Reach out to eligible members to inform them of Thyme Care’s services and ways we can support them in their cancer care journey. You’ll also build strong, trusting relationships with members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction you have with them.\n\n - Explain the benefits of Thyme Care’s program so that both members and caregivers understand how we can help them and enroll them in our program and the value of our services.\n\n - Obtain consent from members, conduct enrollment surveys, and identify and escalate any urgent member needs.\n\n - Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your quality and productivity goal.\n\nTHIS ROLE IS IDEAL FOR INDIVIDUALS WHO:\n\n - Have experience in sales roles. You know how to build trust, listen deeply, and overcome objections, and you want to continue to hone this skill; or\n\n - Are recent college graduates with 1+ years of experience in a fast-paced environment. Bonus points for experience working in a healthcare environment, start-up, or in a sales capacity.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - A member-first Approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about helping people during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives.\n\n - Metrics Focused. You can hit your daily, weekly, and monthly goals and frequently exceed them. \n\n - Growth Mindset. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.\n\n - Effective listener and communicator. You are a clear and articulate communicator, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Comfort with technology. You have experience working with Zoom, Google Suite, and Slack, and are comfortable learning new technologies with minimal guidance.\n\n - Start-up Flexibility.  You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, and priorities is par for the course and you are energized by start-up life.\n\n - Private Working Environment. To ensure member privacy and compliance with healthcare privacy laws, you must operate in a private, quiet and secure environment during the entirety of your scheduled shifts, and have reliable, high speed internet available at all times (and the ability to check/verify this prior to joining).\n\nSuccessful candidates are resilient, goal-oriented, adaptable, and energized by connecting with people during critical moments in their lives.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $24.03/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.\n\nBonus potential: Up to $2,500 per quarter (up to $10,000 annually) for exceptional performance. New hires are eligible to participate in the bonus program only after successfully graduating from their 90 day probationary period.\n\nThe shift for this role will be 9:00am–5:30pm EST, Monday through Friday.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1590d28c-9cff-4a8c-b424-8825ad5905d9","title":"Senior Platform Engineer, Data","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T16:08:43.224+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1590d28c-9cff-4a8c-b424-8825ad5905d9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/1590d28c-9cff-4a8c-b424-8825ad5905d9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Platform Engineer on the Data Platform team, you will work on a blend of platform and devex engineering – owning key systems and tooling to ensure both our data pipelines and tooling are reliable and scale as Thyme Care continues to grow. You will join an organization that has prioritized the developer experience from day one and believes that our data teams are most effective when they have the right tools for the job. You will partner with our data, analytics, and actuarial teams to scale the tooling and infrastructure to support faster, more accurate insights that directly impact the members we serve.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead our team’s orchestration consolidation to Dagster end-to-end, from technical design through implementation and rollout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to our custom dbt-core infrastructure that has scaled to over 50 dbt projects and 15 thousand models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement the Python abstractions our data tooling is built on, so that a new project or pipeline inherits consistent structure and conventions instead of reinventing them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop proactive monitoring and alerting for our tooling and data pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ownership of both technical solutions and the growth of the engineering team by mentoring junior engineers and fostering a culture of learning, collaboration, and technical excellence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make Databricks easier to build on, developing the tooling, defaults, and guardrails that let our teams run their own workloads without needing to become platform experts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 5+ years of experience building, shipping, and supporting software in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are an experienced Python engineer who has built and operated systems on AWS, including internal tools and complex job orchestration with Dagster or Airflow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have taken ownership of features from idea to production, including design, implementation, testing, and ongoing improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have deployed and operated cloud infrastructure with infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform), and have built or contributed to the CI processes your team ships through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have used and contributed to AI tooling that supports developer productivity, code quality, and engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have worked as a data or platform engineer in a modern data stack environment, ideally in a fast-moving, early-stage or growth-stage company.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have, but not required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have hands-on experience with Databricks or Snowflake.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have built, deployed, and maintained dbt at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have prior experience working in healthcare or health tech.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.</strong> You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and problems aren’t fully defined. You take ownership, bias toward action, and are comfortable making progress with imperfect information, while maintaining a high bar for quality as products and teams mature.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Curiosity.</strong> You have a drive to understand how things work and love sharing that knowledge with others. You’re energized by learning new technologies, improving systems, and helping your teammates grow. (Find out more about our engineering team’s culture of learning <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://eng.thymecare.com/blog/culture-of-learning\"><u>here</u></a>!)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engineering fundamentals.</strong> You know how to deploy software engineering best practices, such as unit tests, code reviews, and design documentation. You have also worked building internal tools and systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply. You’re an empathetic teammate who communicates clearly, collaborates across disciplines, and values giving and receiving thoughtful feedback. You care about building products that improve people’s lives as much as you care about helping your teammates succeed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $175,500-$195,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Platform Engineer on the Data Platform team, you will work on a blend of platform and devex engineering – owning key systems and tooling to ensure both our data pipelines and tooling are reliable and scale as Thyme Care continues to grow. You will join an organization that has prioritized the developer experience from day one and believes that our data teams are most effective when they have the right tools for the job. You will partner with our data, analytics, and actuarial teams to scale the tooling and infrastructure to support faster, more accurate insights that directly impact the members we serve.\n\nAdditionally, you will:\n\n - Lead our team’s orchestration consolidation to Dagster end-to-end, from technical design through implementation and rollout.\n\n - Contribute to our custom dbt-core infrastructure that has scaled to over 50 dbt projects and 15 thousand models.\n\n - Design and implement the Python abstractions our data tooling is built on, so that a new project or pipeline inherits consistent structure and conventions instead of reinventing them.\n\n - Develop proactive monitoring and alerting for our tooling and data pipelines.\n\n - Take ownership of both technical solutions and the growth of the engineering team by mentoring junior engineers and fostering a culture of learning, collaboration, and technical excellence.\n\n - Make Databricks easier to build on, developing the tooling, defaults, and guardrails that let our teams run their own workloads without needing to become platform experts.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - You have 5+ years of experience building, shipping, and supporting software in production.\n\n - You are an experienced Python engineer who has built and operated systems on AWS, including internal tools and complex job orchestration with Dagster or Airflow.\n\n - You have taken ownership of features from idea to production, including design, implementation, testing, and ongoing improvements.\n\n - You have deployed and operated cloud infrastructure with infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform), and have built or contributed to the CI processes your team ships through.\n\n - You have used and contributed to AI tooling that supports developer productivity, code quality, and engineering best practices.\n\n - You have worked as a data or platform engineer in a modern data stack environment, ideally in a fast-moving, early-stage or growth-stage company.\n\nNice to have, but not required:\n\n - You have hands-on experience with Databricks or Snowflake.\n\n - You have built, deployed, and maintained dbt at scale.\n\n - You have prior experience working in healthcare or health tech.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nComfort with ambiguity. You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and problems aren’t fully defined. You take ownership, bias toward action, and are comfortable making progress with imperfect information, while maintaining a high bar for quality as products and teams mature.\n\nCuriosity. You have a drive to understand how things work and love sharing that knowledge with others. You’re energized by learning new technologies, improving systems, and helping your teammates grow. (Find out more about our engineering team’s culture of learning here https://eng.thymecare.com/blog/culture-of-learning!)\n\nEngineering fundamentals. You know how to deploy software engineering best practices, such as unit tests, code reviews, and design documentation. You have also worked building internal tools and systems.\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply. You’re an empathetic teammate who communicates clearly, collaborates across disciplines, and values giving and receiving thoughtful feedback. You care about building products that improve people’s lives as much as you care about helping your teammates succeed.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $175,500-$195,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"88ca71a9-d45a-40ea-a866-ce4ac4381639","title":"Technical Implementation Specialist","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-06T01:02:30.148+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/88ca71a9-d45a-40ea-a866-ce4ac4381639","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/88ca71a9-d45a-40ea-a866-ce4ac4381639/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>Our Mission </h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.<br /></p><h2>What You’ll Do</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you'll sit at the intersection of product development and care delivery — translating complex clinical and operational processes into our purpose-built tools to support our care team in their day-to-day work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll partner closely with a service designer who works with operations teams to understand and map new processes onto our tools. You’ll focus on the technical implementation and productization of those processes, ensuring that your approach serves the care team, engineering, and data science.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your work will span creative implementation within our current tooling, maintaining and curating what exists, and helping shape the product direction that will evolve these tools to better support care teams over time.</p><h3><strong>Day-to-day, you will:</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute configurations in close collaboration with a service designer, including forms, automations, and our proprietary tasking system</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build structured documentation systems to support clean data capture, with conditional logic and extensibility in mind</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and test automations within Thyme Box, accounting for edge cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build tasking that clearly and cleanly maps out complex, branching processes</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate bugs and unexpected behavior, educate users on underlying logic, and build towards transparency and understandability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit and maintain existing configurations: improving consistency, defining best practices, deprecating what is outdated, and building for scale</p></li></ul><h2>What Leads to Success</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product and technical foundations</strong>. You have relevant experience with digital products — as a product manager, product designer, or in a technical implementation role. While not necessarily an engineer, you understand web applications and can read, debug, and write simple code. You think like an engineer about data models, edge cases, and downstream impacts of implementation decisions. Where you may not have the skillset or expertise in a particular area today, you are willing to invest time to learn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Detail orientation</strong>. You can juggle a high volume of requests without sacrificing organization or accuracy. You document carefully and communicate proactively. You don’t let details slip.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems stewardship</strong>. You take ownership of our tools as living systems — not just building, but curating on an ongoing basis. Naming conventions and consistency matter to you. You proactively address technical debt, define best practices, and push back when a short-term request would create long-term disorder.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Creative problem solving</strong>. When a request fits neatly into existing patterns, you execute with precision. When it doesn't, you quickly generate scrappy short-term solutions while articulating a longer-term alternative vision. You make educated guesses and iterate rigorously.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical translation</strong>. You communicate fluidly in both directions — explaining technical concepts plainly to non-technical teammates, and engaging clearly with engineers and data scientists on existing logic, edge cases, and future tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Humility and collaboration</strong>. You listen first, act second. You approach new requests and problems with curiosity. You build consensus by default, but can drive tough decisions when needed. You push the pace. You recognize that hard problems are solved by teams, not individuals. You say what you’ll do, and do what you say. You speak up when something goes awry, and roll up your sleeves to help address it.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more about our existing systems:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/thymebox\"><u>Thyme Box: An oncology navigation care delivery platform.</u></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://blog.thymecare.com/what-is-thyme-box-and-how-does-it-drive-better-cancer-care\"><u>What is Thyme Box and How Does It Drive Better Cancer Care?</u></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://blog.thymecare.com/how-thyme-box-supercharges-our-care-team\"><u>How Thyme Box Supercharges our Care Team</u></a></p></li></ul><h2>Our Values</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $139,500-$155,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be cautious of recruitment fraud, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION \n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nIn this role, you'll sit at the intersection of product development and care delivery — translating complex clinical and operational processes into our purpose-built tools to support our care team in their day-to-day work.\n\nYou'll partner closely with a service designer who works with operations teams to understand and map new processes onto our tools. You’ll focus on the technical implementation and productization of those processes, ensuring that your approach serves the care team, engineering, and data science.\n\nYour work will span creative implementation within our current tooling, maintaining and curating what exists, and helping shape the product direction that will evolve these tools to better support care teams over time.\n\n\nDAY-TO-DAY, YOU WILL:\n\n - Execute configurations in close collaboration with a service designer, including forms, automations, and our proprietary tasking system\n   \n   - Build structured documentation systems to support clean data capture, with conditional logic and extensibility in mind\n   \n   - Build and test automations within Thyme Box, accounting for edge cases\n   \n   - Build tasking that clearly and cleanly maps out complex, branching processes\n\n - Investigate bugs and unexpected behavior, educate users on underlying logic, and build towards transparency and understandability\n\n - Audit and maintain existing configurations: improving consistency, defining best practices, deprecating what is outdated, and building for scale\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Product and technical foundations. You have relevant experience with digital products — as a product manager, product designer, or in a technical implementation role. While not necessarily an engineer, you understand web applications and can read, debug, and write simple code. You think like an engineer about data models, edge cases, and downstream impacts of implementation decisions. Where you may not have the skillset or expertise in a particular area today, you are willing to invest time to learn.\n\n - Detail orientation. You can juggle a high volume of requests without sacrificing organization or accuracy. You document carefully and communicate proactively. You don’t let details slip.\n\n - Systems stewardship. You take ownership of our tools as living systems — not just building, but curating on an ongoing basis. Naming conventions and consistency matter to you. You proactively address technical debt, define best practices, and push back when a short-term request would create long-term disorder.\n\n - Creative problem solving. When a request fits neatly into existing patterns, you execute with precision. When it doesn't, you quickly generate scrappy short-term solutions while articulating a longer-term alternative vision. You make educated guesses and iterate rigorously.\n\n - Technical translation. You communicate fluidly in both directions — explaining technical concepts plainly to non-technical teammates, and engaging clearly with engineers and data scientists on existing logic, edge cases, and future tradeoffs.\n\n - Humility and collaboration. You listen first, act second. You approach new requests and problems with curiosity. You build consensus by default, but can drive tough decisions when needed. You push the pace. You recognize that hard problems are solved by teams, not individuals. You say what you’ll do, and do what you say. You speak up when something goes awry, and roll up your sleeves to help address it.\n\nLearn more about our existing systems:\n\n - Thyme Box: An oncology navigation care delivery platform. https://www.thymecare.com/thymebox\n\n - What is Thyme Box and How Does It Drive Better Cancer Care? https://blog.thymecare.com/what-is-thyme-box-and-how-does-it-drive-better-cancer-care\n\n - How Thyme Box Supercharges our Care Team https://blog.thymecare.com/how-thyme-box-supercharges-our-care-team\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $139,500-$155,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"00b7f190-7cda-4eb1-b9b5-3571e138dfe4","title":"Medical Director, Oncology","department":"Clinical Strategy","team":"Clinical Strategy","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T20:17:12.245+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/00b7f190-7cda-4eb1-b9b5-3571e138dfe4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/00b7f190-7cda-4eb1-b9b5-3571e138dfe4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Our Team as a Medical Director for Oncology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Medical Oncologist to join our clinical team as a Medical Director for Oncology. In this role, you will serve as a strategic clinical leader, working across functions to advance our clinical programs, support our frontline care team, and contribute to Thyme Care's broader organizational priorities. You will have three core responsibilities:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1. ePRO Program Leadership:</strong> You will own and drive the evolution of our electronic patient-reported outcomes (ePRO) program, ensuring we deliver measurable outcomes for our members. This means setting the clinical vision for how we collect, interpret, and act on patient-reported data, and working alongside cross-functional teams to bring that vision to life. You will guide program design and iteration, establish and refine clinical thresholds and escalation pathways, enable staff training, and track key performance indicators. You will work closely with our technology and product teams to ensure our ePRO tools reflect current clinical evidence and meet the needs of our member population. Your leadership will ensure that ePROs are a meaningful and scalable part of how we support members throughout their cancer journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2. Frontline Care Team Support and Clinical Collaboration:</strong> You will serve as a clinical resource for our frontline care team, providing education, guidance, and direct collaboration to support quality care. This includes participating in case conferences, offering oncology expertise for complex or escalated clinical situations, and partnering with our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers on challenging cases. You will contribute to care team education through structured training sessions, clinical updates, and ongoing feedback. You will help our team stay current on evolving oncology standards and ensure clinical practices across the organization are grounded in evidence and aligned with member needs. You will also have the opportunity to do virtual visits with our members.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3. Special Projects and Strategic Initiatives:</strong> In close partnership with cross-functional partners, you will lead and contribute to strategic initiatives across the organization. This includes developing and maintaining clinical protocols, helping members access clinical trials, and representing Thyme Care in external meetings with payers, health systems, and other partners. You will serve as a clinical voice on oncology issues, contributing to how Thyme Care is positioned in the broader oncology landscape. You will also support the development of clinical content, policy positions, and responses to external clinical questions as they arise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role offers an opportunity to be part of a forward-thinking, supportive, and highly collaborative team. This role reports to our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/julia-frydman-1b080b1b/\"><u>VP for Clinical Outcomes &amp; Quality</u></a>, and you'll work remotely or in a hybrid setting from our Nashville or New York City offices.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within your first three months, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care's systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. You will develop a working understanding of our member population, care model, and the clinical and operational context in which we operate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a deep understanding of our ePRO program, including its current state, clinical thresholds, escalation pathways, and roadmap. You will build relationships with key stakeholders across clinical, product, and technology teams, and begin identifying opportunities to improve program design, workflows, and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build relationships with our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers, participate in case conferences, and begin serving as a trusted clinical resource for the frontline care team. You will start contributing to care team education and providing guidance on complex or escalated clinical situations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with cross-functional partners and begin contributing to active special projects and strategic initiatives. This may include supporting clinical protocol development, participating in external meetings, or contributing to Thyme Care's clinical positioning on oncology issues.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 3 years of clinical experience caring for oncology patients after fellowship training with board certification in medical oncology. You have an unrestricted medical license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. It would be exceptional if you have experience with electronic patient-reported outcome (ePRO) implementation, iteration, and reporting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are decisive and articulate, but you always start by listening, and you hear what may not be voiced because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action. </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, geography, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role, if filled within New York City, is $246,500-$290,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nJoin Our Team as a Medical Director for Oncology.\n\nWe are looking for a Medical Oncologist to join our clinical team as a Medical Director for Oncology. In this role, you will serve as a strategic clinical leader, working across functions to advance our clinical programs, support our frontline care team, and contribute to Thyme Care's broader organizational priorities. You will have three core responsibilities:\n\n1. ePRO Program Leadership: You will own and drive the evolution of our electronic patient-reported outcomes (ePRO) program, ensuring we deliver measurable outcomes for our members. This means setting the clinical vision for how we collect, interpret, and act on patient-reported data, and working alongside cross-functional teams to bring that vision to life. You will guide program design and iteration, establish and refine clinical thresholds and escalation pathways, enable staff training, and track key performance indicators. You will work closely with our technology and product teams to ensure our ePRO tools reflect current clinical evidence and meet the needs of our member population. Your leadership will ensure that ePROs are a meaningful and scalable part of how we support members throughout their cancer journey.\n\n2. Frontline Care Team Support and Clinical Collaboration: You will serve as a clinical resource for our frontline care team, providing education, guidance, and direct collaboration to support quality care. This includes participating in case conferences, offering oncology expertise for complex or escalated clinical situations, and partnering with our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers on challenging cases. You will contribute to care team education through structured training sessions, clinical updates, and ongoing feedback. You will help our team stay current on evolving oncology standards and ensure clinical practices across the organization are grounded in evidence and aligned with member needs. You will also have the opportunity to do virtual visits with our members.\n\n3. Special Projects and Strategic Initiatives: In close partnership with cross-functional partners, you will lead and contribute to strategic initiatives across the organization. This includes developing and maintaining clinical protocols, helping members access clinical trials, and representing Thyme Care in external meetings with payers, health systems, and other partners. You will serve as a clinical voice on oncology issues, contributing to how Thyme Care is positioned in the broader oncology landscape. You will also support the development of clinical content, policy positions, and responses to external clinical questions as they arise.\n\nThis role offers an opportunity to be part of a forward-thinking, supportive, and highly collaborative team. This role reports to our VP for Clinical Outcomes & Quality https://www.linkedin.com/in/julia-frydman-1b080b1b/, and you'll work remotely or in a hybrid setting from our Nashville or New York City offices.\n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care's systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations. You will develop a working understanding of our member population, care model, and the clinical and operational context in which we operate.\n\n - Develop a deep understanding of our ePRO program, including its current state, clinical thresholds, escalation pathways, and roadmap. You will build relationships with key stakeholders across clinical, product, and technology teams, and begin identifying opportunities to improve program design, workflows, and outcomes.\n\n - Build relationships with our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers, participate in case conferences, and begin serving as a trusted clinical resource for the frontline care team. You will start contributing to care team education and providing guidance on complex or escalated clinical situations.\n\n - Engage with cross-functional partners and begin contributing to active special projects and strategic initiatives. This may include supporting clinical protocol development, participating in external meetings, or contributing to Thyme Care's clinical positioning on oncology issues.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\nExperience. You have at least 3 years of clinical experience caring for oncology patients after fellowship training with board certification in medical oncology. You have an unrestricted medical license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. It would be exceptional if you have experience with electronic patient-reported outcome (ePRO) implementation, iteration, and reporting.\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are decisive and articulate, but you always start by listening, and you hear what may not be voiced because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure.\n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent needs.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, geography, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role, if filled within New York City, is $246,500-$290,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2c81b7e3-b13c-4406-9ddd-55255f54ec69","title":"Enrollment Specialist Team Lead","department":"Member Experience","team":"Team Leads & Leadership - ES","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-02T14:44:19.936+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/2c81b7e3-b13c-4406-9ddd-55255f54ec69","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/2c81b7e3-b13c-4406-9ddd-55255f54ec69/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Team Lead, you're the engine behind a high-performing enrollment team. You'll coach and develop a group of Enrollment Specialists, keep daily operations running smoothly, and drive the results that get patients connected to Thyme Care's program. This is a hands-on leadership role — you'll stay close to the work by doing direct patient outreach yourself, so you can lead from experience, not just from the sidelines.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop your team.</strong> Your primary responsibility will be to coach a team of Enrollment Specialists to hit daily and weekly performance targets, running weekly team huddles and 1:1s to keep everyone trained, supported, and performing at their best.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep operations on track.</strong> You will also handle day-to-day HR tasks like approving timecards and PTO, and coach your team to follow processes seamlessly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive continuous improvement.</strong> You will partner with other team leads to ensure the enrollment queues are working well, and will roll up your sleeves to fix issues when you see them. You will also surface opportunities to leadership to sharpen team scripts, workflows, and hand-offs, always with an eye toward improving enrollment conversion and achieving our team goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stay close to members.</strong> You will continue to do direct patient outreach and enrollment a few hours each week so you stay sharp on best practices and can support your team from real, current experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>First Three Months of Training</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Before stepping into full team management, you'll spend your first few weeks becoming an expert in the Enrollment Specialist role yourself — so you can coach others from a place of genuine knowledge.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Weeks 1–3: Onboarding.</strong> Complete virtual training and get up to speed on Thyme Care's systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations, as well as the ins and out of the Enrollment Specialist role so you can begin to do member outreach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Weeks 4–12: Building Enrollment Proficiency.</strong> Learn and practice Thyme Care's enrollment methods — how to use our proprietary outreach tool, connect with members, explain our program's value, escalate urgent needs, obtain consents, and successfully enroll patients. You'll work in the Enrollment Specialist role until you've demonstrated consistent proficiency across:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Making 60–100 outbound calls per day</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sustaining 30%+ call conversion over 3 weeks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sustaining 85%+ QA scores over 3 weeks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hitting contract-specific targets for 3 weeks</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leading your team.</strong> Once you've hit those benchmarks, you'll take on a team of 8–10 Enrollment Specialists, and learn:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The various data tools and tracking systems we use to measure performance and coach the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HR tools and processes for time-keeping and performance management.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. 3+ years of experience working in patient enrollment or similar field with a sales/conversion component, and a minimum of 2 years directly managing people.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with technology</strong>. Experience with Zoom, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, and comfort in learning new technology is important.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with data tools.</strong> Experience using data tools such as Google Sheets, Looker, or others in order to track performance metrics and ensure team performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator.</strong> You are winsome and articulate, but you always start by listening, and you hear what may not be voiced because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.</strong> You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metrics Focused.</strong> You can hit your daily, weekly, and monthly goals and frequently exceed them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A quiet working space</strong>. It's important you've worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment during your scheduled shifts and be able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A member-first approach.</strong> You're personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose</strong>. You're biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative's needs and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seek diverse perspectives</strong>. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You're always looking to learn and grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $72,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This role is also eligible for a quarterly performance-based bonus.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\nAs a Team Lead, you're the engine behind a high-performing enrollment team. You'll coach and develop a group of Enrollment Specialists, keep daily operations running smoothly, and drive the results that get patients connected to Thyme Care's program. This is a hands-on leadership role — you'll stay close to the work by doing direct patient outreach yourself, so you can lead from experience, not just from the sidelines.\n\n - Lead and develop your team. Your primary responsibility will be to coach a team of Enrollment Specialists to hit daily and weekly performance targets, running weekly team huddles and 1:1s to keep everyone trained, supported, and performing at their best.\n\n - Keep operations on track. You will also handle day-to-day HR tasks like approving timecards and PTO, and coach your team to follow processes seamlessly.\n\n - Drive continuous improvement. You will partner with other team leads to ensure the enrollment queues are working well, and will roll up your sleeves to fix issues when you see them. You will also surface opportunities to leadership to sharpen team scripts, workflows, and hand-offs, always with an eye toward improving enrollment conversion and achieving our team goals.\n\n - Stay close to members. You will continue to do direct patient outreach and enrollment a few hours each week so you stay sharp on best practices and can support your team from real, current experience.\n\nFirst Three Months of Training\n\nBefore stepping into full team management, you'll spend your first few weeks becoming an expert in the Enrollment Specialist role yourself — so you can coach others from a place of genuine knowledge.\n\n - Weeks 1–3: Onboarding. Complete virtual training and get up to speed on Thyme Care's systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations, as well as the ins and out of the Enrollment Specialist role so you can begin to do member outreach.\n\n - Weeks 4–12: Building Enrollment Proficiency. Learn and practice Thyme Care's enrollment methods — how to use our proprietary outreach tool, connect with members, explain our program's value, escalate urgent needs, obtain consents, and successfully enroll patients. You'll work in the Enrollment Specialist role until you've demonstrated consistent proficiency across:\n   \n   - Making 60–100 outbound calls per day\n   \n   - Sustaining 30%+ call conversion over 3 weeks\n   \n   - Sustaining 85%+ QA scores over 3 weeks\n   \n   - Hitting contract-specific targets for 3 weeks\n\n - Leading your team. Once you've hit those benchmarks, you'll take on a team of 8–10 Enrollment Specialists, and learn:\n   \n   - The various data tools and tracking systems we use to measure performance and coach the team.\n   \n   - HR tools and processes for time-keeping and performance management.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nExperience. 3+ years of experience working in patient enrollment or similar field with a sales/conversion component, and a minimum of 2 years directly managing people.\n\nComfort with technology. Experience with Zoom, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, and comfort in learning new technology is important.\n\nComfort with data tools. Experience using data tools such as Google Sheets, Looker, or others in order to track performance metrics and ensure team performance.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start by listening, and you hear what may not be voiced because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.\n\nMetrics Focused. You can hit your daily, weekly, and monthly goals and frequently exceed them.\n\nA quiet working space. It's important you've worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment during your scheduled shifts and be able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.\n\nA member-first approach. You're personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives.\n\nMove with purpose. You're biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative's needs and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nSeek diverse perspectives. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You're always looking to learn and grow.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $72,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This role is also eligible for a quarterly performance-based bonus.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"46a643a2-cb72-446f-b9b3-5251e76ce16b","title":"Senior Product Manager, Care Delivery","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-15T20:47:47.843+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/46a643a2-cb72-446f-b9b3-5251e76ce16b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/46a643a2-cb72-446f-b9b3-5251e76ce16b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>OUR MISSION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person's cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help our care team focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you're inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what's possible, we'd love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL DO</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a Senior Product Manager to drive the evolution of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/partners/thyme-box\"><u>Thyme Box</u></a> — the care management platform our care team lives in every day. Thyme Box is how our nurses, social workers, care partners, nurse practitioners, and medical directors do their work: how they prioritize who to outreach, access clinical information, communicate with members, document care, and move people through every intervention in their cancer journey. When Thyme Box is fast, clear, intuitive, and intelligent, our care team spends less time fighting software and more time caring for people. Getting this right is central to both our care model and our unit economics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role owns a mature, mission-critical product that is used by hundreds of care team members and is under constant demand. You will drive its continued transformation from a workflow tool into an AI-native platform. You'll balance a high volume of day-to-day requests, bugs, and stakeholder needs with a multi-quarter vision for how technology can meaningfully increase our care team's capacity, quality, and joy in their work. You'll partner closely with the Head of Product, Care Delivery, your tech lead, service designers, and a team of engineers to shape what gets built and why.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own a roadmap for Thyme Box:</strong> set the roadmap and drive execution across the core care team surfaces — work prioritization and routing, tasking and next best actions, communications, navigation and summarization of clinical information, and automated documentation — from discovery through rollout and adoption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Make the care team dramatically more efficient:</strong> identify where time and clicks are lost across workflows done hundreds of times a day, and ship the measurement, improvements, , and automations that move real productivity metrics and allow care team members to operate at the top of their licenses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead the AI-native evolution of care delivery:</strong> drive the strategy and delivery of AI-powered capabilities — supporting processes, automating documentation, and providing decision support — determining where AI can augment or automate human work while safeguarding clinical safety, trust, and quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ground every decision in the care team's reality:</strong> spend time with nurses, social workers, care partners, NPs, and medical directors; understand their workflows deeply; and translate messy clinical and operational processes into clean, extensible tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage competing priorities with clarity:</strong> field and triage requests from Care Delivery operations, clinical leadership, enrollment, and compliance (e.g., NCQA), and make transparent, defensible calls about what to build now, later, or never</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own quality and reliability:</strong> run bug triage and release coordination for a platform people depend on in real time, balancing stability with velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner across the org:</strong> work hand-in-hand with engineering, service design, clinical leadership, Care Delivery ops, data science, training, and quality to deliver workflows that actually stick and change behavior on the ground</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leverage AI to accelerate your own work:</strong> stay on the frontier of AI tooling and apply it to sharpen your discovery, specs, analysis, and prototyping</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an individual contributor role today, with the opportunity to build and lead a product team over time as the Care Delivery domain grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'VE DONE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of product management experience, with significant time owning complex, workflow-heavy software used by real operators</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare experience required, preferably in care delivery, digital health, or value-based care models where care delivery execution directly impacts clinical or financial outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of shipping efficiency and workflow improvements that moved measurable outcomes — not just features, but features that are broadly adopted and drive meaningful behavior change</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience translating ambiguous, cross-functional processes (clinical, operational, or otherwise) into clear product requirements engineering can build against</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage a high volume of competing requests and stakeholders while keeping a clear, defensible prioritization framework and building strong, trusting cross-functional relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating close to the technical details — data models, edge cases, automations, and the downstream impact of implementation decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong perspective, based on practical experience, about AI's potential to transform how work gets done — you're constantly tinkering with new AI tools and thinking about how they reshape what's possible for the people you serve</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication, with the ability to translate between technical and non-technical audiences in both directions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating in fast-moving, ambiguous environments where you defined the path forward</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to haves:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in oncology, serious illness / palliative care, or chronic condition management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience shipping AI/LLM-powered product features, including safety guardrails, evaluation, and quality measurement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operator empathy.</strong> You never lose sight of the person using the tool — a nurse mid-call with a scared patient, a care partner juggling a queue. You design for their real day, not an idealized workflow, and you earn their trust by making their work genuinely easier.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI exuberance grounded in craft.</strong> You're energized by what AI can do for care delivery. You're always tinkering, experimenting, and prototyping — while refining your perspective on what actually helps in a high-stakes clinical setting and what doesn't. You approach new technologies with curiosity and thoughtfulness.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ruthless prioritization.</strong> You face far more demand than capacity, and you're comfortable with that. You make transparent trade-offs, say no gracefully, and keep the team focused on the highest-leverage work — even under pressure from senior stakeholders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and operational range.</strong> You can set a multi-quarter vision for an AI-native platform and also dig deeply into a single confusing user flow or a nasty bug. You move fluidly between the two.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems thinking.</strong> You treat Thyme Box as a living system, not a pile of features. You care about consistency, extensibility, and technical debt, and you push back when a quick fix would create long-term disorder.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-functional glue.</strong> You bring clarity where there's confusion across engineering, service design, clinical, and ops. People turn to you when something touches many teams and needs to actually work — and you build trust across those boun</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">daries.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Humility and directness.</strong> You listen first and build consensus by default, but you can drive hard decisions when needed. You say what you'll do and do what you say.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>OUR VALUES</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $171,000-$190,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person's cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help our care team focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you're inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what's possible, we'd love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nWe're hiring a Senior Product Manager to drive the evolution of Thyme Box https://www.thymecare.com/partners/thyme-box — the care management platform our care team lives in every day. Thyme Box is how our nurses, social workers, care partners, nurse practitioners, and medical directors do their work: how they prioritize who to outreach, access clinical information, communicate with members, document care, and move people through every intervention in their cancer journey. When Thyme Box is fast, clear, intuitive, and intelligent, our care team spends less time fighting software and more time caring for people. Getting this right is central to both our care model and our unit economics.\n\nThis role owns a mature, mission-critical product that is used by hundreds of care team members and is under constant demand. You will drive its continued transformation from a workflow tool into an AI-native platform. You'll balance a high volume of day-to-day requests, bugs, and stakeholder needs with a multi-quarter vision for how technology can meaningfully increase our care team's capacity, quality, and joy in their work. You'll partner closely with the Head of Product, Care Delivery, your tech lead, service designers, and a team of engineers to shape what gets built and why.\n\nAdditionally, you will:\n\n - Own a roadmap for Thyme Box: set the roadmap and drive execution across the core care team surfaces — work prioritization and routing, tasking and next best actions, communications, navigation and summarization of clinical information, and automated documentation — from discovery through rollout and adoption\n\n - Make the care team dramatically more efficient: identify where time and clicks are lost across workflows done hundreds of times a day, and ship the measurement, improvements, , and automations that move real productivity metrics and allow care team members to operate at the top of their licenses\n\n - Lead the AI-native evolution of care delivery: drive the strategy and delivery of AI-powered capabilities — supporting processes, automating documentation, and providing decision support — determining where AI can augment or automate human work while safeguarding clinical safety, trust, and quality\n\n - Ground every decision in the care team's reality: spend time with nurses, social workers, care partners, NPs, and medical directors; understand their workflows deeply; and translate messy clinical and operational processes into clean, extensible tooling\n\n - Manage competing priorities with clarity: field and triage requests from Care Delivery operations, clinical leadership, enrollment, and compliance (e.g., NCQA), and make transparent, defensible calls about what to build now, later, or never\n\n - Own quality and reliability: run bug triage and release coordination for a platform people depend on in real time, balancing stability with velocity\n\n - Partner across the org: work hand-in-hand with engineering, service design, clinical leadership, Care Delivery ops, data science, training, and quality to deliver workflows that actually stick and change behavior on the ground\n\n - Leverage AI to accelerate your own work: stay on the frontier of AI tooling and apply it to sharpen your discovery, specs, analysis, and prototyping\n\nThis is an individual contributor role today, with the opportunity to build and lead a product team over time as the Care Delivery domain grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'VE DONE\n\n - 6+ years of product management experience, with significant time owning complex, workflow-heavy software used by real operators\n\n - Healthcare experience required, preferably in care delivery, digital health, or value-based care models where care delivery execution directly impacts clinical or financial outcomes\n\n - Track record of shipping efficiency and workflow improvements that moved measurable outcomes — not just features, but features that are broadly adopted and drive meaningful behavior change\n\n - Experience translating ambiguous, cross-functional processes (clinical, operational, or otherwise) into clear product requirements engineering can build against\n\n - Proven ability to manage a high volume of competing requests and stakeholders while keeping a clear, defensible prioritization framework and building strong, trusting cross-functional relationships\n\n - Comfort operating close to the technical details — data models, edge cases, automations, and the downstream impact of implementation decisions\n\n - A strong perspective, based on practical experience, about AI's potential to transform how work gets done — you're constantly tinkering with new AI tools and thinking about how they reshape what's possible for the people you serve\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication, with the ability to translate between technical and non-technical audiences in both directions\n\n - Experience operating in fast-moving, ambiguous environments where you defined the path forward\n\nNice to haves:\n\n - Experience in oncology, serious illness / palliative care, or chronic condition management\n\n - Hands-on experience shipping AI/LLM-powered product features, including safety guardrails, evaluation, and quality measurement\n\n\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nOperator empathy. You never lose sight of the person using the tool — a nurse mid-call with a scared patient, a care partner juggling a queue. You design for their real day, not an idealized workflow, and you earn their trust by making their work genuinely easier.\n\nAI exuberance grounded in craft. You're energized by what AI can do for care delivery. You're always tinkering, experimenting, and prototyping — while refining your perspective on what actually helps in a high-stakes clinical setting and what doesn't. You approach new technologies with curiosity and thoughtfulness.\n\nRuthless prioritization. You face far more demand than capacity, and you're comfortable with that. You make transparent trade-offs, say no gracefully, and keep the team focused on the highest-leverage work — even under pressure from senior stakeholders.\n\nStrategic and operational range. You can set a multi-quarter vision for an AI-native platform and also dig deeply into a single confusing user flow or a nasty bug. You move fluidly between the two.\n\nSystems thinking. You treat Thyme Box as a living system, not a pile of features. You care about consistency, extensibility, and technical debt, and you push back when a quick fix would create long-term disorder.\n\nCross-functional glue. You bring clarity where there's confusion across engineering, service design, clinical, and ops. People turn to you when something touches many teams and needs to actually work — and you build trust across those boun\n\ndaries.\n\nHumility and directness. You listen first and build consensus by default, but you can drive hard decisions when needed. You say what you'll do and do what you say.\n\n \n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $171,000-$190,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9ffb7265-c5cb-4b9f-a78e-2a23d2d742be","title":"Comprehensive Health Assessment Nurse Practitioner","department":"Member Experience","team":"NP","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T17:09:00.063+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/9ffb7265-c5cb-4b9f-a78e-2a23d2d742be","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/9ffb7265-c5cb-4b9f-a78e-2a23d2d742be/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Comprehensive Health Assessment Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical clinical team member caring for our members. You will conduct the first and annual clinical interaction with our members in this role. Using a telemedicine platform, this interaction will be a thorough, whole-person, comprehensive history and exam. You will evaluate risk scores and assess gaps in care.  You will develop comprehensive care plans to address clinical <u>and</u> non-clinical needs and barriers. You will prioritize our members’ goals and create concrete plans for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers to reach these goals. To do this, you will review available medical records, work with external providers, give clinical insights to our care team, and adhere to best documentation practices to drive high-quality care for our members.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to your primary responsibilities, you may be asked to participate in some holiday, night and weekend emergency coverage as needed. <strong>This role is for the following shifts: 11:30am-8pm or 2:30-11p Eastern Time.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-trocchia-dnp-fnp-bc-ocn-103671172/\"><u>Nurse Practitioner Manager</u></a> and can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Within your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be adept at developing evidence-based, member-centered care plans that will guide our Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators in effectively prioritizing our members' needs and goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete whole-person history and physical assessments for our members with the highest clinical rigor. You’re working fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become the go-to person for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health workers when working with a member with complex and intersecting needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable following policies, procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 3 years of NP experience, including 2 years in adult oncology and at least one year of telehealth experience. Experience completing health risk assessments is a plus! ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensure. </strong>You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted Advanced Practice license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized.</strong> You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify priorities and take action. </strong>You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent needs immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs the Comprehensive Health Assessment Nurse Practitioner, you will be a critical clinical team member caring for our members. You will conduct the first and annual clinical interaction with our members in this role. Using a telemedicine platform, this interaction will be a thorough, whole-person, comprehensive history and exam. You will evaluate risk scores and assess gaps in care.  You will develop comprehensive care plans to address clinical and non-clinical needs and barriers. You will prioritize our members’ goals and create concrete plans for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health Workers to reach these goals. To do this, you will review available medical records, work with external providers, give clinical insights to our care team, and adhere to best documentation practices to drive high-quality care for our members.\n\nIn addition to your primary responsibilities, you may be asked to participate in some holiday, night and weekend emergency coverage as needed. This role is for the following shifts: 11:30am-8pm or 2:30-11p Eastern Time.\n\nThis role reports to our Nurse Practitioner Manager https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-trocchia-dnp-fnp-bc-ocn-103671172/ and can be remote or hybrid-based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Complete training and be up to speed on Thyme Care’s systems, tools, technology, partners, and clinical expectations.\n\n - Be adept at developing evidence-based, member-centered care plans that will guide our Community Health Workers and Oncology Nurse Navigators in effectively prioritizing our members' needs and goals.\n\n - Complete whole-person history and physical assessments for our members with the highest clinical rigor. You’re working fluidly with our in-house care team and providers to ensure any identified needs are met in follow-up to patient visits.\n\n - Become the go-to person for our Oncology Nurse Navigators and Community Health workers when working with a member with complex and intersecting needs.\n\n - Be comfortable following policies, procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\nExperience. You have at least 3 years of NP experience, including 2 years in adult oncology and at least one year of telehealth experience. Experience completing health risk assessments is a plus!  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company.\n\nLicensure. You have a compact RN license, an unrestricted Advanced Practice license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses.\n\nOrganized. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course… and part of the adventure.\n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs and do what it takes to address urgent needs immediately.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3735b256-ad00-4a3b-bc5f-ddab0b0747d4","title":"Senior Product Manager, Data Ingestion & Care Enablement","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T15:56:16.161+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/3735b256-ad00-4a3b-bc5f-ddab0b0747d4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/3735b256-ad00-4a3b-bc5f-ddab0b0747d4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>OUR MISSION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.<br /></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL DO</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Product Manager on our Data Ingestion &amp; Care Enablement (DICE) team, you will be the connective tissue between our external partners, internal data systems, and the product and care teams that depend on them. You'll own the data integrations and partner relationships that power Thyme Care's ability to identify, enroll, and serve our members — making sure the right data flows to the right teams at the right time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role sits at the intersection of contracts, data, product behavior, and care workflows. You'll partner closely with payer and provider organizations to acquire and exchange data, define program populations, and ensure our integrations meet both contractual and clinical requirements. Internally, you'll work across our data science, engineering, growth, health economics, and clinical operations teams to translate complex data problems into clear requirements and actionable plans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own partner data integrations end-to-end:</strong> lead implementations with payers and providers, managing data ingestion, quality, enrollment logic, and return files from kickoff through go-live and ongoing operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Serve as a primary point of contact for external data counterparts:</strong> negotiate data specifications, troubleshoot issues, and build strong working relationships with partner organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Translate technical complexity into business clarity:</strong> break down intricate data and integration challenges into actionable requirements that product, engineering, and data science teams can execute against</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional alignment:</strong> coordinate across DICE, growth, health economics, clinical operations, and care delivery teams to ensure data-dependent initiatives stay on track</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and maintain operational visibility:</strong> develop monitoring, dashboards, and proactive alerting so the team can shift from reactive problem-solving to proactive management of data quality and integration health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own analyses that drive decisions:</strong> lead work on eligibility reconciliation, claims analysis, enrollment trends, and other data investigations that inform executive and operational decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape the DICE roadmap:</strong> partner with your team lead to identify opportunities, prioritize initiatives, and drive multi-quarter projects that improve how Thyme Care acquires, processes, and leverages data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leverage AI to accelerate your work:</strong> stay current with AI tools and capabilities, applying them where they can improve your own productivity and the effectiveness of data workflows</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'VE DONE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in product management, data operations, or a related role within healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience working with healthcare claims data, eligibility files, and value-based care data in a payer, provider, or health tech environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of managing complex data integrations or implementations with external partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience collaborating closely with data science and data engineering teams; comfortable with SQL and working in data-heavy environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to manage competing priorities across multiple partners and internal stakeholders simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate technical concepts for non-technical audiences and vice versa</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating effectively in ambiguous, fast-moving environments where you had to define the path forward</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to haves:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with clinical ontologies or healthcare data standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data pipeline tools and concepts (e.g., dbt, GitHub Actions) — not as a builder, but as a collaborator</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in value-based care contract operations or performance measurement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in health economics, actuarial, or clinical data analysis</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Self-starter mentality.</strong> You don't wait for someone to hand you a problem statement. You see gaps, ask questions, and move toward solutions — even when the path isn't fully defined.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relentless curiosity.</strong> You dig into the data, the contracts, and the workflows until you truly understand how things work. You ask \"why\" repeatedly and aren't satisfied with surface-level answers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-functional glue.</strong> You bring clarity where there's confusion. You're the person teams turn to when something touches multiple systems, partners, or stakeholders and needs to actually work. You build trust across organizational boundaries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner management instincts.</strong> You're comfortable as the face of Thyme Care to external data counterparts. You can navigate competing priorities, negotiate gracefully, and maintain strong relationships through complex implementations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organized under pressure.</strong> You juggle multiple partner launches, data issues, and internal requests without dropping balls. Your documentation and communication keep everyone aligned.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with data.</strong> You can open a dataset, spot anomalies, write queries to investigate, and collaborate fluently with data scientists and engineers — even if you're not building pipelines yourself.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Humility and directness.</strong> You listen first and build consensus by default, but you can drive hard decisions when needed. You say what you'll do and do what you say.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>OUR VALUES</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $171,000-$190,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Product Manager on our Data Ingestion & Care Enablement (DICE) team, you will be the connective tissue between our external partners, internal data systems, and the product and care teams that depend on them. You'll own the data integrations and partner relationships that power Thyme Care's ability to identify, enroll, and serve our members — making sure the right data flows to the right teams at the right time.\n\n\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of contracts, data, product behavior, and care workflows. You'll partner closely with payer and provider organizations to acquire and exchange data, define program populations, and ensure our integrations meet both contractual and clinical requirements. Internally, you'll work across our data science, engineering, growth, health economics, and clinical operations teams to translate complex data problems into clear requirements and actionable plans.\n\nAdditionally, you will:\n\n - Own partner data integrations end-to-end: lead implementations with payers and providers, managing data ingestion, quality, enrollment logic, and return files from kickoff through go-live and ongoing operations\n\n - Serve as a primary point of contact for external data counterparts: negotiate data specifications, troubleshoot issues, and build strong working relationships with partner organizations\n\n - Translate technical complexity into business clarity: break down intricate data and integration challenges into actionable requirements that product, engineering, and data science teams can execute against\n\n - Drive cross-functional alignment: coordinate across DICE, growth, health economics, clinical operations, and care delivery teams to ensure data-dependent initiatives stay on track\n\n - Build and maintain operational visibility: develop monitoring, dashboards, and proactive alerting so the team can shift from reactive problem-solving to proactive management of data quality and integration health\n\n - Own analyses that drive decisions: lead work on eligibility reconciliation, claims analysis, enrollment trends, and other data investigations that inform executive and operational decision-making\n\n - Shape the DICE roadmap: partner with your team lead to identify opportunities, prioritize initiatives, and drive multi-quarter projects that improve how Thyme Care acquires, processes, and leverages data\n\n - Leverage AI to accelerate your work: stay current with AI tools and capabilities, applying them where they can improve your own productivity and the effectiveness of data workflows\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'VE DONE\n\n - 4+ years of experience in product management, data operations, or a related role within healthcare\n\n - Direct experience working with healthcare claims data, eligibility files, and value-based care data in a payer, provider, or health tech environment\n\n - Track record of managing complex data integrations or implementations with external partners\n\n - Experience collaborating closely with data science and data engineering teams; comfortable with SQL and working in data-heavy environments\n\n - Proven ability to manage competing priorities across multiple partners and internal stakeholders simultaneously\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate technical concepts for non-technical audiences and vice versa\n\n - Experience operating effectively in ambiguous, fast-moving environments where you had to define the path forward\n\nNice to haves:\n\n - Experience with clinical ontologies or healthcare data standards\n\n - Familiarity with data pipeline tools and concepts (e.g., dbt, GitHub Actions) — not as a builder, but as a collaborator\n\n - Experience in value-based care contract operations or performance measurement\n\n - Background in health economics, actuarial, or clinical data analysis\n\n\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Self-starter mentality. You don't wait for someone to hand you a problem statement. You see gaps, ask questions, and move toward solutions — even when the path isn't fully defined.\n\n - Relentless curiosity. You dig into the data, the contracts, and the workflows until you truly understand how things work. You ask \"why\" repeatedly and aren't satisfied with surface-level answers.\n\n - Cross-functional glue. You bring clarity where there's confusion. You're the person teams turn to when something touches multiple systems, partners, or stakeholders and needs to actually work. You build trust across organizational boundaries.\n\n - Partner management instincts. You're comfortable as the face of Thyme Care to external data counterparts. You can navigate competing priorities, negotiate gracefully, and maintain strong relationships through complex implementations.\n\n - Organized under pressure. You juggle multiple partner launches, data issues, and internal requests without dropping balls. Your documentation and communication keep everyone aligned.\n\n - Comfort with data. You can open a dataset, spot anomalies, write queries to investigate, and collaborate fluently with data scientists and engineers — even if you're not building pipelines yourself.\n\n - Humility and directness. You listen first and build consensus by default, but you can drive hard decisions when needed. You say what you'll do and do what you say.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $171,000-$190,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"35e11a74-3730-4a5e-b902-d9fe1803627f","title":"Sr. Manager, CRM & Lifecycle Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-17T14:39:34.064+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/35e11a74-3730-4a5e-b902-d9fe1803627f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/35e11a74-3730-4a5e-b902-d9fe1803627f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Your role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the <strong>Senior Manager, CRM &amp; Lifecycle Marketing</strong>, you’ll be part of Thyme Care’s member marketing team, which leads the strategy, execution, and optimization of asynchronous member communications across the care journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care partners with health plans to support their members through cancer care, and that model shapes the work. Each enrollment campaign is customized per health plan partner, and on the engagement side, programs are built around specific care behaviors, each with its own messaging, timing, and audience logic. It's a high-volume, high-customization environment, and the craft of this role is honoring what makes each partner and program distinct while building the reusable logic that keeps the system scalable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own the execution, optimization, and ongoing management of lifecycle marketing programs spanning member awareness, enrollment, activation, onboarding, engagement, and retention. Working primarily in <strong>Customer.io</strong>, you'll be the expert on how campaigns get built: how audience logic is structured, how personalization renders, how data attributes flow into messages, and whether a concept is feasible before work begins. You'll design, build, QA, and maintain cross-channel campaigns (email, SMS, direct mail) that are accurate, personalized, and delivered seamlessly. Consulted directly as campaigns are scoped, you'll partner closely with Enrollment Marketing, Member Engagement Marketing, Brand, Product, Engineering, and Data to define data requirements, monitor performance, and translate lifecycle strategies into personalized, scalable member experiences built on reusable logic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving complex marketing and technical challenges as much as creating exceptional member experiences. You’ll combine strong marketing instincts with systems thinking to build communications that are timely, empathetic, data-driven, and scalable.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and manage CRM journeys:</strong> Develop and maintain a high-volume portfolio of automated campaigns in <strong>Customer.io</strong> (or similar tools like Iterable or Braze) that drive awareness, enrollment, engagement, and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage data flow and integrations:</strong> Partner with engineering and data teams to optimize how member data moves between proprietary systems and marketing platforms, ensuring reliability and personalization at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design scalable campaign architecture:</strong> Create workflows and automations across channels (email, SMS, print, and landing pages) with a focus on compliance, brand alignment, and QA.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead testing and reporting:</strong> Define, run, and evaluate A/B tests; use Looker and other analytics tools to measure campaign performance, identify opportunities, and deliver actionable insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support co-branded initiatives:</strong> Execute marketing programs with payer and provider partners, maintaining strong collaboration and brand integrity across all audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Establish operational excellence:</strong> Maintain CRM hygiene, manage segmentation and audience lists, and create documentation and standards for campaign deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate cross-functionally:</strong> Work with internal partners across Enrollment, Brand, and Member Engagement to translate strategic goals into technical execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Champion the member experience:</strong> Reduce friction in communications by simplifying journeys, clarifying messaging, and ensuring members receive timely, supportive information.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in CRM or lifecycle marketing, with a strong focus on marketing automation and data-driven campaign management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with <strong>Customer.io</strong>, Iterable, Braze, or similar CRM platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of HTML, dynamic content, and data integrations via APIs or data pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort collaborating closely with engineering and data partners to solve technical challenges.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing complex, multi-channel programs with high attention to detail and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical mindset with proficiency in performance reporting (e.g., Looker or similar BI tools).</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What leads to success</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission, and in particular, our member experience, matters deeply to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose.</strong> You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on purposefully.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator</strong>. Must be an articulate professional with excellent oral and written communication skills, with demonstrated experience in the ability to positively and creatively influence change and direction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong>. You have experience in lifestyle marketing and healthcare. You’ve demonstrated the ability to develop impactful campaigns that engage and resonate with patients and providers. You’re an adept project manager; you stay organized even as priorities change quickly. You also earned a Bachelor’s degree in a related field.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with pace and ambiguity</strong>. You have experience with scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Beginning with the end in mind</strong>. You are highly analytical. You can dive into member demographics and provider referral pathways to drive enrollment and use those insights to drive growth and results. You can translate research and insights into actionable marketing plans.</p><h2><br /><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,250-$165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n \n\n\nYOUR ROLE\n\nAs the Senior Manager, CRM & Lifecycle Marketing, you’ll be part of Thyme Care’s member marketing team, which leads the strategy, execution, and optimization of asynchronous member communications across the care journey.\n\nThyme Care partners with health plans to support their members through cancer care, and that model shapes the work. Each enrollment campaign is customized per health plan partner, and on the engagement side, programs are built around specific care behaviors, each with its own messaging, timing, and audience logic. It's a high-volume, high-customization environment, and the craft of this role is honoring what makes each partner and program distinct while building the reusable logic that keeps the system scalable.\n\nYou'll own the execution, optimization, and ongoing management of lifecycle marketing programs spanning member awareness, enrollment, activation, onboarding, engagement, and retention. Working primarily in Customer.io, you'll be the expert on how campaigns get built: how audience logic is structured, how personalization renders, how data attributes flow into messages, and whether a concept is feasible before work begins. You'll design, build, QA, and maintain cross-channel campaigns (email, SMS, direct mail) that are accurate, personalized, and delivered seamlessly. Consulted directly as campaigns are scoped, you'll partner closely with Enrollment Marketing, Member Engagement Marketing, Brand, Product, Engineering, and Data to define data requirements, monitor performance, and translate lifecycle strategies into personalized, scalable member experiences built on reusable logic.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving complex marketing and technical challenges as much as creating exceptional member experiences. You’ll combine strong marketing instincts with systems thinking to build communications that are timely, empathetic, data-driven, and scalable.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build and manage CRM journeys: Develop and maintain a high-volume portfolio of automated campaigns in Customer.io (or similar tools like Iterable or Braze) that drive awareness, enrollment, engagement, and retention.\n\n - Manage data flow and integrations: Partner with engineering and data teams to optimize how member data moves between proprietary systems and marketing platforms, ensuring reliability and personalization at scale.\n\n - Design scalable campaign architecture: Create workflows and automations across channels (email, SMS, print, and landing pages) with a focus on compliance, brand alignment, and QA.\n\n - Lead testing and reporting: Define, run, and evaluate A/B tests; use Looker and other analytics tools to measure campaign performance, identify opportunities, and deliver actionable insights.\n\n - Support co-branded initiatives: Execute marketing programs with payer and provider partners, maintaining strong collaboration and brand integrity across all audiences.\n\n - Establish operational excellence: Maintain CRM hygiene, manage segmentation and audience lists, and create documentation and standards for campaign deployment.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally: Work with internal partners across Enrollment, Brand, and Member Engagement to translate strategic goals into technical execution.\n\n - Champion the member experience: Reduce friction in communications by simplifying journeys, clarifying messaging, and ensuring members receive timely, supportive information.\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 6+ years of experience in CRM or lifecycle marketing, with a strong focus on marketing automation and data-driven campaign management.\n\n - Deep familiarity with Customer.io, Iterable, Braze, or similar CRM platforms.\n\n - Working knowledge of HTML, dynamic content, and data integrations via APIs or data pipelines.\n\n - Comfort collaborating closely with engineering and data partners to solve technical challenges.\n\n - Experience managing complex, multi-channel programs with high attention to detail and documentation.\n\n - Analytical mindset with proficiency in performance reporting (e.g., Looker or similar BI tools).\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. Thyme Care’s mission, and in particular, our member experience, matters deeply to you.\n\nMove with purpose. You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on purposefully.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. Must be an articulate professional with excellent oral and written communication skills, with demonstrated experience in the ability to positively and creatively influence change and direction.\n\nExperience. You have experience in lifestyle marketing and healthcare. You’ve demonstrated the ability to develop impactful campaigns that engage and resonate with patients and providers. You’re an adept project manager; you stay organized even as priorities change quickly. You also earned a Bachelor’s degree in a related field.\n\nComfort with pace and ambiguity. You have experience with scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.\n\nBeginning with the end in mind. You are highly analytical. You can dive into member demographics and provider referral pathways to drive enrollment and use those insights to drive growth and results. You can translate research and insights into actionable marketing plans.\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,250-$165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6574ed3a-0710-4fab-9b77-e0daeaca5c1f","title":"Oncology Nurse Navigator (Saturday + 4 Weekdays Shift)","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T13:23:58.302+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/6574ed3a-0710-4fab-9b77-e0daeaca5c1f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/6574ed3a-0710-4fab-9b77-e0daeaca5c1f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, offering triage, support, and education during their cancer journey via phone, email, and video communication. Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will involve actively engaging with members, addressing clinical issues, and efficiently managing any escalations that arise.<strong> </strong><em><strong>This role follows a fixed schedule of 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM EST, working four weekdays and Saturdays. The designated weekday off must be Monday, Thursday, or Friday.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Within your first three months, you will:</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and address member needs promptly, offering assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Performs other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Member-Centric Approach: </strong>You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented:</strong> You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills:</strong> You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong> An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. <strong>Compact + single state licensure in New York and/or Illinois licensure is preferred. </strong>Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications: </strong>Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is <em>$41.54/hour.</em> <em>To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. </em>We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Be cautious of </strong></em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em><strong>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</strong><br /></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE\n\nThyme Care Inc., the management company to Thyme Care Medical PLLC, is the employing entity with your duties to be performed for Thyme Care Medical PLLC, a medical practice, and its patients. As a Thyme Care Oncology Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members and their care network, offering triage, support, and education during their cancer journey via phone, email, and video communication. Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive clinical assessments, oversee member health, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions. Your main objective will involve actively engaging with members, addressing clinical issues, and efficiently managing any escalations that arise. This role follows a fixed schedule of 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM EST, working four weekdays and Saturdays. The designated weekday off must be Monday, Thursday, or Friday.\n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners, conducting a minimum of 20 member calls per day.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.\n\n - Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.\n\n - Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.\n\n - Support members throughout the oncology care continuum, from screening to survivorship or end-of-life care, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.\n\n - Identify and address member needs promptly, offering assistance with care coordination, symptom management, nutritional support, discharge planning, and provider referrals.\n\n - Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.\n\n - Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.\n\n - Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required.\n\nPerforms other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Member-Centric Approach: You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.\n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - Qualifications: An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. Compact + single state licensure in New York and/or Illinois licensure is preferred. Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in solid tumor oncology nursing. \n\n - Certifications: Oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM) are required or obtained within 2 years of hire. \n\nThis job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications.   Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $41.54/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.\n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate. \n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"20483de1-db58-48e0-a0c3-c9df22a55f00","title":"Oncology Nurse Team Lead","department":"Member Experience","team":"Team Leads & Leadership - Clinical","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T19:40:32.668+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/20483de1-db58-48e0-a0c3-c9df22a55f00","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/20483de1-db58-48e0-a0c3-c9df22a55f00/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Oncology Nurse Team Lead, you will oversee and manage one or more of our frontline nurse teams, ensuring their ability to deliver the highest standards of clinical care and operational efficiency as they advocate, coach, and provide members with clinical guidance throughout their care journey.  Reporting to the Nurse Manager, you will manage clinical escalations, provide ongoing training, coaching, and mentoring to your teams, drive the productivity and performance of your team, and foster cross-team collaboration.  This role is pivotal in driving individual and team performance, identifying opportunities for quality improvement initiatives and enhancing Thyme Care’s service offerings by effectively communicating feedback to our clinical leadership from members, providers, and your teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To excel in this role, you must demonstrate strong leadership and mentorship capabilities, with a proven track record of managing hourly staff and high-performing nurse teams. You are a proactive problem solver who views challenges as opportunities for growth and is committed to continuous improvement. Experience in healthcare, particularly in oncology, as a nurse navigator or case manager is essential. Knowledge and an understanding of provider and health plan operations are also beneficial.  </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>After your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed Nurse training and demonstrated competencies in a Nurse role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Know our Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards backward and forward, and actively share ideas on improving them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be on the path to becoming an expert on our Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Directly manage and serve as an escalation point to a team of Oncology Nurses, including but not limited to escalated member or caregiver interactions and process-related questions or issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your team and leadership, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead team meetings such as weekly team huddles to drive queue management, prioritization, and performance, and ultimately establish targeted support plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as an air traffic controller by monitoring assignments and ensuring queues are effectively and efficiently managed. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the performance of your direct team members, both quality and productivity and address issues and challenges through coaching, mentorship, and performance improvement plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the skills, qualities, and experience that set a candidate up for success and participate in the oncology nurse interview loop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support our nurses in identifying and prioritizing member needs and assisting them with care coordination and clinical support such as symptom management, nutritional support, discharge coordination, connecting members to high-quality providers, and preventing readmissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide clinical expertise in medical, behavioral, and crisis management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide support on building and maintaining resources, optimizing schedules, and contributing to updating staffing requirements, project initiatives, and policies and procedures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide support in conducting root-cause analyses to identify knowledge, data, or procedure gaps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive engagement and promote the Thyme Care vision and strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide Nurse overflow, holiday, and on-call coverage support as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop strategies to promote culturally competent care and close the health literacy gap.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.<br /><strong>A BSN. </strong>You must have a Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN preferred), a multi-state, unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) compact license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses, as needed.<br /></em><strong>Experience</strong>. You have at least 8 years of nursing experience, with 2 years as a people manager in oncology and/or case management. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).<br /><strong>Team player.</strong> You’re a strong collaborator who understands what it's like to lead a team in a growing and evolving environment. You’ll ensure your team meets and exceeds the standards set while collaborating with the rest of the organization.<br /><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with your team, leadership, and stakeholders.<br /><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.</strong> You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course… and part of the adventure. <br /><strong>Coach</strong>. You know your team’s strengths and what motivates them, and you strive to keep morale high while constantly challenging them to beat their best and never lose sight of the goal.<br /><strong>Grit</strong>. You’re never afraid to get your hands dirty, but you can also take a step back and connect the company’s strategy to your team’s performance and execution.<br /><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies. </strong>We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in learning new technology is essential.<br /><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong> You know how to identify and prioritize your team’s needs and do what it takes to address urgent and essential needs immediately.<br /><strong>Bias to action</strong>. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $103,500. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs an Oncology Nurse Team Lead, you will oversee and manage one or more of our frontline nurse teams, ensuring their ability to deliver the highest standards of clinical care and operational efficiency as they advocate, coach, and provide members with clinical guidance throughout their care journey.  Reporting to the Nurse Manager, you will manage clinical escalations, provide ongoing training, coaching, and mentoring to your teams, drive the productivity and performance of your team, and foster cross-team collaboration.  This role is pivotal in driving individual and team performance, identifying opportunities for quality improvement initiatives and enhancing Thyme Care’s service offerings by effectively communicating feedback to our clinical leadership from members, providers, and your teams.\n\nTo excel in this role, you must demonstrate strong leadership and mentorship capabilities, with a proven track record of managing hourly staff and high-performing nurse teams. You are a proactive problem solver who views challenges as opportunities for growth and is committed to continuous improvement. Experience in healthcare, particularly in oncology, as a nurse navigator or case manager is essential. Knowledge and an understanding of provider and health plan operations are also beneficial.  \n\nAfter your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed Nurse training and demonstrated competencies in a Nurse role.\n\n - Know our Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards backward and forward, and actively share ideas on improving them.\n\n - Be on the path to becoming an expert on our Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations.\n\n - Directly manage and serve as an escalation point to a team of Oncology Nurses, including but not limited to escalated member or caregiver interactions and process-related questions or issues.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your team and leadership, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. \n\n - Lead team meetings such as weekly team huddles to drive queue management, prioritization, and performance, and ultimately establish targeted support plans.\n\n - Act as an air traffic controller by monitoring assignments and ensuring queues are effectively and efficiently managed. \n\n - Understand the performance of your direct team members, both quality and productivity and address issues and challenges through coaching, mentorship, and performance improvement plans.\n\n - Understand the skills, qualities, and experience that set a candidate up for success and participate in the oncology nurse interview loop.\n\n - Support our nurses in identifying and prioritizing member needs and assisting them with care coordination and clinical support such as symptom management, nutritional support, discharge coordination, connecting members to high-quality providers, and preventing readmissions.\n\n - Provide clinical expertise in medical, behavioral, and crisis management.\n\n - Provide support on building and maintaining resources, optimizing schedules, and contributing to updating staffing requirements, project initiatives, and policies and procedures.\n\n - Provide support in conducting root-cause analyses to identify knowledge, data, or procedure gaps.\n\n - Drive engagement and promote the Thyme Care vision and strategy.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and clinical consult support. \n\n - Provide Nurse overflow, holiday, and on-call coverage support as needed.\n\n - Develop strategies to promote culturally competent care and close the health literacy gap.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\nA BSN. You must have a Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN preferred), a multi-state, unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) compact license, and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses, as needed.\nExperience. You have at least 8 years of nursing experience, with 2 years as a people manager in oncology and/or case management. Additionally, you are certified as an Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).\nTeam player. You’re a strong collaborator who understands what it's like to lead a team in a growing and evolving environment. You’ll ensure your team meets and exceeds the standards set while collaborating with the rest of the organization.\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and hearing what may not be voiced because you listen intently to others. You build rapport and excellent working relationships with your team, leadership, and stakeholders.\nComfort with ambiguity. You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course… and part of the adventure. \nCoach. You know your team’s strengths and what motivates them, and you strive to keep morale high while constantly challenging them to beat their best and never lose sight of the goal.\nGrit. You’re never afraid to get your hands dirty, but you can also take a step back and connect the company’s strategy to your team’s performance and execution.\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort in learning new technology is essential.\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize your team’s needs and do what it takes to address urgent and essential needs immediately.\nBias to action. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $103,500. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a0b0234d-1855-4d32-aad2-8fb0166feea3","title":"Enrollment Specialist Manager","department":"Member Experience","team":"Team Leads & Leadership - ES","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T16:58:44.663+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/a0b0234d-1855-4d32-aad2-8fb0166feea3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/a0b0234d-1855-4d32-aad2-8fb0166feea3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>THE ROLE<br /></strong>We're seeking a dynamic Enrollment Specialist Manager to lead our growing Enrollment team. The Enrollment team is responsible for outreaching and enrolling prospective new members. Our Enrollment Specialists outreach prospective members to educate them on our services and encourage them to enroll in Thyme Care to receive free-of-cost support throughout their cancer journey. As the Enrollment Specialist Manager, you’ll report directly to the Head of Enrollment Strategy and will oversee a team of Enrollment Specialist Team Leads while driving operational excellence, training effectiveness, and strategic initiatives to meet our enrollment goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Lead Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Directly manage, coach, and develop 3-5 Enrollment Specialist Team Leads</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be directly accountable for the performance of 30-50 Enrollment Specialists</strong> supervised by Team Leads, including enrollment volume, conversion, and quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work closely with Team Leads on performance management</strong> and career development conversations with Enrollment Specialists to build and maintain high-performing culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build effective communication channels</strong> to ensure Team Leads are appropriately informed and aligned, and that they can surface insights and challenges from their teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and maintain strong team culture</strong> grounded in Thyme Care values</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operations &amp; Workflows</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Intimately understand enrollment team workflows and systems</strong> to be able to answer team questions, edge case scenarios, and member escalations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Closely monitor enrollment team “queue”</strong> to identify and resolve data and system issues, ensure proper outreach prioritization, and resolve operational bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Monitor team performance</strong> to ensure appropriate workflows are being followed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Revamp workflows as needed to drive improvements in efficiency and throughput</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement new workflows in collaboration with cross-functional partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead change management </strong>processes and<strong> </strong>build<strong> </strong>clear communication protocols for workflow changes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training &amp; Enablement</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with the Quality, Training &amp; Enablement</strong> team to identify skill gaps, create continuous feedback loops between QA findings and training, and reinforce training</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ensure new hires are effectively trained</strong> prior to going live, monitor performance closely, and support coaching during their first 90 days to ensure a quick and effective ramp</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ensure training materials and job aids are up to date</strong> and meet operational needs</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategy &amp; Innovation</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Analyze performance data</strong> to identify opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead testing and piloting</strong> of new approaches to improve member enrollment rates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adapt strategies</strong> in response to evolving member needs and market conditions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHY YOU’LL LOVE THIS ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This position offers a unique opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the lives of patients with cancer while supporting a critical function within our organization. You'll have the chance to shape our enrollment strategy, develop future leaders, and directly contribute to our mission of providing exceptional support throughout the cancer journey. If you're passionate about building high-performing teams and driving operational excellence in service of a powerful mission, we want to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong management experience.</strong> You have significant experience managing and coaching teams toward success, and ideally have managed managers in addition to individual contributors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational orientation. </strong>You have successfully built, improved, and maintained effective operational processes and documentation, with a bias for simplicity and efficacy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-functional leadership</strong>. You are able to drive cross-functional initiatives through effective influencing, project management, and communication.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity</strong>. You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data savvy</strong>. You leverage data and analytics to measure success, find opportunities for improvement, and inform decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Excellent communication skills. </strong>You have excellent written and verbal communication skills, whether facilitating a live training session or presenting results to leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $103,500 - $115,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nTHE ROLE\nWe're seeking a dynamic Enrollment Specialist Manager to lead our growing Enrollment team. The Enrollment team is responsible for outreaching and enrolling prospective new members. Our Enrollment Specialists outreach prospective members to educate them on our services and encourage them to enroll in Thyme Care to receive free-of-cost support throughout their cancer journey. As the Enrollment Specialist Manager, you’ll report directly to the Head of Enrollment Strategy and will oversee a team of Enrollment Specialist Team Leads while driving operational excellence, training effectiveness, and strategic initiatives to meet our enrollment goals.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nTeam Lead Management\n\n - Directly manage, coach, and develop 3-5 Enrollment Specialist Team Leads\n\n - Be directly accountable for the performance of 30-50 Enrollment Specialists supervised by Team Leads, including enrollment volume, conversion, and quality\n\n - Work closely with Team Leads on performance management and career development conversations with Enrollment Specialists to build and maintain high-performing culture\n\n - Build effective communication channels to ensure Team Leads are appropriately informed and aligned, and that they can surface insights and challenges from their teams\n\n - Build and maintain strong team culture grounded in Thyme Care values\n\nOperations & Workflows\n\n - Intimately understand enrollment team workflows and systems to be able to answer team questions, edge case scenarios, and member escalations\n\n - Closely monitor enrollment team “queue” to identify and resolve data and system issues, ensure proper outreach prioritization, and resolve operational bottlenecks\n\n - Monitor team performance to ensure appropriate workflows are being followed\n\n - Revamp workflows as needed to drive improvements in efficiency and throughput\n\n - Design and implement new workflows in collaboration with cross-functional partners\n\n - Lead change management processes and build clear communication protocols for workflow changes\n\nTraining & Enablement\n\n - Partner with the Quality, Training & Enablement team to identify skill gaps, create continuous feedback loops between QA findings and training, and reinforce training\n\n - Ensure new hires are effectively trained prior to going live, monitor performance closely, and support coaching during their first 90 days to ensure a quick and effective ramp\n\n - Ensure training materials and job aids are up to date and meet operational needs\n\nStrategy & Innovation\n\n - Analyze performance data to identify opportunities for improvement\n\n - Lead testing and piloting of new approaches to improve member enrollment rates\n\n - Adapt strategies in response to evolving member needs and market conditions\n\nWHY YOU’LL LOVE THIS ROLE\n\nThis position offers a unique opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the lives of patients with cancer while supporting a critical function within our organization. You'll have the chance to shape our enrollment strategy, develop future leaders, and directly contribute to our mission of providing exceptional support throughout the cancer journey. If you're passionate about building high-performing teams and driving operational excellence in service of a powerful mission, we want to hear from you.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nStrong management experience. You have significant experience managing and coaching teams toward success, and ideally have managed managers in addition to individual contributors.\n\nOperational orientation. You have successfully built, improved, and maintained effective operational processes and documentation, with a bias for simplicity and efficacy.\n\nCross-functional leadership. You are able to drive cross-functional initiatives through effective influencing, project management, and communication.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.\n\nData savvy. You leverage data and analytics to measure success, find opportunities for improvement, and inform decisions.\n\nExcellent communication skills. You have excellent written and verbal communication skills, whether facilitating a live training session or presenting results to leadership.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $103,500 - $115,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n\n ","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"95c7dd65-826a-4264-8f03-600d0e67bd69","title":"Practice Coordinator","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T19:48:35.315+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/95c7dd65-826a-4264-8f03-600d0e67bd69","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/95c7dd65-826a-4264-8f03-600d0e67bd69/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Practice Coordinator, you will play a crucial role in supporting our healthcare providers by delivering seamless remote administrative and patient care coordination. Your efforts will ensure efficient telehealth visits, enhance patient experience, and contribute to the overall success of our virtual care operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">  Scheduling &amp; Patient Coordination:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule, reschedule, and confirm (virtual) patient appointments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage provider calendars and resolve scheduling conflicts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">  Telehealth Support:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Initiate and troubleshoot telehealth visits for patients and providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide patients through virtual check-in and technology setup.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">  Administrative Duties:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect member consents for virtual appointments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify insurance benefits and collect copays/deductibles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process and send clinical notes, referrals, and consents to providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate electronic health records (EHR) and patient data.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">  Provider Support (Non-Clinical Tasks):</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist NPs/MDs with documentation, forms, and prescription requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure HIPAA compliance during virtual interactions and data handling.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual (Spanish) preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in administrative roles, virtual assistance, or telehealth support preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oncology experience preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational, multitasking, and communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with EHR systems, telehealth platforms, and basic technical troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compassionate, patient-centric approach with a commitment to high-quality care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a fast-paced remote environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After your first three months, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed training and be up to speed on Thyme Care tools, processes, and expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable with and correctly follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generate daily member reports and assist with day-to-day functions to help prepare our healthcare provider team for consultations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide inbound telephonic, text, fax, and email support for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be able to identify and triage a member's needs to connect them with our Care Teams for clinical support and care coordination.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule patient and provider visits.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to special projects or data entry, including the growth of our virtual medical practice and stop-gap process execution.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>People-first.</strong> Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Organized.</strong> You bring structure to chaos. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.</strong> Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies</strong>. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Identify priorities and take action.</strong> You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are addressed immediately.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Culture carrier.</strong> You’re curious, resilient, have a growth mindset, and are committed to fostering a positive environment.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $21/hour. <em>To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHI. </em>We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be cautious of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Thyme Care Practice Coordinator, you will play a crucial role in supporting our healthcare providers by delivering seamless remote administrative and patient care coordination. Your efforts will ensure efficient telehealth visits, enhance patient experience, and contribute to the overall success of our virtual care operations.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n  Scheduling & Patient Coordination:\n\n - Schedule, reschedule, and confirm (virtual) patient appointments.\n\n - Manage provider calendars and resolve scheduling conflicts.\n\n  Telehealth Support:\n\n - Initiate and troubleshoot telehealth visits for patients and providers.\n\n - Guide patients through virtual check-in and technology setup.\n\n  Administrative Duties:\n\n - Collect member consents for virtual appointments.\n\n - Verify insurance benefits and collect copays/deductibles.\n\n - Process and send clinical notes, referrals, and consents to providers.\n\n - Maintain accurate electronic health records (EHR) and patient data.\n\n  Provider Support (Non-Clinical Tasks):\n\n - Assist NPs/MDs with documentation, forms, and prescription requests.\n\n - Ensure HIPAA compliance during virtual interactions and data handling.\n\nQualifications:\n\n - Bilingual (Spanish) preferred\n\n - Prior experience in administrative roles, virtual assistance, or telehealth support preferred.\n\n - Oncology experience preferred.\n\n - Strong organizational, multitasking, and communication skills.\n\n - Proficiency with EHR systems, telehealth platforms, and basic technical troubleshooting.\n\n - Compassionate, patient-centric approach with a commitment to high-quality care.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a fast-paced remote environment.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\nAfter your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed training and be up to speed on Thyme Care tools, processes, and expectations.\n\n - Be comfortable with and correctly follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, communications best practices, and documentation standards.\n\n - Generate daily member reports and assist with day-to-day functions to help prepare our healthcare provider team for consultations.\n\n - Provide inbound telephonic, text, fax, and email support for our members.\n\n - Be able to identify and triage a member's needs to connect them with our Care Teams for clinical support and care coordination.\n\n - Schedule patient and provider visits.\n\n - Contribute to special projects or data entry, including the growth of our virtual medical practice and stop-gap process execution.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.\n\nOrganized. You bring structure to chaos. You’re skilled in juggling multiple tasks and working under pressure without sacrificing organization in your communications and documentation.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. Start-ups are fast-paced environments, and you understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.\n\nA desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.\n\nIdentify priorities and take action. You know how to identify and prioritize a member's needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are addressed immediately.\n\nCulture carrier. You’re curious, resilient, have a growth mindset, and are committed to fostering a positive environment.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $21/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHI. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"18f66522-e7b2-4048-bfb3-3dfda05a1d96","title":"Senior Software Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T21:54:00.666+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/18f66522-e7b2-4048-bfb3-3dfda05a1d96","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/18f66522-e7b2-4048-bfb3-3dfda05a1d96/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Imagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Backend Engineer, you will be a key part of our ever-growing technical team that owns the development of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/thymebox\"><u>Thyme Box</u></a>, our proprietary internal care management platform. Thyme Box is the primary tool that enables 600+ Care Team members to deliver clinical and non-clinical navigation services to members every day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additionally, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Connect with and add to our collaborative, agile team, and learn our tech stack inside and out.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wrap your head around our business model at a high level and develop a deep empathy for the challenges our care team faces in supporting our members.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently plan, build, and deliver multiple features within the Thyme Box product, from concept through launch and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product to scope experiments and shape new product ideas that improve outcomes for our members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with oncology leaders to help them solve quickly evolving business problems through creative, elegant technical solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Play a key role in building the technology that enables our oncology care team to surface ancillary benefit programs and services more efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help create an intuitive user interface that allows our care team to triage patient touch points, from hospitalizations to changes in chemotherapy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Surface data from multiple sources, including user inputs, to keep the care team as up-to-date as possible on their patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ownership of both technical solutions and the growth of the engineering team by mentoring junior engineers and fostering a culture of learning, collaboration, and technical excellence.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 5+ years of experience building, shipping, and supporting software in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve worked in fast-paced, early stage environments. You’re comfortable iterating quickly to make decisions and deliver value to others.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong experience with web development. You’ve built single-page applications in stacks similar to ours: Vue.js/TypeScript, FastAPI/Python, and Postgres.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve taken ownership of features from idea to production, including design, implementation, testing, and ongoing improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve collaborated closely with engineers, product, and cross-functional partners and can clearly communicate technical tradeoffs and solutions to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have, but not required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve used and contributed to AI tooling that supports developer productivity, code quality, and engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have prior experience working in healthcare or health tech.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity. </strong>You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and problems aren’t fully defined. You take ownership, bias toward action, and are comfortable making progress with imperfect information, while maintaining a high bar for quality as products and teams mature.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Curiosity.</strong> You have a drive to understand how things work and love sharing that knowledge with others. You’re energized by learning new technologies, improving systems, and helping your teammates grow. (Find out more about our engineering team’s culture of learning <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://eng.thymecare.com/blog/culture-of-learning\"><u>here</u></a>!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first.</strong> Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply. You’re an empathetic teammate who communicates clearly, collaborates across disciplines, and values giving and receiving thoughtful feedback. You care about building products that improve people’s lives as much as you care about helping your teammates succeed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Net-new development</strong>. You've built and deployed web applications from the ground up. You can deploy and operate services in a Cloud environment with ease and a good fundamental understanding of networking. Our stack includes Python (FastAPI), Postgres, and AWS, but experience with similar technologies is welcome.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Engineering fundamentals.</strong> You know how to deploy software engineering best practices, such as unit tests, code reviews, and design documentation. You have also worked with user interface design. Working in the Healthcare ecosystem is a plus!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $175,500-$195,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nImagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way. \n\nAt Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it. \n\nTo make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Backend Engineer, you will be a key part of our ever-growing technical team that owns the development of Thyme Box https://www.thymecare.com/thymebox, our proprietary internal care management platform. Thyme Box is the primary tool that enables 600+ Care Team members to deliver clinical and non-clinical navigation services to members every day.\n\nAdditionally, you will:\n\n - Connect with and add to our collaborative, agile team, and learn our tech stack inside and out.\n\n - Wrap your head around our business model at a high level and develop a deep empathy for the challenges our care team faces in supporting our members.\n\n - Independently plan, build, and deliver multiple features within the Thyme Box product, from concept through launch and iteration.\n\n - Partner closely with Product to scope experiments and shape new product ideas that improve outcomes for our members.\n\n - Work closely with oncology leaders to help them solve quickly evolving business problems through creative, elegant technical solutions.\n\n - Play a key role in building the technology that enables our oncology care team to surface ancillary benefit programs and services more efficiently.\n\n - Help create an intuitive user interface that allows our care team to triage patient touch points, from hospitalizations to changes in chemotherapy.\n\n - Surface data from multiple sources, including user inputs, to keep the care team as up-to-date as possible on their patients.\n\n - Take ownership of both technical solutions and the growth of the engineering team by mentoring junior engineers and fostering a culture of learning, collaboration, and technical excellence.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - You have 5+ years of experience building, shipping, and supporting software in production.\n\n - You’ve worked in fast-paced, early stage environments. You’re comfortable iterating quickly to make decisions and deliver value to others.\n\n - You have strong experience with web development. You’ve built single-page applications in stacks similar to ours: Vue.js/TypeScript, FastAPI/Python, and Postgres.\n\n - You’ve taken ownership of features from idea to production, including design, implementation, testing, and ongoing improvements.\n\n - You’ve collaborated closely with engineers, product, and cross-functional partners and can clearly communicate technical tradeoffs and solutions to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\nNice to have, but not required:\n\n - You’ve used and contributed to AI tooling that supports developer productivity, code quality, and engineering best practices.\n\n - You have prior experience working in healthcare or health tech.\n\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity. You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and problems aren’t fully defined. You take ownership, bias toward action, and are comfortable making progress with imperfect information, while maintaining a high bar for quality as products and teams mature.\n\n - Curiosity. You have a drive to understand how things work and love sharing that knowledge with others. You’re energized by learning new technologies, improving systems, and helping your teammates grow. (Find out more about our engineering team’s culture of learning here https://eng.thymecare.com/blog/culture-of-learning!)\n\n - People-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply. You’re an empathetic teammate who communicates clearly, collaborates across disciplines, and values giving and receiving thoughtful feedback. You care about building products that improve people’s lives as much as you care about helping your teammates succeed.\n\n - Net-new development. You've built and deployed web applications from the ground up. You can deploy and operate services in a Cloud environment with ease and a good fundamental understanding of networking. Our stack includes Python (FastAPI), Postgres, and AWS, but experience with similar technologies is welcome.\n\n - Engineering fundamentals. You know how to deploy software engineering best practices, such as unit tests, code reviews, and design documentation. You have also worked with user interface design. Working in the Healthcare ecosystem is a plus!\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $175,500-$195,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9a365bf1-61fa-4db7-9ae4-9f1053c16e07","title":"Senior Data Scientist, Data Ingestion & Care Enablement","department":"Data Science","team":"Data Science","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T18:21:59.913+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/9a365bf1-61fa-4db7-9ae4-9f1053c16e07","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/9a365bf1-61fa-4db7-9ae4-9f1053c16e07/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Data Scientist, you will join our Data team to help us build and maintain strong analytic capabilities supporting Thyme Care’s mission. In this position, you will collaborate closely with our Product Manager and our Growth and Operations teams to understand, ingest, and accurately model healthcare data for new and existing customers, supporting updates and fixes throughout the life of the relationship. You’ll develop novel attributes and flags from our existing data to drive action on our Care Team, and build visualizations to report on their impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In the course of your work you should also expect to:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gain a deep understanding of our data platform and contribute to improving our data models and pipelines using SQL and dbt</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with other data scientists, data engineers, and analysts to build scalable and sustainable data models and pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transform incoming eligibility, claims, prior auth, and ADT data to fit into our standard data models, identifying data quality issue or proposed standard data model enhancements as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business requirements into technical plans so you can design data models, pipelines, and analytics before you begin building them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build relationships with data teams at risk-bearing entities (insurers, ACOs, PCPs, etc.) and demonstrate Thyme Care’s expertise in building data &amp; analytics products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that internal customers have fast, accurate, and reliable access to data, supporting their decision-making and operations with high-quality data pipelines</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU HAVE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in working with large healthcare datasets (eligibility, medical / pharmacy claims, prior auth, ADT, etc.), ideally in a healthcare-focused technology startup with mature data structures and pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing data models to support both operations and analytics and building the data transformations in SQL to bring them to life</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An ability to “see beyond the question” to develop scalable solutions that are easily learned and reused by internal customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with, or willingness to quickly learn, dbt and Looker</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission, and in particular our member experience, matters deeply to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose. </strong>You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seek diverse perspectives</strong>. You are humble and actively seek feedback from others, eager to learn and share knowledge.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience.</strong> You have worked with large datasets, ideally in a healthcare-focused technology startup with mature data structures and pipelines as an Analytics Engineer, Data Scientist, or Data Engineer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical ability</strong>.  Proficiency in data modeling, transformation, and claims analytics is crucial. Familiarity with dbt is preferred, but we are open to candidates willing to learn it quickly. A working knowledge of Python and experience with Looker or similar BI tools for data analysis and visualization is a plus.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clear communication.</strong>  You can effectively convey your thoughts and ideas to both technical and non-technical colleagues and stakeholders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.</strong> You have a successful track record working at scaling organizations, in fast-paced environments, and at ambitious startups. You navigate through challenges and find solutions in uncertain situations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $166,500-$185,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Data Scientist, you will join our Data team to help us build and maintain strong analytic capabilities supporting Thyme Care’s mission. In this position, you will collaborate closely with our Product Manager and our Growth and Operations teams to understand, ingest, and accurately model healthcare data for new and existing customers, supporting updates and fixes throughout the life of the relationship. You’ll develop novel attributes and flags from our existing data to drive action on our Care Team, and build visualizations to report on their impact.\n\nIn the course of your work you should also expect to:\n\n - Gain a deep understanding of our data platform and contribute to improving our data models and pipelines using SQL and dbt\n\n - Collaborate with other data scientists, data engineers, and analysts to build scalable and sustainable data models and pipelines\n\n - Transform incoming eligibility, claims, prior auth, and ADT data to fit into our standard data models, identifying data quality issue or proposed standard data model enhancements as needed\n\n - Translate business requirements into technical plans so you can design data models, pipelines, and analytics before you begin building them\n\n - Build relationships with data teams at risk-bearing entities (insurers, ACOs, PCPs, etc.) and demonstrate Thyme Care’s expertise in building data & analytics products\n\n - Ensure that internal customers have fast, accurate, and reliable access to data, supporting their decision-making and operations with high-quality data pipelines\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\n - Expertise in working with large healthcare datasets (eligibility, medical / pharmacy claims, prior auth, ADT, etc.), ideally in a healthcare-focused technology startup with mature data structures and pipelines\n\n - Experience designing data models to support both operations and analytics and building the data transformations in SQL to bring them to life\n\n - An ability to “see beyond the question” to develop scalable solutions that are easily learned and reused by internal customers\n\n - Experience with, or willingness to quickly learn, dbt and Looker\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. Thyme Care’s mission, and in particular our member experience, matters deeply to you.\n\nMove with purpose. You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nSeek diverse perspectives. You are humble and actively seek feedback from others, eager to learn and share knowledge.\n\nExperience. You have worked with large datasets, ideally in a healthcare-focused technology startup with mature data structures and pipelines as an Analytics Engineer, Data Scientist, or Data Engineer.\n\nTechnical ability.  Proficiency in data modeling, transformation, and claims analytics is crucial. Familiarity with dbt is preferred, but we are open to candidates willing to learn it quickly. A working knowledge of Python and experience with Looker or similar BI tools for data analysis and visualization is a plus.\n\nClear communication.  You can effectively convey your thoughts and ideas to both technical and non-technical colleagues and stakeholders.\n\nComfort with ambiguity. You have a successful track record working at scaling organizations, in fast-paced environments, and at ambitious startups. You navigate through challenges and find solutions in uncertain situations.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $166,500-$185,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4d823657-19fd-435c-b9a5-0a918ad46cf1","title":"Collaborating Physician - Georgia (Remote)","department":"Clinical Strategy","team":"Clinical Strategy","employmentType":"PartTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T16:12:09.305+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/4d823657-19fd-435c-b9a5-0a918ad46cf1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/4d823657-19fd-435c-b9a5-0a918ad46cf1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a Georgia-licensed physician who resides within the state to serve as the collaborating physician for our nurse practitioner team providing general oncology triage and palliative care services. This is an oversight and collaboration role — the physician does not see patients directly but provides the required supervision, chart co-signature, clinical consultation, and periodic collaboration with Thyme Care NPs.</p><h3><br /><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as collaborating physician of record under a written nurse protocol agreement filed with the Georgia Medical Board for each supervised NP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Co-sign NP clinical notes and charts per the schedule defined in the protocol agreement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in regular (e.g., monthly or as defined) collaboration meetings with NPs to review cases, patterns of care, and quality concerns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct required periodic chart/record reviews.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">No direct patient care, independent panel, or hands-on clinical services required under this role.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Qualifications</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted Georgia medical license (MD or DO).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Principal practice location physically based in Georgia.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience with NP/APRN collaborative or supervisory relationships preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with remote/asynchronous consultation model.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Time Commitment</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Part-time structured around: (a) scheduled availability windows for clinical questions, (b) periodic (e.g., monthly) collaboration meetings, (c) regular chart reviews.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Compensation</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structured as 1099 independent contractor fee, flat fee of $200/hr x 10hr/week.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nWe are seeking a Georgia-licensed physician who resides within the state to serve as the collaborating physician for our nurse practitioner team providing general oncology triage and palliative care services. This is an oversight and collaboration role — the physician does not see patients directly but provides the required supervision, chart co-signature, clinical consultation, and periodic collaboration with Thyme Care NPs.\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Serve as collaborating physician of record under a written nurse protocol agreement filed with the Georgia Medical Board for each supervised NP.\n\n - Co-sign NP clinical notes and charts per the schedule defined in the protocol agreement.\n\n - Participate in regular (e.g., monthly or as defined) collaboration meetings with NPs to review cases, patterns of care, and quality concerns.\n\n - Conduct required periodic chart/record reviews.\n\n - No direct patient care, independent panel, or hands-on clinical services required under this role.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Active, unrestricted Georgia medical license (MD or DO).\n\n - Principal practice location physically based in Georgia.\n\n - Prior experience with NP/APRN collaborative or supervisory relationships preferred.\n\n - Comfortable with remote/asynchronous consultation model.\n\n\nTIME COMMITMENT\n\n - Part-time structured around: (a) scheduled availability windows for clinical questions, (b) periodic (e.g., monthly) collaboration meetings, (c) regular chart reviews.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n - Structured as 1099 independent contractor fee, flat fee of $200/hr x 10hr/week.\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.\n\n \n ","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8727af90-d580-4260-8e06-3d16899e359f","title":"Director, Strategic Accounts, Health Systems","department":"Hospitals & Health Systems","team":"Hospitals & Health Systems","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T14:13:40.172+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/8727af90-d580-4260-8e06-3d16899e359f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/8727af90-d580-4260-8e06-3d16899e359f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care's health system partnership footprint is growing quickly across new markets. We're hiring an implementation and account management leader to own the full lifecycle of our partnered health system: onboarding new accounts, integrating our care model with their clinical and operational teams, and building the durable operational relationships that make these partnerships perform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is the connective tissue between our health system partners and Thyme Care's internal clinical, product, and analytics teams. You'll be the day-to-day owner our partners rely on, and the internal advocate who ensures we deliver on what we've promised.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a highly visible opportunity to help shape a growing health system partnership portfolio from the ground up. You’ll work closely with growth leadership and partner executives while building the implementation and account management playbook that will support the team as it scales. It’s an ideal role for someone who wants meaningful ownership, enjoys creating structure from ambiguity, and is excited to help define a new model for oncology care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own new partner implementation</strong> — Lead onboarding for newly signed health system partnerships end to end: kickoff, stakeholder mapping, workflow design, data and reporting setup, care team introductions, and go-live.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operationalize our collaboration model</strong> — Run working sessions with partner clinical and operational leaders to define delegation levels and responsibilities across care navigation functions, and translate those decisions into documented workflows both teams follow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Manage ongoing account health</strong> — Serve as the primary point of contact for live partnerships. Run recurring operating reviews, track enrollment and engagement performance, surface issues early, and drive resolution across Thyme Care and partner teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build multi-level relationships</strong> — Develop trusted relationships across partner organizations, from service line administrators and nurse navigators to pharmacy, population health, and executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive performance and expansion</strong> — Use enrollment, engagement, and outcomes data to identify improvement opportunities, then partner internally and externally to act on them. Identify and tee up opportunities to expand the partnership into new populations, programs, or markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inform product and service expansion</strong> — Bring structured partner feedback back to product, clinical, and growth teams to sharpen our model and our pitch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support the full partnership lifecycle</strong> — Flex into pre-signature work alongside the growth lead: deal models, market analysis, and pitch materials, then carry those same accounts through implementation once signed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the operational engine of growth</strong> — Run the behind-the-scenes work that keeps the pipeline moving: performance math, market research, and materials development, so partnership conversations are always backed by rigorous analysis.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in healthcare, with meaningful time spent in health system operations, provider-facing implementation, or account management at a healthcare services or digital health company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of taking partnerships from signature to steady-state: you've run implementations, built joint operating models, and owned executive-level relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in how health systems work: service line structures, care team roles, committee dynamics, and the realities of change management inside large provider organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with value-based care arrangements and programs; oncology experience is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional project management: you create structure, keep many workstreams moving, and never let a commitment slip</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A relationship-first operating style, paired with the directness to hold partners and internal teams accountable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity and an early-stage environment where you'll help define the playbook, not just run it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel to partner sites regularly</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>NICE TO HAVE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting oncology service lines, cancer centers, or oncology value-based programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with clinical workflow integration, EHR-adjacent implementation, or care management program launches</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to ACO, MSSP, or health system-owned health plan operations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission matters deeply to you, particularly our <strong>You know how to navigate health systems.</strong> You understand how clinical, operational, and executive stakeholders work together—and how to move decisions forward within complex organizations.<br /><strong>You turn partnerships into operating models.</strong> You can take a signed agreement and translate it into clear workflows, responsibilities, milestones, and ways of working that both teams follow.<br /><strong>You build trust and accountability.</strong> You develop strong relationships at every level while remaining comfortable addressing missed commitments, resistance, or performance concerns directly.<br /><strong>You create clarity from ambiguity.</strong> You bring structure to evolving work, make thoughtful decisions with incomplete information, and build repeatable processes as you go.<br /><strong>You use data to drive action.</strong> You look beyond activity to understand what is actually improving enrollment, engagement, and outcomes, then turn those insights into practical next steps.<br /><strong>You communicate with influence.</strong> You can lead productive working sessions, simplify complex issues, and tailor your communication for clinical teams, operators, and executives.<br /><strong>You keep members at the center.</strong> You understand that strong partnerships and operational decisions ultimately need to create a better experience for people navigating cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $149,000 - $175,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThyme Care's health system partnership footprint is growing quickly across new markets. We're hiring an implementation and account management leader to own the full lifecycle of our partnered health system: onboarding new accounts, integrating our care model with their clinical and operational teams, and building the durable operational relationships that make these partnerships perform.\n\nThis role is the connective tissue between our health system partners and Thyme Care's internal clinical, product, and analytics teams. You'll be the day-to-day owner our partners rely on, and the internal advocate who ensures we deliver on what we've promised.\n\nThis is a highly visible opportunity to help shape a growing health system partnership portfolio from the ground up. You’ll work closely with growth leadership and partner executives while building the implementation and account management playbook that will support the team as it scales. It’s an ideal role for someone who wants meaningful ownership, enjoys creating structure from ambiguity, and is excited to help define a new model for oncology care.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own new partner implementation — Lead onboarding for newly signed health system partnerships end to end: kickoff, stakeholder mapping, workflow design, data and reporting setup, care team introductions, and go-live.\n\n - Operationalize our collaboration model — Run working sessions with partner clinical and operational leaders to define delegation levels and responsibilities across care navigation functions, and translate those decisions into documented workflows both teams follow.\n\n - Manage ongoing account health — Serve as the primary point of contact for live partnerships. Run recurring operating reviews, track enrollment and engagement performance, surface issues early, and drive resolution across Thyme Care and partner teams.\n\n - Build multi-level relationships — Develop trusted relationships across partner organizations, from service line administrators and nurse navigators to pharmacy, population health, and executive sponsors.\n\n - Drive performance and expansion — Use enrollment, engagement, and outcomes data to identify improvement opportunities, then partner internally and externally to act on them. Identify and tee up opportunities to expand the partnership into new populations, programs, or markets.\n\n - Inform product and service expansion — Bring structured partner feedback back to product, clinical, and growth teams to sharpen our model and our pitch.\n\n - Support the full partnership lifecycle — Flex into pre-signature work alongside the growth lead: deal models, market analysis, and pitch materials, then carry those same accounts through implementation once signed\n\n - Own the operational engine of growth — Run the behind-the-scenes work that keeps the pipeline moving: performance math, market research, and materials development, so partnership conversations are always backed by rigorous analysis.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - 8+ years of experience in healthcare, with meaningful time spent in health system operations, provider-facing implementation, or account management at a healthcare services or digital health company\n\n - A track record of taking partnerships from signature to steady-state: you've run implementations, built joint operating models, and owned executive-level relationships\n\n - Fluency in how health systems work: service line structures, care team roles, committee dynamics, and the realities of change management inside large provider organizations\n\n - Familiarity with value-based care arrangements and programs; oncology experience is a strong plus\n\n - Exceptional project management: you create structure, keep many workstreams moving, and never let a commitment slip\n\n - A relationship-first operating style, paired with the directness to hold partners and internal teams accountable\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and an early-stage environment where you'll help define the playbook, not just run it\n\n - Willingness to travel to partner sites regularly\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting oncology service lines, cancer centers, or oncology value-based programs\n\n - Experience with clinical workflow integration, EHR-adjacent implementation, or care management program launches\n\n - Exposure to ACO, MSSP, or health system-owned health plan operations\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. Thyme Care’s mission matters deeply to you, particularly our You know how to navigate health systems. You understand how clinical, operational, and executive stakeholders work together—and how to move decisions forward within complex organizations.\nYou turn partnerships into operating models. You can take a signed agreement and translate it into clear workflows, responsibilities, milestones, and ways of working that both teams follow.\nYou build trust and accountability. You develop strong relationships at every level while remaining comfortable addressing missed commitments, resistance, or performance concerns directly.\nYou create clarity from ambiguity. You bring structure to evolving work, make thoughtful decisions with incomplete information, and build repeatable processes as you go.\nYou use data to drive action. You look beyond activity to understand what is actually improving enrollment, engagement, and outcomes, then turn those insights into practical next steps.\nYou communicate with influence. You can lead productive working sessions, simplify complex issues, and tailor your communication for clinical teams, operators, and executives.\nYou keep members at the center. You understand that strong partnerships and operational decisions ultimately need to create a better experience for people navigating cancer.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $149,000 - $175,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bb4e419f-7203-4e43-a7e2-41195bc37e08","title":"Sr. Manager, Learning & Quality Operations, Enrollment","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Experience - Enrollment QTE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T01:06:30.807+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/bb4e419f-7203-4e43-a7e2-41195bc37e08","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/bb4e419f-7203-4e43-a7e2-41195bc37e08/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>THE ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care's Enrollment team introduces new members to our model and enrolls them in our cancer care program. While members are already eligible through their insurance, speaking with our team is often the first time they learn the program exists and is available to them. Our team educates them about the many ways we can support them and their caregivers — across both clinical and non-clinical needs — and collects the necessary information to schedule their initial touchpoint with their dedicated care team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>As Sr. Manager of Learning &amp; Quality Operations, you'll lead the team that equips our Enrollment Specialists with the knowledge and expertise to support new members and enroll them into our program. </strong>As Thyme Care continues to grow, the ability to enroll members quickly and effectively will remain a key differentiator in the market — giving this role a unique opportunity to drive organizational impact at scale. The Enrollment Specialist role is at the heart of the enrollment operation and requires a rare blend of sales acumen and a warm, compassionate listening ear. The Learning &amp; Quality Ops team is responsible for helping Enrollment Specialists meet our high standards.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>We're looking for a senior operator and people leader to take our Learning &amp; Quality organization to the next level as Thyme Care continues its rapid growth.</strong> You'll have the opportunity to redesign how we onboard, coach, and develop our team while modernizing our quality program through AI, automation, and new technologies. You'll inherit a strong foundation and build the next generation of learning and quality programs that improve performance, accelerate new hire readiness, and create a more scalable organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to the Head of Enrollment Strategy and is directly responsible for leading the Enrollment team's Learning &amp; Quality function — 10 team members across Quality Assurance and Education &amp; Enablement — supporting a broader Enrollment organization of approximately 150 Enrollment Specialists.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role has an enormous impact on the success of our Enrollment organization — improving the quality of every member conversation and helping more people enroll in Thyme Care's life-changing services.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Planning &amp; Operations</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the Learning &amp; Quality operating cadence.</strong> Lead our planning process each cycle, translating org priorities into clear goals and metrics, and keeping leadership informed on progress, risks, and decisions needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead and develop the team.</strong> Manage and grow a team of 10, including QA and Education &amp; Enablement SMEs, building a strong bench that can execute at a high level as the org scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Close the loop between quality and training.</strong> Build the process that ensures issues surfaced through quality review are captured, routed to the right owners, and converted into training priorities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education &amp; Enablement</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Modernize onboarding.</strong> Redesign the Enrollment onboarding curriculum to boost engagement and cut time-to-proficiency, blending instructor-led training with scalable, self-paced learning through our LMS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the knowledge base.</strong> Maintain the Enrollment Specialist knowledge base and handbook as a single source of truth that's current, accurate, and easy to use.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Quality</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Modernize QA through AI and automation.</strong> Identify and implement technology solutions that improve efficiency and free the team to focus on higher-judgment coaching.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Run the quality engine.</strong> Own monthly QA processes end-to-end: call evaluations, coaching, calibration, and performance reporting, continuously refining standards to measure what matters most.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-8 years in operations, program management and people leadership within a high-growth startup</strong>, with a track record of owning outcomes from strategy through execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Managed a team and drove performance through people leadership</strong> — coaching direct reports, setting clear expectations, and holding your team accountable to results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Built and scaled operational programs or processes</strong> that improved as the organization grew, designing systems that held up under increasing complexity and headcount.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Presented strategy and results to senior leadership,</strong> using data to justify recommendations, secure buy-in, and drive decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partnered cross-functionally at a senior level,</strong> working closely with Operations, Product, Data, or similar functions to align programs with evolving business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Owned metrics and reporting for a function or program,</strong> building the infrastructure that gave leadership visibility into performance and progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exposure to employee training and quality assurance programs</strong> is ideal but not required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind.</strong> The success of your work team whether someone with cancer gets connected to the support they need — you hold that accountability at the center of your work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose.</strong> You're biased toward action. You spot what the team needs to perform well, prioritize without being told to, and keep initiatives moving at pace rather than waiting for a perfect mandate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sharp prioritization instincts.</strong> You know the difference between work that drives real impact and work that satisfies the urge to check something off the list. You juggle competing demands across onboarding, training, and quality without dropping the ball.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong operational and program management chops.</strong> You bring structure to ambiguous problems, scope work clearly, and hold your team accountable to milestones. You've built systems that scale with a growing org, not just run individual projects.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Thrive in ambiguity.</strong> Shifting strategy, priorities, or org structure doesn't throw you off. You build your own clarity and move forward, even when the playbook is still being written.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Self-directed and outcome-oriented.</strong> You figure out what needs to happen, create your own structure to get there, and hold yourself accountable to results, not just effort.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fluent with data.</strong> You're comfortable crunching numbers and drawing conclusions from them, whether you're planning team growth, estimating impact, or assessing progress against goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Excited by technology.</strong> You seek out AI, automation, and new tools as a way to work smarter, and you know how to evaluate what's actually worth adopting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training, learning, or quality program experience is a plus.</strong> Prior involvement in onboarding design, coaching frameworks, or quality review processes will help you ramp more quickly, but isn't essential for success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Healthcare experience is ideal.</strong> Familiarity with healthcare terminology and regulations will help you hit the ground running; if you haven’t worked in healthcare, we’ll want to see a track record of quickly coming up to speed in new industries and environments instead.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, geography, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role, if filled within New York City, is $140,000 - 165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.  This position is also bonus-eligible.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThyme Care's Enrollment team introduces new members to our model and enrolls them in our cancer care program. While members are already eligible through their insurance, speaking with our team is often the first time they learn the program exists and is available to them. Our team educates them about the many ways we can support them and their caregivers — across both clinical and non-clinical needs — and collects the necessary information to schedule their initial touchpoint with their dedicated care team.\n\nAs Sr. Manager of Learning & Quality Operations, you'll lead the team that equips our Enrollment Specialists with the knowledge and expertise to support new members and enroll them into our program. As Thyme Care continues to grow, the ability to enroll members quickly and effectively will remain a key differentiator in the market — giving this role a unique opportunity to drive organizational impact at scale. The Enrollment Specialist role is at the heart of the enrollment operation and requires a rare blend of sales acumen and a warm, compassionate listening ear. The Learning & Quality Ops team is responsible for helping Enrollment Specialists meet our high standards.\n\nWe're looking for a senior operator and people leader to take our Learning & Quality organization to the next level as Thyme Care continues its rapid growth. You'll have the opportunity to redesign how we onboard, coach, and develop our team while modernizing our quality program through AI, automation, and new technologies. You'll inherit a strong foundation and build the next generation of learning and quality programs that improve performance, accelerate new hire readiness, and create a more scalable organization.\n\nThis role reports to the Head of Enrollment Strategy and is directly responsible for leading the Enrollment team's Learning & Quality function — 10 team members across Quality Assurance and Education & Enablement — supporting a broader Enrollment organization of approximately 150 Enrollment Specialists.\n\nThis role has an enormous impact on the success of our Enrollment organization — improving the quality of every member conversation and helping more people enroll in Thyme Care's life-changing services.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nStrategic Planning & Operations\n\n - Own the Learning & Quality operating cadence. Lead our planning process each cycle, translating org priorities into clear goals and metrics, and keeping leadership informed on progress, risks, and decisions needed.\n\n - Lead and develop the team. Manage and grow a team of 10, including QA and Education & Enablement SMEs, building a strong bench that can execute at a high level as the org scales.\n\n - Close the loop between quality and training. Build the process that ensures issues surfaced through quality review are captured, routed to the right owners, and converted into training priorities.\n\nEducation & Enablement\n\n - Modernize onboarding. Redesign the Enrollment onboarding curriculum to boost engagement and cut time-to-proficiency, blending instructor-led training with scalable, self-paced learning through our LMS.\n\n - Own the knowledge base. Maintain the Enrollment Specialist knowledge base and handbook as a single source of truth that's current, accurate, and easy to use.\n\nQuality\n\n - Modernize QA through AI and automation. Identify and implement technology solutions that improve efficiency and free the team to focus on higher-judgment coaching.\n\n - Run the quality engine. Own monthly QA processes end-to-end: call evaluations, coaching, calibration, and performance reporting, continuously refining standards to measure what matters most.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - 6-8 years in operations, program management and people leadership within a high-growth startup, with a track record of owning outcomes from strategy through execution.\n\n - Managed a team and drove performance through people leadership — coaching direct reports, setting clear expectations, and holding your team accountable to results.\n\n - Built and scaled operational programs or processes that improved as the organization grew, designing systems that held up under increasing complexity and headcount.\n\n - Presented strategy and results to senior leadership, using data to justify recommendations, secure buy-in, and drive decisions.\n\n - Partnered cross-functionally at a senior level, working closely with Operations, Product, Data, or similar functions to align programs with evolving business priorities.\n\n - Owned metrics and reporting for a function or program, building the infrastructure that gave leadership visibility into performance and progress.\n\n - Exposure to employee training and quality assurance programs is ideal but not required.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. The success of your work team whether someone with cancer gets connected to the support they need — you hold that accountability at the center of your work.\n\nMove with purpose. You're biased toward action. You spot what the team needs to perform well, prioritize without being told to, and keep initiatives moving at pace rather than waiting for a perfect mandate.\n\nSharp prioritization instincts. You know the difference between work that drives real impact and work that satisfies the urge to check something off the list. You juggle competing demands across onboarding, training, and quality without dropping the ball.\n\nStrong operational and program management chops. You bring structure to ambiguous problems, scope work clearly, and hold your team accountable to milestones. You've built systems that scale with a growing org, not just run individual projects.\n\nThrive in ambiguity. Shifting strategy, priorities, or org structure doesn't throw you off. You build your own clarity and move forward, even when the playbook is still being written.\n\nSelf-directed and outcome-oriented. You figure out what needs to happen, create your own structure to get there, and hold yourself accountable to results, not just effort.\n\nFluent with data. You're comfortable crunching numbers and drawing conclusions from them, whether you're planning team growth, estimating impact, or assessing progress against goals.\n\nExcited by technology. You seek out AI, automation, and new tools as a way to work smarter, and you know how to evaluate what's actually worth adopting.\n\nTraining, learning, or quality program experience is a plus. Prior involvement in onboarding design, coaching frameworks, or quality review processes will help you ramp more quickly, but isn't essential for success.\n\nHealthcare experience is ideal. Familiarity with healthcare terminology and regulations will help you hit the ground running; if you haven’t worked in healthcare, we’ll want to see a track record of quickly coming up to speed in new industries and environments instead.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, geography, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. In accordance with New York City law, the base salary for this role, if filled within New York City, is $140,000 - 165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.  This position is also bonus-eligible.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c255230d-e195-4f26-822e-e12526a2c778","title":"Palliative Oncology Nurse Navigator","department":"Member Experience","team":"RN","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T18:58:33.585+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/c255230d-e195-4f26-822e-e12526a2c778","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/c255230d-e195-4f26-822e-e12526a2c778/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE<br /></strong>As a Thyme Care Palliative Care Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members with serious illness and their care network, conducting conversations about goals and values, advance care planning, and palliative care via phone, email, and video communication. Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive symptom assessments, support members with serious illness longitudinally, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions, when appropriate. You will actively engage with members, addressing clinical issues and efficiently managing any escalations that arise.<strong> <br /><br /></strong><em>Within your first three months, you will:</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support members with serious illness and at the end of life, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Member-Centric Approach: </strong>You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented:</strong> You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills:</strong> You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications:</strong> An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, in addition to <strong>New York, Illinois and/or Michigan licensure preferred</strong>. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in outpatient palliative care and/or home hospice taking care of oncology patients and their caregivers. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications: </strong>It would be exceptional, although not required, that you are a Certified Hospice and Palliative Nurse (CHPN) or have oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications. Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.<br /><br /><strong>OUR VALUES<br /></strong><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.<br /><br />This is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate is non-negotiable at </em>$46.35<em>/hour. Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>To ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.<br /><br />Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.<br /><br />Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nYOUR ROLE\nAs a Thyme Care Palliative Care Nurse Navigator, you'll be a vital clinical resource for our members with serious illness and their care network, conducting conversations about goals and values, advance care planning, and palliative care via phone, email, and video communication. Under the guidance of our Nurse Team Lead, you'll conduct comprehensive symptom assessments, support members with serious illness longitudinally, and facilitate end-of-life care discussions, when appropriate. You will actively engage with members, addressing clinical issues and efficiently managing any escalations that arise. \n\nWithin your first three months, you will:\n\n - Familiarize yourself with Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, and partners.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Nurse leaders and Medical Directors to ensure alignment with clinical protocols and best practices.\n\n - Establish trusting relationships with members and their care network, prioritizing empathy and active listening in every interaction.\n\n - Adhere to Care Team policies, procedures, and documentation standards, contributing to efficient operations and maintaining quality standards.\n\n - Support members with serious illness and at the end of life, coordinating care and providing clinical support as needed.\n\n - Participate in case conferences to monitor member progress, provide updates, and collaborate on targeted support plans with the healthcare team.\n\n - Foster strong partnerships with payers and providers to optimize care delivery and minimize readmissions.\n\n - Collaborate with non-clinical Care Team members to address social determinants of health needs, such as food resources and transportation access.\n\n - Be available for urgent clinical escalations and provide clinical consult support as required.\n\n - Perform other projects and duties as assigned and as related to department business needs and objectives.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - Member-Centric Approach: You prioritize the member experience and demonstrate a deep commitment to Thyme Care's mission.\n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - Qualifications: An active, unrestricted compact Registered Nurse (RN) license is required, in addition to New York, Illinois and/or Michigan licensure preferred. Degree in Nursing (ADN or BSN) required; BSN preferred. Additionally, you have at least 5 years of nursing experience, including 3 years in outpatient palliative care and/or home hospice taking care of oncology patients and their caregivers. \n\n - Certifications: It would be exceptional, although not required, that you are a Certified Hospice and Palliative Nurse (CHPN) or have oncology-related certifications such as Oncology Certified Nurse (OCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse (AOCN), Advanced Oncology Certified Nurse Specialist (AOCNS), or Certified Case Manager (CCM).\n\nThis job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position, its responsibilities, and the required qualifications. Thyme Care reserves the right to modify, add, or remove duties as necessary to meet business needs and organizational objectives.\n\nOUR VALUES\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full-time position. The pay rate is non-negotiable at $46.35/hour. Due to contractual limitations regarding access to PHIs, you must be located within the lower 48 United States to perform this role. OCN certification is required at time of hire or a commitment to obtain within 2 years of hire at Thyme Care. \n\nFluency in Spanish, both written and verbal, is preferred.\n\nTo ensure sufficient clinical coverage, we ask that our Care Team be prepared to work up to 2 holidays per year, compensated at a 1x hourly rate and a 2.5x holiday rate.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5ab2749d-6efd-4f5f-ac95-b476082a8009","title":"Director, Actuarial Services","department":"Health Economics","team":"Health Economics","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T22:12:35.701+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/5ab2749d-6efd-4f5f-ac95-b476082a8009","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/5ab2749d-6efd-4f5f-ac95-b476082a8009/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Imagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Director, Actuarial Services within Thyme Care, you will help lead the development, implementation, and oversight of actuarial models and financial frameworks that support our value-based care partnerships. You will take ownership of end-to-end actuarial functions, including reserving, forecasting, contract reconciliations, and other performance-related actuarial support. Working cross-functionally, you will evaluate contract performance and provide strategic guidance for a portfolio of partners, including risk-based entities, regional plans, and national plans. This is a high-profile position that will regularly collaborate with the C-suite and help advance financial structures through actuarial studies and industry expertise. The responsibilities of the Director, Actuarial Services will include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the development and reporting for a portfolio of Thyme Care partner’s total cost of care savings performance estimates, ensuring the accuracy of the underlying data and methodological consistency with risk-based contracts and actuarial standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead annual financial reconciliations for a portfolio of Thyme Care partner’s value-based contracts, coordinating internal data resources to execute reconciliations and directly interface with actuarial counterparts at existing partners to validate results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide guidance on the fidelity of performance estimates, identify/quantify financial risks and opportunities, and advise the Finance team on revenue recognition decisions tied to projected shared savings.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help identify and evaluate areas of potential underperformance, providing interpretation of results and partnering with health economics and clinical teams to find root causes of emerging issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute actuarial analyses and develop models that allow Thyme Care to quantify the financial and risk trade-offs between different contract features in value-based arrangements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the development and maintenance of financial models that map the organization’s clinical and operational activities to outcomes that drive Thyme Care’s financial performance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Statistics, Actuarial Sciences, Economics, Math or other quantitative discipline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Associateship or Fellowship from the Society of Actuaries (ASA or FSA)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of actuarial experience in health care and/or medical economics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience mentoring junior staff members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Medicare Advantage health plan data (Claims, MMR, MAO-04, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using SQL or another coding language to pull and transform data in a structured manner from large healthcare claims databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in writing clean, efficient code and maintaining strong data management practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working across organizations, building rapport with data teams as well as downstream consumers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in value-based care arrangements and contracting, with a focus on reserving and forecasting for shared savings programs, shared risk programs, and/or global capitation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and demonstrated the ability to articulate the “Here’s What”, the “So What”, and the “Now What” to executive audiences or external parties</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong understanding of financial and clinical metrics used in healthcare and strong working knowledge of industry standards for presenting data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing financial models and/or forecasts in Excel that evaluate the cost of care impact of different clinical interventions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with BI Tools like Looker, Tableau, or Power BI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of pharmacy benefits and/or Medicare Part D</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind:</strong> Thyme Care’s mission, and particularly our member experience, matters deeply to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Critical eye for detail:</strong> Not only do you maintain high standards for data accuracy, presentation and documentation, you have a natural ability to detect data anomalies and identify when outputs look suspicious and warrant further investigation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose:</strong> You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs; and you do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity:</strong>  You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Expertise:</strong> You have a solid understanding of healthcare data and financial concepts; and you can use analytic methods to drive tactical decisions and strategic plans. You’re an expert in right sizing solutions and tailoring your communication to your audience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $190,000 to $210,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nImagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way.\n\nAt Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it.\n\nTo make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Director, Actuarial Services within Thyme Care, you will help lead the development, implementation, and oversight of actuarial models and financial frameworks that support our value-based care partnerships. You will take ownership of end-to-end actuarial functions, including reserving, forecasting, contract reconciliations, and other performance-related actuarial support. Working cross-functionally, you will evaluate contract performance and provide strategic guidance for a portfolio of partners, including risk-based entities, regional plans, and national plans. This is a high-profile position that will regularly collaborate with the C-suite and help advance financial structures through actuarial studies and industry expertise. The responsibilities of the Director, Actuarial Services will include:\n\n - Lead the development and reporting for a portfolio of Thyme Care partner’s total cost of care savings performance estimates, ensuring the accuracy of the underlying data and methodological consistency with risk-based contracts and actuarial standards.\n\n - Lead annual financial reconciliations for a portfolio of Thyme Care partner’s value-based contracts, coordinating internal data resources to execute reconciliations and directly interface with actuarial counterparts at existing partners to validate results.\n\n - Provide guidance on the fidelity of performance estimates, identify/quantify financial risks and opportunities, and advise the Finance team on revenue recognition decisions tied to projected shared savings.\n\n - Help identify and evaluate areas of potential underperformance, providing interpretation of results and partnering with health economics and clinical teams to find root causes of emerging issues.\n\n - Execute actuarial analyses and develop models that allow Thyme Care to quantify the financial and risk trade-offs between different contract features in value-based arrangements.\n\n - Support the development and maintenance of financial models that map the organization’s clinical and operational activities to outcomes that drive Thyme Care’s financial performance.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\nRequired:\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Statistics, Actuarial Sciences, Economics, Math or other quantitative discipline\n\n - Associateship or Fellowship from the Society of Actuaries (ASA or FSA)\n\n - 8+ years of actuarial experience in health care and/or medical economics\n\n - 2+ years of experience mentoring junior staff members\n\n - Understanding of Medicare Advantage health plan data (Claims, MMR, MAO-04, etc.)\n\n - Experience using SQL or another coding language to pull and transform data in a structured manner from large healthcare claims databases\n\n - Proficiency in writing clean, efficient code and maintaining strong data management practices\n\n - Experience working across organizations, building rapport with data teams as well as downstream consumers\n\nPreferred:\n\n - 3+ years of experience in value-based care arrangements and contracting, with a focus on reserving and forecasting for shared savings programs, shared risk programs, and/or global capitation\n\n - Strong communication skills and demonstrated the ability to articulate the “Here’s What”, the “So What”, and the “Now What” to executive audiences or external parties\n\n - A strong understanding of financial and clinical metrics used in healthcare and strong working knowledge of industry standards for presenting data\n\n - Experience developing financial models and/or forecasts in Excel that evaluate the cost of care impact of different clinical interventions\n\n - Familiarity with BI Tools like Looker, Tableau, or Power BI\n\n - Understanding of pharmacy benefits and/or Medicare Part D\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind: Thyme Care’s mission, and particularly our member experience, matters deeply to you.\n\nCritical eye for detail: Not only do you maintain high standards for data accuracy, presentation and documentation, you have a natural ability to detect data anomalies and identify when outputs look suspicious and warrant further investigation.\n\nMove with purpose: You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs; and you do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nComfort with ambiguity:  You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course.\n\nExpertise: You have a solid understanding of healthcare data and financial concepts; and you can use analytic methods to drive tactical decisions and strategic plans. You’re an expert in right sizing solutions and tailoring your communication to your audience.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $190,000 to $210,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d6b6e6e4-337c-440d-b1d8-abcdacde962d","title":"Actuary/Senior Actuarial Analyst","department":"Health Economics","team":"Health Economics","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T22:12:29.865+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d6b6e6e4-337c-440d-b1d8-abcdacde962d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d6b6e6e4-337c-440d-b1d8-abcdacde962d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Actuary or Senior Actuarial Analyst at Thyme Care, you will play a key role in supporting the development, maintenance, and execution of actuarial models and analytics that underpin our value-based care partnerships. This role sits at the intersection of actuarial science, data analytics, and operations, with a strong emphasis on working directly with large healthcare datasets to produce accurate, timely, and actionable insights.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will operate with a meaningful degree of autonomy, owning defined processes and analyses end-to-end, while collaborating closely with actuarial, finance, data science, and clinical partners. This role is well-suited for an actuarial professional who enjoys hands-on technical work, problem solving, and growing responsibility within a fast-paced start-up environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This role is open at multiple levels, depending on experience and scope.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The responsibilities of the Actuary or Senior Actuarial Analyst will include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and execute recurring actuarial and financial analysis for multiple value-based care contracts, including development and maintenance of forecasting models, evaluation of program efficacy using advanced statistical methods, and designing / deploying large-scale database solutions to drive innovation and efficiency in actuarial workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support business development by building actuarial client relationships and own end-to-end actuarial analytic functions relating to a portfolio of national payer clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with actuarial and finance leadership to support financial reconciliations and performance reviews, including preparing analysis outputs and presenting results to executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, run, and optimize SQL queries to extract, transform, and validate healthcare claims and operational data used in actuarial analyses and performance estimates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform ad hoc and exploratory data analyses to investigate performance trends, identify drivers of over- or under-performance, and surface actionable insights for internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the reasonableness and sensitivity of model outputs, proactively identifying data quality issues, assumptions, or emerging risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with analytics, clinical, and operations teams to ensure alignment between data, models, and real-world workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the improvement and automation of actuarial processes and analytical pipelines as the organization scales, helping to establish best practices in a start-up environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Statistics, Actuarial Sciences, Economics, Math or other quantitative discipline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ASA, or near-ASA with demonstrated progress towards credentials (4+ exams)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of actuarial experience in a healthcare environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using SQL or another structured coding language to pull and transform healthcare data from large databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in writing clean, efficient code and ability to troubleshoot and review code written by yourself or others</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with claim-level datasets</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and ability to articulate results, solutions, and recommendations to internal stakeholders (i.e., the “So What”).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in value-based care arrangements and working knowledge of key value-based concepts like Medicare Advantage, risk scores, shared savings, or CMS payment models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to multiple actuarial functions (pricing, reserving, forecasting, trend, pharmacy, etc.) via rotational program or consulting role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one other coding language aside from SQL or SAS (e.g., Python, R, dbt, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise working with spreadsheet software utilizing functions, formulas, and graphs</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind:</strong> Thyme Care’s mission, and particularly our member experience, matters deeply to you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Curiosity</strong>: You’re devoted to discovering something new every day. You’re excited about seeking answers to questions, even if it means thinking outside the box sometimes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Critical eye for detail:</strong> Not only do you maintain high standards for data accuracy, presentation and documentation, you have a natural ability to detect data anomalies and identify when outputs look suspicious and warrant further investigation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose:</strong> You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs; and you do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity:</strong> You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course. You’re comfortable with defining the boundaries of your work, and striking the right balance between seeking guidance and taking initiative.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong><br />OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $108,000 to $150,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs an Actuary or Senior Actuarial Analyst at Thyme Care, you will play a key role in supporting the development, maintenance, and execution of actuarial models and analytics that underpin our value-based care partnerships. This role sits at the intersection of actuarial science, data analytics, and operations, with a strong emphasis on working directly with large healthcare datasets to produce accurate, timely, and actionable insights.\n\nThis role will operate with a meaningful degree of autonomy, owning defined processes and analyses end-to-end, while collaborating closely with actuarial, finance, data science, and clinical partners. This role is well-suited for an actuarial professional who enjoys hands-on technical work, problem solving, and growing responsibility within a fast-paced start-up environment.\n\nThis role is open at multiple levels, depending on experience and scope.\n\nThe responsibilities of the Actuary or Senior Actuarial Analyst will include:\n\n - Own and execute recurring actuarial and financial analysis for multiple value-based care contracts, including development and maintenance of forecasting models, evaluation of program efficacy using advanced statistical methods, and designing / deploying large-scale database solutions to drive innovation and efficiency in actuarial workflows.\n\n - Support business development by building actuarial client relationships and own end-to-end actuarial analytic functions relating to a portfolio of national payer clients.\n\n - Partner with actuarial and finance leadership to support financial reconciliations and performance reviews, including preparing analysis outputs and presenting results to executive audiences.\n\n - Develop, run, and optimize SQL queries to extract, transform, and validate healthcare claims and operational data used in actuarial analyses and performance estimates.\n\n - Perform ad hoc and exploratory data analyses to investigate performance trends, identify drivers of over- or under-performance, and surface actionable insights for internal stakeholders.\n\n - Evaluate the reasonableness and sensitivity of model outputs, proactively identifying data quality issues, assumptions, or emerging risks.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with analytics, clinical, and operations teams to ensure alignment between data, models, and real-world workflows.\n\n - Contribute to the improvement and automation of actuarial processes and analytical pipelines as the organization scales, helping to establish best practices in a start-up environment.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\nRequired:\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Statistics, Actuarial Sciences, Economics, Math or other quantitative discipline\n\n - ASA, or near-ASA with demonstrated progress towards credentials (4+ exams)\n\n - 2+ years of actuarial experience in a healthcare environment\n\n - Experience using SQL or another structured coding language to pull and transform healthcare data from large databases\n\n - Proficiency in writing clean, efficient code and ability to troubleshoot and review code written by yourself or others\n\n - Experience working with claim-level datasets\n\nPreferred:\n\n - Strong communication skills and ability to articulate results, solutions, and recommendations to internal stakeholders (i.e., the “So What”).\n\n - Experience in value-based care arrangements and working knowledge of key value-based concepts like Medicare Advantage, risk scores, shared savings, or CMS payment models\n\n - Exposure to multiple actuarial functions (pricing, reserving, forecasting, trend, pharmacy, etc.) via rotational program or consulting role\n\n - Proficiency in at least one other coding language aside from SQL or SAS (e.g., Python, R, dbt, etc.)\n\n - Expertise working with spreadsheet software utilizing functions, formulas, and graphs\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind: Thyme Care’s mission, and particularly our member experience, matters deeply to you.\n\nCuriosity: You’re devoted to discovering something new every day. You’re excited about seeking answers to questions, even if it means thinking outside the box sometimes.\n\nCritical eye for detail: Not only do you maintain high standards for data accuracy, presentation and documentation, you have a natural ability to detect data anomalies and identify when outputs look suspicious and warrant further investigation.\n\nMove with purpose: You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs; and you do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nComfort with ambiguity: You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities are par for the course. You’re comfortable with defining the boundaries of your work, and striking the right balance between seeking guidance and taking initiative.\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $108,000 to $150,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"016bad94-8fcb-4cb3-a5fc-0569919c5342","title":"Manager of Quality (RN)","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Experience - QTE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T16:44:38.464+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/016bad94-8fcb-4cb3-a5fc-0569919c5342","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/016bad94-8fcb-4cb3-a5fc-0569919c5342/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As <strong>Manager of Quality at Thyme Care</strong>, you will own the day-to-day operation and ongoing maturation of Thyme Care’s patient safety and clinical risk program as our care model and membership continue to grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will ensure safety events are consistently identified, escalated, reviewed, remediated, tracked, and translated into meaningful improvements in care. Building on an established program foundation, you will strengthen workflows and controls, improve the reliability of event review and follow-through, identify trends and emerging risks, and help evolve the program toward a more mature model of structured review and prevention.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will also serve as a clinical quality resource across broader Quality priorities to support NCQA accreditation, annual mock audits, HEDIS/Stars clinical quality gap closure. You will use your RN background to evaluate clinical evidence, data, identify gaps, support remediation, and help ensure Thyme Care’s quality programs are clinically rigorous and operationally sound.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role requires both strong clinical judgment and strong operational instincts. You should be equally comfortable reviewing a complex patient event, facilitating a root cause analysis, improving an existing workflow, analyzing trends, and leading clinical and operational leaders toward sustainable improvements.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/juliastanton/\"><u>Director of Quality</u></a>, you’ll partner closely with Clinical, Care Teams, Compliance, Partnership Operations, Product, and Care Delivery Operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO<br /></strong>Operate &amp; Mature the Patient Safety Program</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own day-to-day operation of Thyme Care’s patient safety program, including event intake, review, escalation, documentation, remediation, and follow-through.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and continuously improve the program’s taxonomy, severity framework, policies, workflows, review criteria, and escalation pathways as needs evolve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify gaps or friction in the program and recommend practical improvements to strengthen reliability, timeliness, and usability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reinforce consistent safety practices through staff education, guidance, and ongoing enablement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help mature the program over time, including structured multidisciplinary review, stronger trend monitoring, and more proactive approaches to clinical risk.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct or facilitate clinical audits, root cause analyses, failure point analyses, and other structured investigations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate findings into corrective actions, prevention strategies, workflow improvements, and staff education.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor safety metrics, incident themes, resolution SLAs, and emerging clinical risks, and prepare monthly reporting for leadership and Quality governance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Clinical Quality, Accreditation &amp; Complaints</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a clinical quality resource supporting case management and population health quality measures and contractual quality measures (Stars/HEDIS).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Complaints program owner on complex investigations and systemic improvement opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support NCQA accreditation readiness, including annual mock audits, clinical evidence review, documentation validation, identification of gaps, and remediation planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support operationalization and monitoring of clinical quality measures, clinical coordination, accreditation, and other clinical quality requirements or standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop or support clinical quality, training, job aids, and enablement based on audit findings, investigations, emerging risks, or identified performance gaps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute clinical expertise to other quality, regulatory, accreditation, and contractual initiatives based on organizational priorities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active, unrestricted RN license.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in clinical care, healthcare quality, patient safety, clinical risk management, care management, health plan operations, or a related healthcare environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing clinical events, quality of care concerns, incidents, complaints, or other patient safety matters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to conduct structured investigations and translate findings into corrective or preventive actions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong clinical documentation, written communication, and critical-thinking skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing or implementing healthcare policies, workflows, SOPs, or staff education.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project management and organizational skills with the ability to manage both recurring operational work and longer-term program initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate and influence effectively across clinical and non-clinical teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort analyzing data and producing recurring quality or safety reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Google Suite/Excel and comfort learning EHR, reporting, and workflow tools.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>NICE TO HAVE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with root cause analysis, failure mode/failure point analysis, PDSA/PDCA, or Lean Six Sigma methods.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in oncology, care management, population health, or complex/high-risk patient populations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CMS, Models of Care, NCQA accreditation or regulatory requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with member complaints, grievances, quality-of-care investigations, or service recovery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPHQ, CPPS, Lean Six Sigma, or related quality/patient safety certification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a startup or value-based care environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with Product or Data teams to build clinical safety reporting or monitoring tools.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Clinical Judgment. </strong>You can assess complex clinical situations, distinguish safety concerns from expected variation, and know when and how to escalate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Safety Mindset. </strong>You approach events with curiosity and rigor, seeking to understand systems and contributing factors rather than simply identifying individual errors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Structured Investigator. </strong>You can gather facts, synthesize clinical and operational information, identify root causes, document conclusions, and develop practical recommendations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Operator &amp; Continuous Improver. </strong>You can take ownership of a new program, run it reliably, identify where processes or controls are falling short, and make practical improvements that strengthen quality and safety over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Member-First. </strong>You consistently connect processes, policies, investigations, and metrics back to the quality and safety of the member experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Analytical &amp; Detail-Oriented. </strong>You are comfortable tracking events, evaluating patterns, monitoring SLAs, and using data to identify risks and improvement opportunities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Collaborator. </strong>You can work effectively with clinicians, operations teams, Compliance, Product, Data, and senior leaders, including when the subject matter is sensitive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Calm Under Pressure. </strong>You can manage urgent or high-risk situations methodically, communicate clearly, and maintain appropriate confidentiality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $126,000-$140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Manager of Quality at Thyme Care, you will own the day-to-day operation and ongoing maturation of Thyme Care’s patient safety and clinical risk program as our care model and membership continue to grow.\n\nYou will ensure safety events are consistently identified, escalated, reviewed, remediated, tracked, and translated into meaningful improvements in care. Building on an established program foundation, you will strengthen workflows and controls, improve the reliability of event review and follow-through, identify trends and emerging risks, and help evolve the program toward a more mature model of structured review and prevention.\n\nYou will also serve as a clinical quality resource across broader Quality priorities to support NCQA accreditation, annual mock audits, HEDIS/Stars clinical quality gap closure. You will use your RN background to evaluate clinical evidence, data, identify gaps, support remediation, and help ensure Thyme Care’s quality programs are clinically rigorous and operationally sound.\n\nThis role requires both strong clinical judgment and strong operational instincts. You should be equally comfortable reviewing a complex patient event, facilitating a root cause analysis, improving an existing workflow, analyzing trends, and leading clinical and operational leaders toward sustainable improvements.\n\nReporting to the Director of Quality https://www.linkedin.com/in/juliastanton/, you’ll partner closely with Clinical, Care Teams, Compliance, Partnership Operations, Product, and Care Delivery Operations.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\nOperate & Mature the Patient Safety Program\n\n - Own day-to-day operation of Thyme Care’s patient safety program, including event intake, review, escalation, documentation, remediation, and follow-through.\n\n - Maintain and continuously improve the program’s taxonomy, severity framework, policies, workflows, review criteria, and escalation pathways as needs evolve.\n\n - Identify gaps or friction in the program and recommend practical improvements to strengthen reliability, timeliness, and usability.\n\n - Reinforce consistent safety practices through staff education, guidance, and ongoing enablement.\n\n - Help mature the program over time, including structured multidisciplinary review, stronger trend monitoring, and more proactive approaches to clinical risk.\n\n - Conduct or facilitate clinical audits, root cause analyses, failure point analyses, and other structured investigations.\n\n - Translate findings into corrective actions, prevention strategies, workflow improvements, and staff education.\n\n - Monitor safety metrics, incident themes, resolution SLAs, and emerging clinical risks, and prepare monthly reporting for leadership and Quality governance.\n\nSupport Clinical Quality, Accreditation & Complaints\n\n - Serve as a clinical quality resource supporting case management and population health quality measures and contractual quality measures (Stars/HEDIS).\n\n - Partner with the Complaints program owner on complex investigations and systemic improvement opportunities.\n\n - Support NCQA accreditation readiness, including annual mock audits, clinical evidence review, documentation validation, identification of gaps, and remediation planning.\n\n - Support operationalization and monitoring of clinical quality measures, clinical coordination, accreditation, and other clinical quality requirements or standards.\n\n - Develop or support clinical quality, training, job aids, and enablement based on audit findings, investigations, emerging risks, or identified performance gaps.\n\n - Contribute clinical expertise to other quality, regulatory, accreditation, and contractual initiatives based on organizational priorities.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - Active, unrestricted RN license.\n\n - 4+ years of experience in clinical care, healthcare quality, patient safety, clinical risk management, care management, health plan operations, or a related healthcare environment.\n\n - Experience reviewing clinical events, quality of care concerns, incidents, complaints, or other patient safety matters.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to conduct structured investigations and translate findings into corrective or preventive actions.\n\n - Strong clinical documentation, written communication, and critical-thinking skills.\n\n - Experience developing or implementing healthcare policies, workflows, SOPs, or staff education.\n\n - Strong project management and organizational skills with the ability to manage both recurring operational work and longer-term program initiatives.\n\n - Ability to collaborate and influence effectively across clinical and non-clinical teams.\n\n - Comfort analyzing data and producing recurring quality or safety reports.\n\n - Proficiency with Google Suite/Excel and comfort learning EHR, reporting, and workflow tools.\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with root cause analysis, failure mode/failure point analysis, PDSA/PDCA, or Lean Six Sigma methods.\n\n - Experience in oncology, care management, population health, or complex/high-risk patient populations.\n\n - Experience with CMS, Models of Care, NCQA accreditation or regulatory requirements.\n\n - Experience with member complaints, grievances, quality-of-care investigations, or service recovery.\n\n - CPHQ, CPPS, Lean Six Sigma, or related quality/patient safety certification.\n\n - Experience in a startup or value-based care environment.\n\n - Experience partnering with Product or Data teams to build clinical safety reporting or monitoring tools.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nStrong Clinical Judgment. You can assess complex clinical situations, distinguish safety concerns from expected variation, and know when and how to escalate.\n\nPatient Safety Mindset. You approach events with curiosity and rigor, seeking to understand systems and contributing factors rather than simply identifying individual errors.\n\nStructured Investigator. You can gather facts, synthesize clinical and operational information, identify root causes, document conclusions, and develop practical recommendations.\n\nStrong Operator & Continuous Improver. You can take ownership of a new program, run it reliably, identify where processes or controls are falling short, and make practical improvements that strengthen quality and safety over time.\n\nMember-First. You consistently connect processes, policies, investigations, and metrics back to the quality and safety of the member experience.\n\nAnalytical & Detail-Oriented. You are comfortable tracking events, evaluating patterns, monitoring SLAs, and using data to identify risks and improvement opportunities.\n\nStrong Collaborator. You can work effectively with clinicians, operations teams, Compliance, Product, Data, and senior leaders, including when the subject matter is sensitive.\n\nCalm Under Pressure. You can manage urgent or high-risk situations methodically, communicate clearly, and maintain appropriate confidentiality.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $126,000-$140,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n \n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"12874a6d-7e53-4f77-8b3b-e06d3f695970","title":"Senior Manager, Quality","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Experience - QTE","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T17:03:52.626+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/12874a6d-7e53-4f77-8b3b-e06d3f695970","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/12874a6d-7e53-4f77-8b3b-e06d3f695970/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Senior Manager, Quality, you will own Thyme Care’s approach to contractual quality performance, including HEDIS, Stars, partner-specific quality measures, and other emerging quality priorities and opportunities.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own the end-to-end operationalization of quality measures and campaigns—from understanding the measure and identifying the opportunity, to designing the workflow, developing job aids and enablement, coordinating implementation, monitoring execution, and evaluating performance. This portfolio includes measures and programs such as seasonal flu vaccination, health risk assessments, in-home wellness assessments, transition of care measures, preventive screenings, and other payer-specific quality initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is both an operational and analytical role. You will be expected to work directly with quality and operational data, investigate performance questions, define reporting requirements and measure logic, and translate findings into practical workflows and interventions. You’ll partner closely with Data and Product, while also working directly with Care Teams and Operations to make sure campaigns can be executed reliably in practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reporting to the Director of Quality, this is an opportunity to build and scale a critical capability and improve patient outcomes. As capacity allows, you may also contribute to broader Quality priorities such as accreditation, member complaints, and patient safety initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own Quality Measures &amp; Campaigns</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the portfolio of HEDIS, Stars, contractual quality measures, and related campaigns across Thyme Care’s payer partnerships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate measure specifications and partner requirements into executable workflows, including member identification, tasking, outreach models, roles, timelines, escalation paths, and reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain the job aids, SOPs, training, and enablement needed for Care Teams and Operations to execute campaigns consistently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead implementation of initiatives such as vaccinations, HRAs, in-home wellness assessments, preventive screenings, transition-of-care measures, and other quality gap-closure programs.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently analyze quality and operational data to identify gaps, validate performance, understand drivers, and recommend interventions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish performance metrics and operating cadences for each initiative and monitor and report updates on both measure outcomes and operational execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct retrospectives, root cause analyses, and structured improvement cycles to identify where workflows are breaking down and improve future performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Data as needed to define measure logic, dashboards, patient lists, gap reporting, and automated monitoring; independently validate outputs and troubleshoot discrepancies.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Scalable Quality Operations</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead cross-functional execution across Partnership Operations, Care Teams, Clinical, Data, Product, Marketing, and Care Delivery Operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build repeatable playbooks, campaign calendars, prioritization processes, and operating infrastructure that allow Thyme Care to support a growing portfolio of quality measures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply automation and AI to improve processes, structured data capture, reporting files, and other capabilities that reduce manual work and make quality programs easier to scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Surface risks, tradeoffs, and recommendations to senior leaders and contribute to the Quality Committee and other quality governance activities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 6+ years of experience in healthcare quality, quality operations, population health, value-based care, managed care, health plan operations, consulting, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have meaningful experience with HEDIS, Stars, payer quality measures, or other healthcare quality performance programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have translated quality, clinical, or payer requirements into operational workflows and successfully implemented them across frontline teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience prioritizing across multiple quality opportunities, balancing expected impact, contractual importance, operational effort, feasibility, and team capacity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong project and program management skills, including experience managing multiple concurrent campaigns or initiatives with different owners, populations, timelines, and dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have independently analyzed healthcare or operational data and translated findings into actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are advanced in Excel or Google Sheets, including working with large datasets, complex formulas, and data validation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have working proficiency with SQL, or comparable experience independently querying and manipulating complex datasets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience with BI and reporting tools such as Looker, Tableau, Power BI, or equivalent platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can define reporting requirements, measure logic, and data specifications in partnership with Data or Analytics teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You communicate clearly in writing and verbally, from staff-facing operational guidance to performance updates, tradeoffs, and recommendations for senior and cross-functional stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>NICE TO HAVE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing member outreach campaigns, care-team workflows, tasking, job aids, or training in support of quality measures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with claims, eligibility, clinical, care management, or quality-measure datasets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building dashboards, automated reporting, or reusable quality analytics workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience with NCQA HEDIS specifications or Stars programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Medicare Advantage, Medicaid managed care, or risk adjustment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using automation or AI to support quality reporting, gap identification, or workflow efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPHQ, Lean Six Sigma, or related quality improvement or analytics training.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational &amp; Execution-Oriented.</strong> You can take a quality measure or payer requirement and turn it into a practical, scalable operating model. You think through workflows, owners, tasking, job aids, training, timelines, member lists, escalation paths, and reporting—not just the strategy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Analytical &amp; Technically Fluent.</strong> You can independently work through messy healthcare data, validate assumptions, identify trends and outliers, and turn analysis into action. You are comfortable moving between spreadsheets, BI tools, measure specifications, and operational workflows—and partnering with Data teams on more complex analyses.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Quality Performance Expertise. </strong>You understand how HEDIS, Stars, payer quality measures, and contractual requirements translate into operational workflows and performance improvement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Cross-Functional Leader. </strong>You can influence teams you do not manage directly and establish alignment across technical, clinical, operational, and commercial stakeholders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuous Improvement Mindset. </strong>You don't stop at launching a campaign or reporting performance. You want to understand where execution is breaking down, why gaps persist, what should change, and whether the intervention worked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,250 - $165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Senior Manager, Quality, you will own Thyme Care’s approach to contractual quality performance, including HEDIS, Stars, partner-specific quality measures, and other emerging quality priorities and opportunities.\n\nYou will own the end-to-end operationalization of quality measures and campaigns—from understanding the measure and identifying the opportunity, to designing the workflow, developing job aids and enablement, coordinating implementation, monitoring execution, and evaluating performance. This portfolio includes measures and programs such as seasonal flu vaccination, health risk assessments, in-home wellness assessments, transition of care measures, preventive screenings, and other payer-specific quality initiatives.\n\nThis is both an operational and analytical role. You will be expected to work directly with quality and operational data, investigate performance questions, define reporting requirements and measure logic, and translate findings into practical workflows and interventions. You’ll partner closely with Data and Product, while also working directly with Care Teams and Operations to make sure campaigns can be executed reliably in practice.\n\nReporting to the Director of Quality, this is an opportunity to build and scale a critical capability and improve patient outcomes. As capacity allows, you may also contribute to broader Quality priorities such as accreditation, member complaints, and patient safety initiatives.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nOwn Quality Measures & Campaigns\n\n - Own the portfolio of HEDIS, Stars, contractual quality measures, and related campaigns across Thyme Care’s payer partnerships.\n\n - Translate measure specifications and partner requirements into executable workflows, including member identification, tasking, outreach models, roles, timelines, escalation paths, and reporting.\n\n - Develop and maintain the job aids, SOPs, training, and enablement needed for Care Teams and Operations to execute campaigns consistently.\n\n - Lead implementation of initiatives such as vaccinations, HRAs, in-home wellness assessments, preventive screenings, transition-of-care measures, and other quality gap-closure programs.\n\n - Independently analyze quality and operational data to identify gaps, validate performance, understand drivers, and recommend interventions.\n\n - Establish performance metrics and operating cadences for each initiative and monitor and report updates on both measure outcomes and operational execution.\n\n - Conduct retrospectives, root cause analyses, and structured improvement cycles to identify where workflows are breaking down and improve future performance.\n\n - Partner with Data as needed to define measure logic, dashboards, patient lists, gap reporting, and automated monitoring; independently validate outputs and troubleshoot discrepancies.\n\nBuild Scalable Quality Operations\n\n - Lead cross-functional execution across Partnership Operations, Care Teams, Clinical, Data, Product, Marketing, and Care Delivery Operations.\n\n - Build repeatable playbooks, campaign calendars, prioritization processes, and operating infrastructure that allow Thyme Care to support a growing portfolio of quality measures.\n\n - Apply automation and AI to improve processes, structured data capture, reporting files, and other capabilities that reduce manual work and make quality programs easier to scale.\n\n - Surface risks, tradeoffs, and recommendations to senior leaders and contribute to the Quality Committee and other quality governance activities.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - You have 6+ years of experience in healthcare quality, quality operations, population health, value-based care, managed care, health plan operations, consulting, or a related field.\n\n - You have meaningful experience with HEDIS, Stars, payer quality measures, or other healthcare quality performance programs.\n\n - You have translated quality, clinical, or payer requirements into operational workflows and successfully implemented them across frontline teams.\n\n - You have experience prioritizing across multiple quality opportunities, balancing expected impact, contractual importance, operational effort, feasibility, and team capacity.\n\n - You have strong project and program management skills, including experience managing multiple concurrent campaigns or initiatives with different owners, populations, timelines, and dependencies.\n\n - You have independently analyzed healthcare or operational data and translated findings into actionable recommendations.\n\n - You are advanced in Excel or Google Sheets, including working with large datasets, complex formulas, and data validation.\n\n - You have working proficiency with SQL, or comparable experience independently querying and manipulating complex datasets.\n\n - You have experience with BI and reporting tools such as Looker, Tableau, Power BI, or equivalent platforms.\n\n - You can define reporting requirements, measure logic, and data specifications in partnership with Data or Analytics teams.\n\n - You communicate clearly in writing and verbally, from staff-facing operational guidance to performance updates, tradeoffs, and recommendations for senior and cross-functional stakeholders.\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience designing member outreach campaigns, care-team workflows, tasking, job aids, or training in support of quality measures.\n\n - Experience working with claims, eligibility, clinical, care management, or quality-measure datasets.\n\n - Experience building dashboards, automated reporting, or reusable quality analytics workflows.\n\n - Direct experience with NCQA HEDIS specifications or Stars programs.\n\n - Experience with Medicare Advantage, Medicaid managed care, or risk adjustment.\n\n - Experience using automation or AI to support quality reporting, gap identification, or workflow efficiency.\n\n - CPHQ, Lean Six Sigma, or related quality improvement or analytics training.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nOperational & Execution-Oriented. You can take a quality measure or payer requirement and turn it into a practical, scalable operating model. You think through workflows, owners, tasking, job aids, training, timelines, member lists, escalation paths, and reporting—not just the strategy.\n\nAnalytical & Technically Fluent. You can independently work through messy healthcare data, validate assumptions, identify trends and outliers, and turn analysis into action. You are comfortable moving between spreadsheets, BI tools, measure specifications, and operational workflows—and partnering with Data teams on more complex analyses.\n\nQuality Performance Expertise. You understand how HEDIS, Stars, payer quality measures, and contractual requirements translate into operational workflows and performance improvement.\n\nStrong Cross-Functional Leader. You can influence teams you do not manage directly and establish alignment across technical, clinical, operational, and commercial stakeholders.\n\nContinuous Improvement Mindset. You don't stop at launching a campaign or reporting performance. You want to understand where execution is breaking down, why gaps persist, what should change, and whether the intervention worked.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $140,250 - $165,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. This position is also bonus-eligible.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n \n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"71e95299-56f1-46eb-aa68-3f3f88894bae","title":"IT Support Engineer","department":"IT & Security","team":"IT & Security","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York, NY ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T17:22:54.627+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/71e95299-56f1-46eb-aa68-3f3f88894bae","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/71e95299-56f1-46eb-aa68-3f3f88894bae/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an IT Support Engineer at Thyme Care, you’ll deliver exceptional day-to-day IT support to our fast-growing team. Your primary focus is fast, friendly help for our Care team, and you’ll also support a diverse group of remote employees across the United States. You’ll be a primary point of contact for internal end users and the face of our \"Support Thyme\" helpdesk — the person people are glad to see when something isn’t working.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is based in our New York City office, where you’ll be our onsite presence — owning the in-office IT experience while partnering with a distributed IT &amp; Security team to support a hybrid workforce. Reporting to our IT Manager, you’ll cover a broad range of work: endpoint and identity management, SaaS administration, security and access, conference-room and A/V support, networking, and everyday break-fix. Our job is to remove technical friction and put the right tools, automation, and AI in people’s hands so they can do their best work for our members. Supporting a modern, fast-growing organization takes a versatile IT team that’s as comfortable with security and automation as it is with white-glove support.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within your first sixty days on the job, we’ll expect you to:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get to know our organization and build relationships across the team, with emphasis on our NYC office</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with our People Operations Manager and IT team to drive new-hire orientation and get new employees fully onboarded</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a first point of contact for helpdesk tickets — in person for the NYC office and remotely for distributed teammates across the organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strengthen our internal support operations with clear, well-maintained documentation, and keep device lifecycle and asset management running smoothly</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">By the end of your fourth month, you will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Know our ticketing system inside out and consistently meet first-response and time-to-resolution targets that scale as we grow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead IT onboarding for new hires so they’re fully set up and productive from day one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own your scope within cross-functional IT projects that make the whole team more efficient — from tooling rollouts to automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the go-to onsite support in our NYC office — from configuring and troubleshooting conference rooms of every size to providing white-glove A/V support for executive and all-hands meetings. You own the office’s conference-room tech: displays, Zoom Rooms, and everything that makes a meeting just work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administer our MDM and endpoint fleet, support telephony and softphone systems, help manage identity and access, and handle light networking troubleshooting as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help mature our IT and security posture — device compliance, access reviews, and safe, effective use of AI tools that make the team faster</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first</strong>. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience. </strong>You have 3–5 years of IT support experience, ideally in a fast-paced startup environment. You’re well versed in supporting and administering macOS and Windows, and comfortable with modern SaaS, identity, and device management — Google Workspace, Mosyle (or a comparable MDM), Cisco Meraki, 1Password, Zoom, Neat AV hardware. and Slack. You know how to deploy, configure, and maintain macOS and Windows fleets at scale, and you can hold your own on identity, access, and endpoint security. Bonus points if you script and automate routine work and use AI tools to move faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Delight</strong>. You thrive in a customer-facing role supporting a vast array of users: from tech savvy engineers to first time tech users. You’re comfortable supporting team members in person or remotely. No matter what the situation or pressure, you always maintain your composure with a warm smile and friendly invitation to return.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective collaboration</strong>. You build collaborative and productive working relationships that allow you to do your job well, regardless the level, location, or situation of your team member. These relationships drive business outcomes and allow us to serve our members even better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growth mindset</strong>. You constantly strive to implement best practices and find new ways to bring more to the table and do your job well.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with Purpose</strong>. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $84,600-$94,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs an IT Support Engineer at Thyme Care, you’ll deliver exceptional day-to-day IT support to our fast-growing team. Your primary focus is fast, friendly help for our Care team, and you’ll also support a diverse group of remote employees across the United States. You’ll be a primary point of contact for internal end users and the face of our \"Support Thyme\" helpdesk — the person people are glad to see when something isn’t working.\n\nThis role is based in our New York City office, where you’ll be our onsite presence — owning the in-office IT experience while partnering with a distributed IT & Security team to support a hybrid workforce. Reporting to our IT Manager, you’ll cover a broad range of work: endpoint and identity management, SaaS administration, security and access, conference-room and A/V support, networking, and everyday break-fix. Our job is to remove technical friction and put the right tools, automation, and AI in people’s hands so they can do their best work for our members. Supporting a modern, fast-growing organization takes a versatile IT team that’s as comfortable with security and automation as it is with white-glove support.\n\n - Within your first sixty days on the job, we’ll expect you to:\n   \n   - Get to know our organization and build relationships across the team, with emphasis on our NYC office\n   \n   - Partner with our People Operations Manager and IT team to drive new-hire orientation and get new employees fully onboarded\n   \n   - Be a first point of contact for helpdesk tickets — in person for the NYC office and remotely for distributed teammates across the organization\n   \n   - Strengthen our internal support operations with clear, well-maintained documentation, and keep device lifecycle and asset management running smoothly\n\n - By the end of your fourth month, you will:\n   \n   - Know our ticketing system inside out and consistently meet first-response and time-to-resolution targets that scale as we grow\n   \n   - Lead IT onboarding for new hires so they’re fully set up and productive from day one\n   \n   - Own your scope within cross-functional IT projects that make the whole team more efficient — from tooling rollouts to automation\n   \n   - Be the go-to onsite support in our NYC office — from configuring and troubleshooting conference rooms of every size to providing white-glove A/V support for executive and all-hands meetings. You own the office’s conference-room tech: displays, Zoom Rooms, and everything that makes a meeting just work\n   \n   - Administer our MDM and endpoint fleet, support telephony and softphone systems, help manage identity and access, and handle light networking troubleshooting as needed\n   \n   - Help mature our IT and security posture — device compliance, access reviews, and safe, effective use of AI tools that make the team faster\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nPeople-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.\n\nExperience. You have 3–5 years of IT support experience, ideally in a fast-paced startup environment. You’re well versed in supporting and administering macOS and Windows, and comfortable with modern SaaS, identity, and device management — Google Workspace, Mosyle (or a comparable MDM), Cisco Meraki, 1Password, Zoom, Neat AV hardware. and Slack. You know how to deploy, configure, and maintain macOS and Windows fleets at scale, and you can hold your own on identity, access, and endpoint security. Bonus points if you script and automate routine work and use AI tools to move faster.\n\nCustomer Delight. You thrive in a customer-facing role supporting a vast array of users: from tech savvy engineers to first time tech users. You’re comfortable supporting team members in person or remotely. No matter what the situation or pressure, you always maintain your composure with a warm smile and friendly invitation to return.\n\nEffective collaboration. You build collaborative and productive working relationships that allow you to do your job well, regardless the level, location, or situation of your team member. These relationships drive business outcomes and allow us to serve our members even better.\n\nGrowth mindset. You constantly strive to implement best practices and find new ways to bring more to the table and do your job well.\n\nMove with Purpose. You’re a self-starter and don’t need anyone to tell you when to do something. You’re always solving problems and going the extra mile for others.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $84,600-$94,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d3eb20a7-7c50-4beb-bf3a-9bfc21a262bf","title":"Care Partner","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Experience- Care Partner","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:28:14.926+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d3eb20a7-7c50-4beb-bf3a-9bfc21a262bf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d3eb20a7-7c50-4beb-bf3a-9bfc21a262bf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Care Partner, your job is to engage Thyme Care members and navigate them through their cancer journey. You will report into a Care Partner Team Lead and spend most of your day reaching out to our members by phone, text, and email.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will engage with our members to identify changes in their health &amp; social needs, discuss their goals and values to support advanced care planning, and connect them to resources. Part of your role will also be to assess the urgency of their need, determine the root cause and establish the appropriate next step. You will be responsible to connect the member to appropriate healthcare and community-based resources including Thyme Care nurses and providers.  You will also research and connect members with external healthcare providers, transportation, financial grants, emotional support resources, and insurance-provided benefits.  You will execute your member support using evidence-based assessments, prior experience, and problem solving skills. In this critical role, you will serve as the primary point of contact throughout the member’s Thyme Care journey, while collaborating closely with an interdisciplinary team of healthcare professionals to ensure the member has holistic support in their care. You will spend the majority of your day working within a phone queue, handling both inbound and outbound calls in a structured, high-volume environment. You will frequently shift between member interactions, documentation, and coordination tasks throughout the day, requiring strong time management and the ability to stay focused in a fast-moving environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Note:</strong> In order to ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes a 30-minute lunch and two 15-minute breaks.<br /><br /><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>After your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed virtual onboarding and training (two weeks long) and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. You’ll spend your day outreaching to members, researching community and healthcare resources that meet their needs, and connecting members to those resources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. You use that relationship to prioritize how we should address their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be able to identify and prioritize a member's needs and then know where to go to get them help. This means you’ll be working to connect them with their healthcare providers, community resources, social services, diagnostic appointments, and medical treatments and assist with overcoming barriers (e.g., health literacy, unstable housing).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, best practices, and highest standards. You consistently meet or exceed defined productivity and quality metrics, including call volume, responsiveness, documentation timeliness, and member engagement  while managing your time effectively in a structured environment where performance is measured in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your productivity and quality goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to scheduled shifts, including time in queue, breaks, and availability expectations to ensure consistent member coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently drive value in your member interactions through high priority activities and assessments such as:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced care planning support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinating care, including telehealth visits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalating clinical symptoms to our clinical teams</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your resume and prior roles reflect:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 2 years of experience in a patient-facing role conducting care coordination, healthcare navigation, non-clinical case management, resource navigation, or community health work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in a metrics-driven, feedback-oriented environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a fast-paced, high-volume, metrics-driven environment (e.g., contact center, care navigation, care coordination).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in assessing and addressing both patient/member’s stated needs as well as the ability to identify needs that aren’t explicitly expressed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build rapport and trust quickly with patients/members in a high-volume, primarily phone-based environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate, trustworthy, and empathetic when working with clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build relationships with different types of people, including clients, organization members, and health care providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and interpersonal skills and ability to speak concisely to clients and Care Team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized with confidential client material and appointment tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible and adaptable in response to changing client and health care providers’ needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for individuals who thrive in structured, high-volume environments and are energized by balancing efficiency with meaningful member interactions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives. Healthcare experience preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose. </strong>You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seek diverse perspectives. </strong>You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.  </strong>You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with technology. </strong>We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A quiet working space. </strong>It’s important you’ve worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment with no/limited distractions during your scheduled shifts and are able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a non-exempt, full time position. <em>The pay rate for this role is $24.76/hour.</em> To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a growing organization and recruit and employ a large number of these roles. Because of this, we actively interview for this position even when we don't have an immediate opening. Candidates who complete the interview process and fit the role are eligible for the next available opening. We will reach back out once an open position becomes available.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Recruiting team will share more information about our hiring philosophy during an initial phone screen and can answer questions you might have about it then.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be cautious of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><u>recruitment fraud</u></a>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Care Partner, your job is to engage Thyme Care members and navigate them through their cancer journey. You will report into a Care Partner Team Lead and spend most of your day reaching out to our members by phone, text, and email.\n\nYou will engage with our members to identify changes in their health & social needs, discuss their goals and values to support advanced care planning, and connect them to resources. Part of your role will also be to assess the urgency of their need, determine the root cause and establish the appropriate next step. You will be responsible to connect the member to appropriate healthcare and community-based resources including Thyme Care nurses and providers.  You will also research and connect members with external healthcare providers, transportation, financial grants, emotional support resources, and insurance-provided benefits.  You will execute your member support using evidence-based assessments, prior experience, and problem solving skills. In this critical role, you will serve as the primary point of contact throughout the member’s Thyme Care journey, while collaborating closely with an interdisciplinary team of healthcare professionals to ensure the member has holistic support in their care. You will spend the majority of your day working within a phone queue, handling both inbound and outbound calls in a structured, high-volume environment. You will frequently shift between member interactions, documentation, and coordination tasks throughout the day, requiring strong time management and the ability to stay focused in a fast-moving environment.\n\nNote: In order to ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes a 30-minute lunch and two 15-minute breaks.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\nAfter your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed virtual onboarding and training (two weeks long) and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. You’ll spend your day outreaching to members, researching community and healthcare resources that meet their needs, and connecting members to those resources\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. You use that relationship to prioritize how we should address their needs.\n\n - Be able to identify and prioritize a member's needs and then know where to go to get them help. This means you’ll be working to connect them with their healthcare providers, community resources, social services, diagnostic appointments, and medical treatments and assist with overcoming barriers (e.g., health literacy, unstable housing).\n\n - Follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, best practices, and highest standards. You consistently meet or exceed defined productivity and quality metrics, including call volume, responsiveness, documentation timeliness, and member engagement  while managing your time effectively in a structured environment where performance is measured in real time.\n\n - Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your productivity and quality goals\n\n - Adhere to scheduled shifts, including time in queue, breaks, and availability expectations to ensure consistent member coverage.\n\n - Consistently drive value in your member interactions through high priority activities and assessments such as:\n   \n   - Advanced care planning support\n   \n   - Coordinating care, including telehealth visits\n   \n   - Escalating clinical symptoms to our clinical teams\n     \n     \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nYour resume and prior roles reflect:\n\n - At least 2 years of experience in a patient-facing role conducting care coordination, healthcare navigation, non-clinical case management, resource navigation, or community health work\n\n - Success in a metrics-driven, feedback-oriented environment\n\n - Experience working in a fast-paced, high-volume, metrics-driven environment (e.g., contact center, care navigation, care coordination).\n\n - Experience in assessing and addressing both patient/member’s stated needs as well as the ability to identify needs that aren’t explicitly expressed\n\n - Ability to build rapport and trust quickly with patients/members in a high-volume, primarily phone-based environment\n\n - Passionate, trustworthy, and empathetic when working with clients\n\n - Ability to build relationships with different types of people, including clients, organization members, and health care providers\n\n - Good communication and interpersonal skills and ability to speak concisely to clients and Care Team members\n\n - Organized with confidential client material and appointment tracking\n\n - Flexible and adaptable in response to changing client and health care providers’ needs\n\n - This role is ideal for individuals who thrive in structured, high-volume environments and are energized by balancing efficiency with meaningful member interactions\n\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives. Healthcare experience preferred.\n\nMove with purpose. You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nSeek diverse perspectives. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity.  You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.\n\nComfort with technology. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.\n\nA quiet working space. It’s important you’ve worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment with no/limited distractions during your scheduled shifts and are able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $24.76/hour. To perform this role you must be located within the lower 48 United States due to contractual limitations with accessing PHIs. We offer a choice of great medical, dental, and vision insurance plans as well as a generous vacation policy for full-time employees, so you can prioritize the most important parts of your life.\n\nWe are a growing organization and recruit and employ a large number of these roles. Because of this, we actively interview for this position even when we don't have an immediate opening. Candidates who complete the interview process and fit the role are eligible for the next available opening. We will reach back out once an open position becomes available.\n\nThe Recruiting team will share more information about our hiring philosophy during an initial phone screen and can answer questions you might have about it then.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"259f323d-2435-48f8-bd60-575a2c9356d6","title":"Bilingual Care Partner","department":"Member Experience","team":"Member Experience- Care Partner","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:31:46.184+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/259f323d-2435-48f8-bd60-575a2c9356d6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/259f323d-2435-48f8-bd60-575a2c9356d6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Imagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>YOUR ROLE</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a bilingual Spanish/English Care Partner, your job is to engage Thyme Care members and navigate them through their cancer journey. You will report into a Care Partner Team Lead and spend most of your day reaching out to our members by phone, text, and email.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will engage with our members to identify changes in their health &amp; social needs, discuss their goals and values to support advanced care planning, and connect them to resources.  Part of your role will also be to assess the urgency of their need, determine the root cause and establish the appropriate next step.  You will be responsible to connect the member to appropriate healthcare and community-based resources including Thyme Care nurses and providers.  You will also research and connect members with external healthcare providers, transportation, financial grants, emotional support resources, and insurance-provided benefits. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will execute your member support using evidence-based assessments, prior experience, and problem solving skills.  In this critical role, you will serve as the primary point of contact throughout the member’s Thyme Care journey, while collaborating closely with an interdisciplinary team of healthcare professionals to ensure the member has holistic support in their care. You will spend the majority of your day working within a phone queue, handling both inbound and outbound calls in a structured, high-volume environment. You will frequently shift between member interactions, documentation, and coordination tasks throughout the day, requiring strong time management and the ability to stay focused in a fast-moving environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Note: In order to ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes a 30-minute lunch and two 15-minute breaks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>After your first three months, you will:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed virtual onboarding and training (two weeks long) and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. You’ll spend your day outreaching to members, researching community and healthcare resources that meet their needs, and connecting members to those resources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have completed  language proficiency testing for team members who interact directly with members in Spanish or evaluate the quality of member interactions conducted in Spanish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. You use that relationship to prioritize how we should address their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be able to identify and prioritize a member's needs and then know where to go to get them help. This means you’ll be working to connect them with their healthcare providers, community resources, social services, diagnostic appointments, and medical treatments and assist with overcoming barriers (e.g., health literacy, unstable housing).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, best practices, and highest standards. You consistently meet or exceed defined productivity and quality metrics, including call volume, responsiveness, documentation timeliness, and member engagement  while managing your time effectively in a structured environment where performance is measured in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your productivity and quality goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to scheduled shifts, including time in queue, breaks, and availability expectations to ensure consistent member coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently drive value in your member interactions through high priority activities and assessments such as:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced care planning support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinating care, including telehealth visits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalating clinical symptoms to our clinical teams</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your resume and prior roles reflect:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 2 years of experience in a patient-facing role conducting care coordination, healthcare navigation, non-clinical case management, resource navigation, or community health work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in a metrics-driven, feedback-oriented environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual (Spanish/English) Proficiency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a fast-paced, high-volume, metrics-driven environment (e.g., contact center, care navigation, care coordination).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in assessing and addressing both patient/member’s stated needs as well as the ability to identify needs that aren’t explicitly expressed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build rapport and trust quickly with patients/members in a high-volume, primarily phone-based environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passionate, trustworthy, and empathetic when working with clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build relationships with different types of people, including clients, organization members, and health care providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and interpersonal skills and ability to speak concisely to clients and Care Team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized with confidential client material and appointment tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible and adaptable in response to changing client and health care providers’ needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for individuals who thrive in structured, high-volume environments and are energized by balancing efficiency with meaningful member interactions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>A member-first approach. </strong>You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives. Healthcare experience preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose. </strong>You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seek diverse perspectives. </strong>You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Effective listener and communicator. </strong>You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity.  </strong>You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with technology. </strong>We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A quiet working space. </strong>It’s important you’ve worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment with no/limited distractions during your scheduled shifts and are able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $24.76/hour.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We are a growing organization and recruit and employ a large number of these roles. Because of this, we actively interview for this position even when we don't have an immediate opening. Candidates who complete the interview process and fit the role are eligible for the next available opening. We will reach back out once an open position becomes available.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The Recruiting team will share more information about our hiring philosophy during an initial phone screen and can answer questions you might have about it then.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We are committed to promoting the health and well-being of all individuals. As a provider of cancer care navigation, we recognize that those with cancer constitute a vulnerable population at risk of contracting COVID-19.  As such, Thyme Care employees are expected to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 as defined by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, subject to conflicting laws and exemptions based on medical or religious objections.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Additionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nImagine building a better healthcare journey for patients with cancer, where individuals and their loved ones feel seen, supported, and heard by their care team – both in and out of the clinic. Where fast access to high-quality care is the norm, not the exception. Where patients have access to a care navigator to guide them through their diagnosis and trusted support all along the way.\n\nAt Thyme Care, we share a passion for transforming the cancer care experience – not just for patients but also for their caregivers and loved ones, as well as those delivering and paying for their care. Today, Thyme Care is known predominantly as a cancer care navigation company enabling value-based cancer care; in the next few years, we will become a nationally recognized technology-driven and provider-centric care delivery model, reshaping the landscape of cancer care access, delivery, and experience. Our commitment runs deep—we're not satisfied with the status quo but determined to redefine it.\n\nTo make this happen, we’re building a diverse team of problem solvers and critical thinkers to drive innovation and shape the future of healthcare. If you share our vision and want to be part of something truly meaningful, we want to hear from you. Together, we can revolutionize cancer care and make a difference that lasts a lifetime.\n\n\n\nYOUR ROLE\n\nAs a bilingual Spanish/English Care Partner, your job is to engage Thyme Care members and navigate them through their cancer journey. You will report into a Care Partner Team Lead and spend most of your day reaching out to our members by phone, text, and email.\n\nYou will engage with our members to identify changes in their health & social needs, discuss their goals and values to support advanced care planning, and connect them to resources.  Part of your role will also be to assess the urgency of their need, determine the root cause and establish the appropriate next step.  You will be responsible to connect the member to appropriate healthcare and community-based resources including Thyme Care nurses and providers.  You will also research and connect members with external healthcare providers, transportation, financial grants, emotional support resources, and insurance-provided benefits. \n\nYou will execute your member support using evidence-based assessments, prior experience, and problem solving skills.  In this critical role, you will serve as the primary point of contact throughout the member’s Thyme Care journey, while collaborating closely with an interdisciplinary team of healthcare professionals to ensure the member has holistic support in their care. You will spend the majority of your day working within a phone queue, handling both inbound and outbound calls in a structured, high-volume environment. You will frequently shift between member interactions, documentation, and coordination tasks throughout the day, requiring strong time management and the ability to stay focused in a fast-moving environment.\n\nNote: In order to ensure we have sufficient coverage at all times, we maintain a schedule that includes a 30-minute lunch and two 15-minute breaks.\n\n\n\nAfter your first three months, you will:\n\n - Have completed virtual onboarding and training (two weeks long) and are up to speed on Thyme Care systems, tools, technology, partners, and expectations. You’ll spend your day outreaching to members, researching community and healthcare resources that meet their needs, and connecting members to those resources\n\n - Have completed  language proficiency testing for team members who interact directly with members in Spanish or evaluate the quality of member interactions conducted in Spanish.\n\n - Have built strong, trusting relationships with your members, where listening and empathy are the foundation for every interaction. You use that relationship to prioritize how we should address their needs.\n\n - Be able to identify and prioritize a member's needs and then know where to go to get them help. This means you’ll be working to connect them with their healthcare providers, community resources, social services, diagnostic appointments, and medical treatments and assist with overcoming barriers (e.g., health literacy, unstable housing).\n\n - Follow Care Team policies and procedures, escalation pathways, best practices, and highest standards. You consistently meet or exceed defined productivity and quality metrics, including call volume, responsiveness, documentation timeliness, and member engagement  while managing your time effectively in a structured environment where performance is measured in real time.\n\n - Participate in coaching and development sessions, and apply feedback and best practices to meet your productivity and quality goals\n\n - Adhere to scheduled shifts, including time in queue, breaks, and availability expectations to ensure consistent member coverage.\n\n - Consistently drive value in your member interactions through high priority activities and assessments such as:\n   \n   - Advanced care planning support\n   \n   - Coordinating care, including telehealth visits\n   \n   - Escalating clinical symptoms to our clinical teams\n\n\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nYour resume and prior roles reflect:\n\n - At least 2 years of experience in a patient-facing role conducting care coordination, healthcare navigation, non-clinical case management, resource navigation, or community health work\n\n - Success in a metrics-driven, feedback-oriented environment\n\n - Bilingual (Spanish/English) Proficiency\n\n - Experience working in a fast-paced, high-volume, metrics-driven environment (e.g., contact center, care navigation, care coordination).\n\n - Experience in assessing and addressing both patient/member’s stated needs as well as the ability to identify needs that aren’t explicitly expressed\n\n - Ability to build rapport and trust quickly with patients/members in a high-volume, primarily phone-based environment\n\n - Passionate, trustworthy, and empathetic when working with clients\n\n - Ability to build relationships with different types of people, including clients, organization members, and health care providers\n\n - Good communication and interpersonal skills and ability to speak concisely to clients and Care Team members\n\n - Organized with confidential client material and appointment tracking\n\n - Flexible and adaptable in response to changing client and health care providers’ needs\n\n - This role is ideal for individuals who thrive in structured, high-volume environments and are energized by balancing efficiency with meaningful member interactions\n\n\nA member-first approach. You’re personally motivated by our mission and are passionate about assisting people and their families during one of the most challenging seasons in their lives. Healthcare experience preferred.\n\nMove with purpose. You’re biased to action. You know how to identify and prioritize your initiative’s needs, and do what it takes to ensure that urgent and important needs are acted on immediately.\n\nSeek diverse perspectives. You are humble and proactively seek feedback from others. You’re always looking to learn and grow.\n\nEffective listener and communicator. You are winsome and articulate, but you always start with listening and you hear what may not be voiced, because you listen so intently to others. You build rapport and great working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\nComfort with ambiguity.  You have a proven track record of success within scaling businesses, fast-paced environments, and/or startups. You understand that rapid changes to the business, strategy, organization, and priorities is par for the course.\n\nComfort with technology. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season where they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records or comfort learning new technology is important.\n\nA quiet working space. It’s important you’ve worked in a remote role in the past. To ensure member privacy, you must operate in a quiet and secure environment with no/limited distractions during your scheduled shifts and are able to test your internet speed prior to starting to ensure our applications function as expected.\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values—Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives—guide us in everything we do. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThis is a non-exempt, full time position. The pay rate for this role is $24.76/hour.\n\nWe are a growing organization and recruit and employ a large number of these roles. Because of this, we actively interview for this position even when we don't have an immediate opening. Candidates who complete the interview process and fit the role are eligible for the next available opening. We will reach back out once an open position becomes available.\n\nThe Recruiting team will share more information about our hiring philosophy during an initial phone screen and can answer questions you might have about it then.\n\nWe are committed to promoting the health and well-being of all individuals. As a provider of cancer care navigation, we recognize that those with cancer constitute a vulnerable population at risk of contracting COVID-19.  As such, Thyme Care employees are expected to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 as defined by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, subject to conflicting laws and exemptions based on medical or religious objections.\n\nAdditionally, we recognize a history of inequality in health care. We’re here to challenge these systems with a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the patients our products serve. We are an equal opportunity employer.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"acc02c12-f7cc-4d38-8918-a8a7fca8e50e","title":"Clinical Social Worker (11:30AM - 8:00PM EST)","department":"Member Experience","team":"Social Workers","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T19:00:33.835+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/acc02c12-f7cc-4d38-8918-a8a7fca8e50e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/acc02c12-f7cc-4d38-8918-a8a7fca8e50e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Thyme Care Clinical Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial and emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. Primary responsibilities include: </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment and Counseling: </strong>Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment, and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress. Assess, diagnose, and provide therapeutic interventions to address behavioral health needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Crisis intervention: </strong>Providing immediate support and intervention in behavioral health crises and sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resource linkage: </strong>Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social or behavioral health needs. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care coordination: </strong>Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, behavioral health providers, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Advocacy: </strong>Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education and support group facilitation: </strong>Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift &amp; additional responsibilities may be required. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong>: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LISW, LCSW). </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications</strong>:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People-first. </strong>Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:  </strong>Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed. ​It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Action-Oriented</strong>: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Skills</strong>: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication Skills</strong>: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability</strong>: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A desire to learn how to use new technologies.</strong> We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $92,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. </em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong>recruitment fraud</strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Thyme Care Clinical Social Worker, you'll be a vital resource for our members and their care network, offering comprehensive psychosocial and emotional support during their cancer journey via phone, email, text, and telemedicine. Primary responsibilities include: \n\n - Assessment and Counseling: Conduct comprehensive psychosocial assessments to identify patients' and families' needs to address emotional concerns such as anxiety, depression, grief, adjustment, and coping mechanisms related to cancer diagnosis and treatment. Assess for and address financial toxicity,  distress, changes in relationships/roles, custody planning, caregiver demands, advance care planning, and spiritual/existential distress. Assess, diagnose, and provide therapeutic interventions to address behavioral health needs. \n\n - Crisis intervention: Providing immediate support and intervention in behavioral health crises and sudden changes in prognosis or end-of-life decisions. \n\n - Resource linkage: Identifying and connecting patients and families with relevant community resources when there are complex social or behavioral health needs. \n\n - Care coordination: Collaborating with the healthcare team, including oncologists, behavioral health providers, nurses, and other specialists, to ensure patients receive coordinated care and address any social or emotional barriers impacting treatment adherence. \n\n - Advocacy: Advocating for patients' needs with insurance companies, healthcare providers, and other relevant agencies to access necessary treatment and support services. \n\n - Education and support group facilitation: Leading support groups for cancer patients and their families, providing education on cancer-related topics, and facilitating peer-to-peer support. \n\nAs a growing company with an evolving care model, responsibilities may shift & additional responsibilities may be required. \n\nThis role reports to our Director of Social Work and can be remote or hybrid based in our Nashville or New York City offices. All patient interactions will be virtual via telephone, video, text, or our proprietary virtual care platform.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - Qualifications: Master's degree in Social Work from a school or program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Valid and current master’s level license in current practice state (i.e., LISW, LCSW). \n\n - Certifications:  OSW-C or APHSW-C preferred. \n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\n - People-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you deeply.\n\n - Experience:  Minimum three to five years of experience is preferred, working as a  social worker in a health care setting; oncology, palliative care, serious illness care and/or hospice experience is desired. An unrestricted license and a willingness to obtain additional state licenses as needed.  It would be exceptional if you have worked at a startup or tech-forward company. \n\n - Action-Oriented: You proactively identify and prioritize initiatives, taking prompt action to address urgent needs.\n\n - Organizational Skills: You excel at multitasking and thrive in fast-paced environments while maintaining meticulous organization in communications and documentation.\n\n - Communication Skills: You are an effective listener and communicator, skilled at building rapport and fostering strong working relationships with members and colleagues.\n\n - Adaptability: You are comfortable with change and ambiguity and have a proven track record of success in dynamic environments.\n\n - A desire to learn how to use new technologies. We are a technology company focused on interacting with folks during the season when they need it most. Experience with video chatting, Google Suite, Slack, electronic health records, or comfort in using and learning new technology is vital.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $92,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level. \n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d92968fd-8a08-42fb-876f-9e8e0ec333b1","title":"Senior Financial Analyst ","department":"Finance & Accounting","team":"Finance & Accounting","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:48:58.468+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d92968fd-8a08-42fb-876f-9e8e0ec333b1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d92968fd-8a08-42fb-876f-9e8e0ec333b1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Financial Analyst on the Strategic Finance team, you’ll play a key role in building and maintaining the financial backbone of a scaling, multi-entity business. You will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own core financial reporting processes, including monthly executive and departmental reports, and support quarterly investor reports, materials and presentations to the Board of Directors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the day-to-day finance partner to functional leaders, helping teams understand performance, manage budgets and headcount, evaluate tradeoffs, and improve financial operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve and automate recurring financial processes to reduce manual work and drive scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide clear and actionable financial insights that help executives and functional leaders make informed decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own department-level planning and consolidation while supporting the broader annual budgeting and quarterly forecasting cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Accounting, People team, Operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to ensure forecasts reflect operational reality and that systems, data, and reporting remain aligned with business needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and evolve Thyme Care’s financial model, keeping actuals, updating and revising key assumptions, and operational drivers with input from core business leaders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2–4 years of finance experience (FP&amp;A, investment banking, consulting, or related), with at least some direct exposure to corporate finance or FP&amp;A.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel and modeling skills; able to build and maintain complex models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating recurring reports and presenting insights to business leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to work cross-functionally with operators and accounting teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice-to-have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in healthcare, value-based care, or multi-entity environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to fundraising, investor reporting, or complex partnerships.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind.</strong> You care deeply about the impact of our work in cancer care, and you bring that same thoughtfulness to financial decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose.</strong> You’re proactive and organized, you know how to keep priorities moving and get things done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfortable with ambiguity.</strong> You thrive in a fast-growing environment where things change quickly, and you adapt without losing momentum.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bring expertise.</strong> You have strong financial modeling and analytical skills, and you can turn numbers into insights that drive action.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operate independently.</strong> You can own processes end-to-end with minimal handholding, while keeping stakeholders aligned along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborate well.</strong> You build trust across teams and know how to partner closely with colleagues in operations, accounting, and leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $108,000-$120,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><strong><u>recruitment fraud</u></strong></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Financial Analyst on the Strategic Finance team, you’ll play a key role in building and maintaining the financial backbone of a scaling, multi-entity business. You will:\n\n - Own core financial reporting processes, including monthly executive and departmental reports, and support quarterly investor reports, materials and presentations to the Board of Directors.\n\n - Serve as the day-to-day finance partner to functional leaders, helping teams understand performance, manage budgets and headcount, evaluate tradeoffs, and improve financial operations.\n\n - Improve and automate recurring financial processes to reduce manual work and drive scalability.\n\n - Provide clear and actionable financial insights that help executives and functional leaders make informed decisions.\n\n - Own department-level planning and consolidation while supporting the broader annual budgeting and quarterly forecasting cycles.\n\n - Partner closely with Accounting, People team, Operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to ensure forecasts reflect operational reality and that systems, data, and reporting remain aligned with business needs.\n\n - Maintain and evolve Thyme Care’s financial model, keeping actuals, updating and revising key assumptions, and operational drivers with input from core business leaders.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - 2–4 years of finance experience (FP&A, investment banking, consulting, or related), with at least some direct exposure to corporate finance or FP&A.\n\n - Strong Excel and modeling skills; able to build and maintain complex models.\n\n - Experience creating recurring reports and presenting insights to business leaders.\n\n - Proven ability to work cross-functionally with operators and accounting teams.\n\nNice-to-have:\n\n - Prior experience in healthcare, value-based care, or multi-entity environments.\n\n - Exposure to fundraising, investor reporting, or complex partnerships.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. You care deeply about the impact of our work in cancer care, and you bring that same thoughtfulness to financial decisions.\n\nMove with purpose. You’re proactive and organized, you know how to keep priorities moving and get things done.\n\nComfortable with ambiguity. You thrive in a fast-growing environment where things change quickly, and you adapt without losing momentum.\n\nBring expertise. You have strong financial modeling and analytical skills, and you can turn numbers into insights that drive action.\n\nOperate independently. You can own processes end-to-end with minimal handholding, while keeping stakeholders aligned along the way.\n\nCollaborate well. You build trust across teams and know how to partner closely with colleagues in operations, accounting, and leadership.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care.  Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $108,000-$120,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n \n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d9a512a4-205d-4450-abe1-6804032c350d","title":"Contract Recruiter ","department":"Recruiting","team":"Recruiting","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T16:17:30.650+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d9a512a4-205d-4450-abe1-6804032c350d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/d9a512a4-205d-4450-abe1-6804032c350d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Recruiter, you’ll join Thyme Care for a six-month engagement to help us scale high-volume hiring across our non-clinical Care Delivery teams. You’ll primarily support roles like Social Workers, Enrollment Specialists, Care Partners, Practice Coordinators, and other member-facing or operational roles.  Additionally, you may support hiring for corporate roles as priorities shift.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for an experienced recruiter who can ramp quickly, manage significant hiring volume, and become a trusted partner to our leaders. You’ll bring a process improvement mentality that will help us to continue evolving how we recruit.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own high-volume searches end-to-end, from intake and sourcing through interviews, offers, and close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Care Delivery leaders to understand hiring needs, anticipate demand, and build effective recruiting strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple roles and significant candidate volume while maintaining speed, quality, and a positive candidate experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and engage pipelines through inbound applicants, proactive sourcing, and referrals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use recruiting data and funnel insights to identify bottlenecks, adjust strategies, and improve results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help hiring managers build a competency-based interview process that is efficient, scalable, and grounded in a positive candidate experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand that AI is changing the craft of recruiting and actively experiment with new tools and workflows. Be willing to build, fail, and learn to find where AI can meaningfully improve the process without replacing human judgement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to flex into Corporate roles when needed based on hiring demand and team capacity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to make our high-volume recruiting processes more scalable, efficient, and effective.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of recruiting experience, ideally in a high-growth company or other high-volume environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success managing high-volume hiring across operations, customer/member-facing, sales, support, or similar populations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record independently owning searches and delivering against ambitious hiring targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing multiple roles and large candidate funnels without sacrificing candidate experience or quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sourcing skills with experience using both inbound and outbound strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering directly with hiring managers and confidently advising or pushing back when appropriate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated curiosity and hands-on experience applying AI and emerging technologies to understand how they can improve recruiting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong candidate management, offer negotiation, and closing skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using recruiting data and funnel metrics to diagnose problems and improve results.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent using modern applicant tracking systems, preferably Ashby.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare experience is not required. We care more about your ability to ramp quickly, learn the business, and deliver.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Members-first.</strong> Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>High-volume recruiting expertise.</strong> You know how to move quickly and manage significant hiring volume without sacrificing quality or candidate experience.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>AI curiosity.</strong> You believe AI will change recruiting and want to help figure out how. You experiment, learn quickly, and aren’t afraid to try something that may not work the first time.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Ownership.</strong> You can come in, get context quickly, and run. You identify problems early and take responsibility for getting searches across the finish line.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Strong partnership.</strong> You build credibility with hiring managers and candidates through responsiveness, judgment, and clear communication.  Your relationships allow you to persuade and influence when needed.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Agility and adaptability.</strong> You can move between hiring populations as business needs change and are comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Candidate-focused.</strong> You recognize that recruiting is a relationship business and create an experience that makes great candidates want to join Thyme Care.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Team mindset.</strong> Even in a six-month engagement, you operate as part of the team, share what you learn, and help improve how we recruit beyond your individual searches.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The contract rate for this role is $60 - $75 per hour, 40 hours per week. The contract rate could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The hourly range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be cautious of<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><u> recruitment fraud</u></a>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email</p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nAs a Senior Recruiter, you’ll join Thyme Care for a six-month engagement to help us scale high-volume hiring across our non-clinical Care Delivery teams. You’ll primarily support roles like Social Workers, Enrollment Specialists, Care Partners, Practice Coordinators, and other member-facing or operational roles.  Additionally, you may support hiring for corporate roles as priorities shift.\n\nWe’re looking for an experienced recruiter who can ramp quickly, manage significant hiring volume, and become a trusted partner to our leaders. You’ll bring a process improvement mentality that will help us to continue evolving how we recruit.\n\n - Own high-volume searches end-to-end, from intake and sourcing through interviews, offers, and close.\n\n - Partner closely with Care Delivery leaders to understand hiring needs, anticipate demand, and build effective recruiting strategies.\n\n - Manage multiple roles and significant candidate volume while maintaining speed, quality, and a positive candidate experience.\n\n - Build and engage pipelines through inbound applicants, proactive sourcing, and referrals.\n\n - Use recruiting data and funnel insights to identify bottlenecks, adjust strategies, and improve results.\n\n - Help hiring managers build a competency-based interview process that is efficient, scalable, and grounded in a positive candidate experience.\n\n - Understand that AI is changing the craft of recruiting and actively experiment with new tools and workflows. Be willing to build, fail, and learn to find where AI can meaningfully improve the process without replacing human judgement.\n\n - Ability to flex into Corporate roles when needed based on hiring demand and team capacity.\n\n - Identify opportunities to make our high-volume recruiting processes more scalable, efficient, and effective.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - 5+ years of recruiting experience, ideally in a high-growth company or other high-volume environment.\n\n - Proven success managing high-volume hiring across operations, customer/member-facing, sales, support, or similar populations.\n\n - Strong track record independently owning searches and delivering against ambitious hiring targets.\n\n - Experience managing multiple roles and large candidate funnels without sacrificing candidate experience or quality.\n\n - Strong sourcing skills with experience using both inbound and outbound strategies.\n\n - Experience partnering directly with hiring managers and confidently advising or pushing back when appropriate.\n\n - Demonstrated curiosity and hands-on experience applying AI and emerging technologies to understand how they can improve recruiting.\n\n - Strong candidate management, offer negotiation, and closing skills.\n\n - Experience using recruiting data and funnel metrics to diagnose problems and improve results.\n\n - Fluent using modern applicant tracking systems, preferably Ashby.\n\n - Healthcare experience is not required. We care more about your ability to ramp quickly, learn the business, and deliver.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nMembers-first. Thyme Care’s mission and members matter to you, deeply.\n\nHigh-volume recruiting expertise. You know how to move quickly and manage significant hiring volume without sacrificing quality or candidate experience.\n\nAI curiosity. You believe AI will change recruiting and want to help figure out how. You experiment, learn quickly, and aren’t afraid to try something that may not work the first time.\n\nOwnership. You can come in, get context quickly, and run. You identify problems early and take responsibility for getting searches across the finish line.\n\nStrong partnership. You build credibility with hiring managers and candidates through responsiveness, judgment, and clear communication.  Your relationships allow you to persuade and influence when needed.\n\nAgility and adaptability. You can move between hiring populations as business needs change and are comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment.\n\nCandidate-focused. You recognize that recruiting is a relationship business and create an experience that makes great candidates want to join Thyme Care.\n\nTeam mindset. Even in a six-month engagement, you operate as part of the team, share what you learn, and help improve how we recruit beyond your individual searches.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nThe contract rate for this role is $60 - $75 per hour, 40 hours per week. The contract rate could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.\n\nThe hourly range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired in another location or at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n\n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"53443ebf-d435-410a-b8d7-3448eca12b60","title":"Visual Designer, Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T17:30:11.187+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"United States","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/53443ebf-d435-410a-b8d7-3448eca12b60","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/thyme-care/53443ebf-d435-410a-b8d7-3448eca12b60/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR  MISSION</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Today, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Looking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thyme Care’s brand is growing quickly—and so is our need for thoughtful, effective creativity that brings greater clarity and humanity to cancer care. As a Visual Designer on the Marketing team, you’ll help shape how our brand shows up across campaigns, channels, and experiences. Your work will help people understand who we are, what we offer, and how Thyme Care can make a meaningful difference in their lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll translate ideas, creative briefs, and strategic direction into clear, engaging visual experiences for diverse audiences. Working closely with Marketing, Communications, and cross-functional partners, you’ll create campaigns, digital experiences, and meaningful brand moments. This is a hands-on role for a thoughtful designer with strong visual craft, sound judgment, and the ability to independently manage defined projects within an established brand system.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Design and Creative Execution</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the design and production of marketing campaigns, digital assets, social content, presentations, and experiential materials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate creative briefs, marketing strategies, and established direction into thoughtful, effective deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply Thyme Care’s visual system consistently across digital and print materials while identifying opportunities to strengthen the work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with writers, marketers, and communications partners to align visual design and messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage projects from initial concept through final production, seeking guidance when work involves greater complexity or ambiguity.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Brand Stewardship</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply Thyme Care’s visual identity consistently across channels, audiences, and formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with senior creative team members to extend the design system as new needs, programs, and campaigns emerge.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a high standard of craft across typography, layout, imagery, and production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and help resolve inconsistencies in how the brand is expressed.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Campaign and Channel Design</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create assets for paid media, email, web, social, and other marketing channels that balance creativity, clarity, accessibility, and performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support key internal and external moments, including company events, conferences, and executive presentations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn data, care experiences, and impact stories into visuals that make complex information easier to understand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt creative concepts across formats while maintaining the integrity of the original idea.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Collaboration and Process</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with partners across Marketing and Communications, including Growth, Enrollment, Engagement, and Product Marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate actively in creative reviews, incorporating feedback thoughtfully and explaining design decisions clearly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance multiple projects and deadlines while communicating progress, risks, and dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to templates, documentation, and workflows that help the team work more efficiently and consistently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share knowledge and constructive feedback that strengthen the work of the broader creative team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT YOU’VE DONE</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 4+ years of professional design experience, ideally within a brand, marketing, or communications team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your portfolio demonstrates strong visual storytelling, typography, layout, and multi-channel brand design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have created digital materials—including web, social, email, and presentations—as well as print or physical collateral.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong working knowledge of brand systems and can create varied, engaging work within established guidelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can independently own well-defined projects from concept through final production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You demonstrate sound design judgment and are open to feedback, collaboration, and continued growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are highly organized and able to balance multiple priorities and timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience partnering with marketers, writers, and other stakeholders to translate goals and creative direction into effective design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are proficient in Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Google Workspace, and collaboration tools such as Asana and Slack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare, digital health, or another mission-driven organization is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>WHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Act with our members in mind.</strong> You approach design with empathy and care, recognizing that the work may reach people navigating one of the most difficult periods of their lives. You create experiences that feel clear, accessible, inclusive, and human.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong visual craft.</strong> You bring a strong foundation in typography, layout, imagery, hierarchy, and visual storytelling. You care about the details and consistently produce polished, thoughtful work across digital and physical formats.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Brand fluency.</strong> You understand how to work creatively within an established brand system. You can maintain consistency while thoughtfully adapting and extending the system as new audiences, channels, and needs emerge.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Move with purpose.</strong> You can prioritize effectively, move projects forward, and deliver high-quality work in a fast-paced environment. You communicate early when priorities, timelines, or dependencies need to be clarified.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seek diverse perspectives.</strong> You actively invite input from partners with different experiences and areas of expertise. You incorporate feedback thoughtfully and understand that stronger creative work comes from collaboration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clear communication and ownership.</strong> You can explain the thinking behind your design decisions, ask thoughtful questions, and translate feedback into action. You take responsibility for your work from concept through final production while knowing when to seek additional guidance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with iteration and ambiguity.</strong> You are comfortable working through evolving briefs, shifting priorities, and imperfect information. You remain flexible, curious, and focused on finding the strongest path forward.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $110,500 - $130,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Be cautious of </em><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers\"><em><u>recruitment fraud</u></em></a><em>, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"OUR  MISSION\n\nWe exist to create a more connected, compassionate, and confident experience for people with cancer and those who care for them. We make it easier to get answers, access high-quality care quickly, and feel supported throughout treatment and beyond.\n\nToday, Thyme Care is a market-leading value-based oncology care enabler, partnering with national and regional health plans, providers, and employers to deliver better outcomes and lower costs for thousands of people across the country. Our model combines high-touch human support with powerful technology and AI to bring together everyone involved in a person’s cancer journey: caregivers, oncologists, health plans, and employers.\n\nAs a tech-native organization, we believe technology should strengthen the human connection at the center of care. Through data science, automation, and AI, we simplify complexity, improve collaboration, and help care teams focus on what matters most: supporting people through cancer.\n\nLooking ahead, our vision is bold: to become a household name in cancer care, where every person diagnosed asks for Thyme Care by name. If you’re inspired to make cancer care more human and to help reimagine what’s possible, we’d love to meet you. Together, we can build a future where every person with cancer feels truly cared for, in every moment that matters.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nThyme Care’s brand is growing quickly—and so is our need for thoughtful, effective creativity that brings greater clarity and humanity to cancer care. As a Visual Designer on the Marketing team, you’ll help shape how our brand shows up across campaigns, channels, and experiences. Your work will help people understand who we are, what we offer, and how Thyme Care can make a meaningful difference in their lives.\n\nYou’ll translate ideas, creative briefs, and strategic direction into clear, engaging visual experiences for diverse audiences. Working closely with Marketing, Communications, and cross-functional partners, you’ll create campaigns, digital experiences, and meaningful brand moments. This is a hands-on role for a thoughtful designer with strong visual craft, sound judgment, and the ability to independently manage defined projects within an established brand system.\n\n\n\n\nDESIGN AND CREATIVE EXECUTION\n\n - Own the design and production of marketing campaigns, digital assets, social content, presentations, and experiential materials.\n\n - Translate creative briefs, marketing strategies, and established direction into thoughtful, effective deliverables.\n\n - Apply Thyme Care’s visual system consistently across digital and print materials while identifying opportunities to strengthen the work.\n\n - Collaborate with writers, marketers, and communications partners to align visual design and messaging.\n\n - Manage projects from initial concept through final production, seeking guidance when work involves greater complexity or ambiguity.\n\n\nBRAND STEWARDSHIP\n\n - Apply Thyme Care’s visual identity consistently across channels, audiences, and formats.\n\n - Partner with senior creative team members to extend the design system as new needs, programs, and campaigns emerge.\n\n - Maintain a high standard of craft across typography, layout, imagery, and production.\n\n - Identify and help resolve inconsistencies in how the brand is expressed.\n\n\nCAMPAIGN AND CHANNEL DESIGN\n\n - Create assets for paid media, email, web, social, and other marketing channels that balance creativity, clarity, accessibility, and performance.\n\n - Support key internal and external moments, including company events, conferences, and executive presentations.\n\n - Turn data, care experiences, and impact stories into visuals that make complex information easier to understand.\n\n - Adapt creative concepts across formats while maintaining the integrity of the original idea.\n\n\nCOLLABORATION AND PROCESS\n\n - Work closely with partners across Marketing and Communications, including Growth, Enrollment, Engagement, and Product Marketing.\n\n - Participate actively in creative reviews, incorporating feedback thoughtfully and explaining design decisions clearly.\n\n - Balance multiple projects and deadlines while communicating progress, risks, and dependencies.\n\n - Contribute to templates, documentation, and workflows that help the team work more efficiently and consistently.\n\n - Share knowledge and constructive feedback that strengthen the work of the broader creative team.\n\nWHAT YOU’VE DONE\n\n - You have 4+ years of professional design experience, ideally within a brand, marketing, or communications team.\n\n - Your portfolio demonstrates strong visual storytelling, typography, layout, and multi-channel brand design.\n\n - You have created digital materials—including web, social, email, and presentations—as well as print or physical collateral.\n\n - You have a strong working knowledge of brand systems and can create varied, engaging work within established guidelines.\n\n - You can independently own well-defined projects from concept through final production.\n\n - You demonstrate sound design judgment and are open to feedback, collaboration, and continued growth.\n\n - You are highly organized and able to balance multiple priorities and timelines.\n\n - You have experience partnering with marketers, writers, and other stakeholders to translate goals and creative direction into effective design.\n\n - You are proficient in Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Google Workspace, and collaboration tools such as Asana and Slack.\n\n - Experience in healthcare, digital health, or another mission-driven organization is a plus.\n\nWHAT LEADS TO SUCCESS\n\nAct with our members in mind. You approach design with empathy and care, recognizing that the work may reach people navigating one of the most difficult periods of their lives. You create experiences that feel clear, accessible, inclusive, and human.\n\nStrong visual craft. You bring a strong foundation in typography, layout, imagery, hierarchy, and visual storytelling. You care about the details and consistently produce polished, thoughtful work across digital and physical formats.\n\nBrand fluency. You understand how to work creatively within an established brand system. You can maintain consistency while thoughtfully adapting and extending the system as new audiences, channels, and needs emerge.\n\nMove with purpose. You can prioritize effectively, move projects forward, and deliver high-quality work in a fast-paced environment. You communicate early when priorities, timelines, or dependencies need to be clarified.\n\nSeek diverse perspectives. You actively invite input from partners with different experiences and areas of expertise. You incorporate feedback thoughtfully and understand that stronger creative work comes from collaboration.\n\nClear communication and ownership. You can explain the thinking behind your design decisions, ask thoughtful questions, and translate feedback into action. You take responsibility for your work from concept through final production while knowing when to seek additional guidance.\n\nComfort with iteration and ambiguity. You are comfortable working through evolving briefs, shifting priorities, and imperfect information. You remain flexible, curious, and focused on finding the strongest path forward.\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAt Thyme Care, our core values guide us in everything we do: Act with our members in mind, Move with purpose, and Seek diverse perspectives. They anchor our business decisions, including how we grow, the products we make, and the paths we choose—or don’t choose.\n\nOur salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of the total compensation package that also includes equity, benefits, and other opportunities at Thyme Care. Individual pay decisions are based on several factors, including qualifications, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Thyme Care employees. The base salary for this role is $110,500 - $130,000. The salary range could be lower or higher than this if the role is hired at another level.\n\nWe recognize a history of inequality in healthcare. We’re here to challenge the status quo and create a culture of inclusion through the care we give and the company we build. We embrace and celebrate a diversity of perspectives in reflection of our members and the members we serve. We are an equal-opportunity employer.\n\n \n\nBe cautious of recruitment fraud https://www.thymecare.com/fraudulent-job-offers, and always confirm that communications are coming from an official Thyme Care email.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}